window.FWN_MADAMS_IDENTITIES_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MADAMS_IDENTITIES_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":3601,"title":"Chapter 3601: She Ran Away?","paragraphs":["Chapter 3601: She Ran Away?","Editor: Atlas Studios","He followed him to the men’s washroom and saw the female employee in Qiao Nian’s clothes and the familiar baseball cap...","Shadow’s temples throbbed. He felt he had been played like a fool for the last 10 minutes.","However, worse news was yet to come.","Someone hurried in to report.","“Oh no! Lord Shadow, someone destroyed the fire alarm. Many employees on the first floor are making a fuss about leaving the building.”","...","Shadow suddenly turned his head, and a careless face appeared in his mind.","Qiao Nian!","He immediately ordered, “Contact the security immediately and tell them not to let anyone out!”","He closed his eyes again and called out to the person again.","“Tell them to draw their guns if they try to break out!”","“Yes.”","That person did not dare to delay anymore.","At this moment, his subordinates had already helped the unconscious woman up. They stood in front of him and hesitantly asked, “Do you need to wake this woman up for questioning?”","Shadow suddenly turned around and said coldly, “No need. She doesn’t know anything!”","Then, he ran to the elevator without looking back.","In his mind, he outlined how Qiao Nian had dragged her injured arm and calmly ran in the opposite direction. How she pulled out the steel needle on the ninth floor and then went to the 12th floor. How she had knocked out a female employee of similar size and exchanged their clothes. How she quietly broke the fire alarm, causing the employees in the entire building to panic. How she mixed into the crowd and incited everyone to run downstairs...","If not for the fact that he was here, her plan would have succeeded.","Shadow was shocked to find out how scary the young girl was.","It was also at this moment that he suddenly understood why the Empress would always use the words ‘pervert’ and ‘monster’ to describe the direct descendants of the Ji family.","Qiao Nian was only 20 years old, but this was her reaction to unexpected situations.","How talented was Ji Wusun back then to force the entire reclusive families and Continent M to submit to him?!","The elevator finally stopped on the 12th floor.","Every minute and second here made his heart jump.","Shadow called Nie Qingru before getting into the elevator.","**","The black Rolls-Royce Phantom rushed to the bank building in the dark.","Along the way, they followed her orders and ran straight through the red light without stopping. The car was like a ghost and a beautiful shadow speeding through the night.","In the car.","Nie Qingru saw that Shadow was calling and picked it up with a dark expression. “Did she run away?”","Her tone showed how upset she was.","The taste of rust rose in her throat.","Her eyes were filled with killing intent.","Fortunately, Shadow did not bring bad news, even though it was not good news either.","“Are you saying that she’s injured?” Nie Qingru’s eyelids lifted coldly. There was no fluctuation in her cold eyes. “It’s not even wrong to ask for a life as compensation for what she did. It’s just an injury. Is it worth reporting to me?”","She did not give Shadow a chance to explain before looking at the scenery outside the car window and saying indifferently, “I know what you are thinking. She’s not my granddaughter. If we have to calculate, she’s just a dog from the Ji family. I’ve already made it clear to you before. Get her, dead or alive!”","The person on the other end responded in a low voice.","Nie Qingru did not care about his feelings. She hung up expressionlessly and threw her phone on the back seat.","She supported her forehead with her hand and pressed it as the scene of her meeting the girl’s eyes in the cell phone’s surveillance cameras appeared in her mind."]},{"number":3602,"title":"Chapter 3602: Shadow Discovered Sister Nian’s Plan","paragraphs":["Chapter 3602: Shadow Discovered Sister Nian’s Plan","Editor: Atlas Studios","That evil creature raised its head as if it had sensed something. Its eyes were shockingly bright as their eyes met. In those eyes, she only saw arrogance and savagery. There was no trace of begging for mercy or fear.","Nie Qingru’s breathing gradually became heavier as she raised her fist and palm.","She knew that Qiao Nian was a smart person.","The moment Qiao Nian triggered the mechanism, she knew she had already discovered it. Hence, her first reaction was to look at the vault’s surveillance footage.","However, even though she had reached that stage and had already become a trapped beast, her spine still did not break. The look in her eyes was still arrogant and rebellious!","...","Nie Qingru thought of someone.","The man she had hated and feared for half her life.","As soon as this thought appeared, her heart felt like it had been pinched by an invisible hand. Nie Qingru’s expression changed from calm to ferocious. Every breath she took was extremely heavy. There was only one thought in her mind... She couldn’t let Qiao Nian leave safely tonight!","**","The lobby on the first floor of Smith Bank was noisy at this moment, with its usual dazzling elite atmosphere no longer present. More than 200 people crowded the space, and it was as noisy as a market. People talked loudly to the security officers, asking them to move aside so they could leave.","Qiao Nian followed the crowd down. Seeing the two rows of security guards blocking the exit, she lowered her eyes and pursed her lips.","Hiding in the crowd, no one noticed her, nor did anyone notice the redness seeping out of the sleeve of this unfamiliar female colleague’s right arm.","Everyone was panicking about the ‘fire’ upstairs.","These financial elites of Continent M were panicking at this moment. Their faces were red as they argued loudly with the security person in charge, asking to be let out immediately.","The others were also panicking and ready to charge out at any time.","“Everyone, please calm down. We’ve already checked. There’s no fire. Don’t be nervous.”","The person in charge was sweating profusely as he tried to calm the agitated crowd.","However, when it came to their own safety, who would be willing to believe a word of comfort from others?","The man leading the negotiations showed an ugly expression as he clenched his fists and shouted angrily, “Since there’s no fire up there, why can’t you let us go? Move aside, we want to leave! You have no right to keep us here. You’re illegally detaining us~!”","In his anger, he turned around excitedly and said to everyone, “Let’s go. We’ll break out!”","The rest had already become a mess after the alarm and the sprinklers. Coupled with the fact that they were blocked at the door and were not allowed to go out...","With someone taking the lead, everyone prepared to force their way out without thinking.","Having already expected this to happen, Qiao Nian raised her glasses and covered the wound on her right arm, preparing to follow the crowd out.","At this moment, a shot rang out ahead of them.","Bang!","The crowd that was about to rush out was in an uproar. Everyone stood rooted to the ground as if they had been frightened. They were just a step away from leaving, but now they were frozen in place.","Qiao Nian realized what had happened and did not have time to react.","She saw the elevator doors open from the corner of her eye and Shadow walked right out.","He had extremely high prestige among these people.","As soon as he appeared, the restless crowd seemed to have been injected with a stimulant. Even the leader wanting to charge out calmed down and looked in his direction in a daze.","Qiao Nian frowned and lowered her head to avoid Shadow’s searching gaze as she hid behind a tall man."]},{"number":3603,"title":"Chapter 3603: Eh, You’re Injured?","paragraphs":["Chapter 3603: Eh, You’re Injured?","Editor: Atlas Studios","Even though Shadow did not have time to search carefully, her heart sank. She already had a bad feeling.","If her plan had gone smoothly, she would have already broken out with the crowd.","However, this was a temporary solution she had thought of in an emergency. Now that something happened midway, Qiao Nian had no backup plan.","Since Shadow had arrived at the building so quickly, her chances of leaving were slim.","The fat executive in front jogged and handed a microphone to the man in black.","Shadow tried to find that figure among the crowd, but too many people were gathered in the lobby. He couldn’t immediately tell which one was Qiao Nian.","He could only take the speaker from the executive and say in a low voice, “Don’t panic, everyone. We didn’t let you leave because someone broke into the vault and took important documents. The alarm earlier was the alarm sound of the vault being triggered. As for the fire alarm on the 12th floor, it was also caused by that person. It was to cause panic so they could leave with you.”","There was too much information in his few sentences.","Someone in the crowd mustered his courage and asked, “How do we know if you’re telling the truth? If there’s really a fire, we’ll ask to go out.”","Shadow glanced at the crowd expressionlessly and gave an earth-shattering warning. “We’ll open fire if you try to force your way out!”","—We will open fire!","The crowd was shocked by his words, but it had to be said that they were very intimidating. Compared to reasoning with panicking people, fists could make them listen quickly.","Qiao Nian saw that Shadow’s people had already begun to check their identities. In a few minutes, they would find her.","This time, Shadow was fully prepared.","Qiao Nian turned around and saw people guarding the elevator and emergency passageway.","She clenched her fists. Her delicate face was expressionless, her eyes were like a deep pool, and her back was tense, as she looked at Shadow’s subordinates gradually approaching her. Her temples were throbbing, and she was about to give it a try...","At this critical moment, a man beside Qiao Nian suddenly said, pointing at her right arm. “Eh, why is there blood? Are you injured?”","He was probably being kind.","Thinking that his colleague had cut her arm in her panic, and seeing that Qiao Nian was a girl, he said out of gentlemanly kindness, “Let them know, I’ll bandage your wound first.”","What he did not know was that his good intentions had ruined things.","Shadow was also looking for Qiao Nian.","Everyone was stunned by his words. Although many people were in the lobby, no one was speaking.","In the quiet and strange atmosphere, his normal voice was loud enough.","His words attracted a lot of attention to Qiao Nian.","Qiao Nian did not expect to meet a useless teammate. There must be a f*cking bug!","She reacted quickly.","At the same time that Shadow looked at her sharply, she took out a mini pistol from her sleeve and fired three shots at the chandelier.","Only the sound of gunshots and glass shattering could be heard.","The hall fell into darkness.","The crowd was frightened by the sudden gunshots. Screams and noise could be heard incessantly.","They instinctively tried to run out without a care.","At this moment, Shadow’s threat became useless."]},{"number":3604,"title":"Chapter 3604: A Car Charged In!","paragraphs":["Chapter 3604: A Car Charged In!","Editor: Atlas Studios","No one cared about what exactly was happening. They only knew that they had heard gunshots and had to go outside to be safe...","“Stop them! Don’t let anyone out!”","“Block it!”","Shadow shouted sternly!","He had already noticed Qiao Nian before the lights went out and the hall fell into darkness. He even saw the girl’s slightly pale but calm face.","He did not expect Qiao Nian to catch him off guard at this point.","The Empress was right.","He must not let anyone escape tonight.","Even if it was no more than arpse, Qiao Nian had to stay behind.","“Shoot anyone who dares to go out!” Shadow ordered viciously. He pushed through the crowd and chased in the direction he last saw the girl.","Qiao Nian had already quietly left her spot when the crystal lamp above her head went out and was now walking towards the exit.","However, Shadow’s orders were fast and ruthless.","After a short period of panic, the security guards at the door strictly carried out his orders. Even though the crowd was excited, no oneuld break through the human wall.","Qiao Nian took a deep breath and looked back at the stairs, trying to see if there was a way there.","However, things were more troublesome than she had imagined.","These people did not give her a chance to walk out at all. She heard a series of footsteps, and someone behind her used a flashlight to illuminate the place.","Moreover, the situation was urgent. Qiao Nian only had time to extinguish the light in the hall. The lights at the elevator and emergency stairs were still good. As long as she went over, she would immediately be divered...","Qiao Nianuldn’t advance or retreat now. She immediately fell into a difficult situation.","It was rare for her to eunter such a situation, especially with her right hand injured. The friction in the crowd would knock into her injured arm from time to time, causing blood to seep out from the wound.","Injured and in pain, Qiao Nian relied on willpower to hold on until now.","If this dragged on, in less than five minutes, the opportunity she had painstakingly created would disappear and the situation would return to the point where it wasntrolled by the reclusive families...","Snds ticked by.","Shadow found more and more flashlights, enough to light up the hall.","Qiao Nianuldn’t wait any longer!","She gritted her teeth and prepared to fight to the death.","Sheuldn’t fall into Nie Qingru’s hands. Even if she died, that would never happen.","At this moment, two strong lights shone from outside.","Shadow also noticed the sudden situation and asked hoarsely, “What happened?”","Before heuld see clearly, he heard a series of screams in front of him, right on the heels of which was the sound of glass shattering.","Boom!","A black Buick smashed through the glass door. Like a cheetah in the night, it broke through Shadow’s defense at an unstoppable speed.","Someone opened the door.","Before Qiao Nianuld react, she heard Ji Lin’s voice. “Miss Qiao, get in the car, Master Wang is here to pick you up.”","Just this one sentence.","Qiao Nian immediately ran over. Before anyoneuld react, she grabbed Ji Lin’s hand and jumped in.","Ji Lin pulled her in, closed the door, and said to the man in the driver’s seat, “She’s in.”","The man turned the steering wheel, and the black Buick drifted on the spot, causing the car to swing back and rush out like an arrow.","The entire process took less than a minute. The two sidesoperated well and trusted each other enough that they did not waste a snd.","Shadow’s expression changed drastically upon seeing that the black Buick was about to leave under the moonlight. He shouted, “Stop that car! Shoot now!”"]},{"number":3605,"title":"Chapter 3605: Trash, She Actually Escaped","paragraphs":["Chapter 3605: Trash, She Actually Escaped","Editor: Atlas Studios","Stunned by this scene, the other people finally returned to their senses and hurriedly fired at the tail of the car.","However, it was too late.","The black Buick pulled steadily into the road amid a jumble of gunfire, and as the traffic faded out of sight—","At this moment, the fat executive finally found a backup electric light to illuminate the lobby, but he only saw Shadow’s ashen face and the mess on the ground.","“Are... are you alright?”","He carefully went forward tomfort him.","Shadow’s head buzzed and his face was ashen. He kicked the trash can beside him and panted heavily. His mind went blank!","He had never expected this oume.","He was just a little bit away from catching Qiao Nian. Just a little bit... Heuld already feel that he had forced her into arner.","Just give him another minute—no, ten snds—and heuld have caught her!","But in the blink of an eye, she was saved.","Shadow did not know how to explain this to Nie Qingru. He felt that he had made a big mistake this time, so big that heuldn’t accept it.","...","Ten minutes later, Nie Qingru’s car stopped outside the bank building.","Leaving the car, she saw the mess outside and the dejected security guards cleaning up the mess...","She walked in quickly but did not see Shadow. However, she had a bad feeling and vaguely realized that things might be out of herntrol.","Her eyes darkened when she finally found Shadow but saw no trace of that evil creature. She waved her hand and ordered, “Follow me!”","Shadow left the paperwork to someone else and followed her.","Nie Qingru quickly walked in front without stopping.","She did not even have the patience to find a room and turned into the emergencyrridor.","Shadow did not dare to delay and followed.","As soon as he entered, the person walking in front suddenly turned around and slapped him hard, causing his head to tilt heavily to the right.","Shadow did not even dare to touch his face. He stood there with his hands by his side, feeling the numbness on half of his face. He spat out a mouthful of blood and apologized in a low voice. “I’m sorry, Empress.”","Nie Qingru prided herself on being noble and rarely took action personally. This time, sheuld notntrol her emotions and slapped him.","As if looking at a dead person, she lowered her head and asked fiercely, “Where is she?!”","“She ran away.” Shadow lowered his head. He did not even dare to look at her as a fishy taste spread from his throat.","Nie Qingru’s slap was too heavy. His right ear was still buzzing, and he was listening to her questions with his left ear.","However, Shadow did not resent Nie Qingru for slapping him. This time, he let down the Empress’ trust by letting Qiao Nian escape. He deserved to die.","“It’s my mistake this time. I have nothing to refute. You can punish me however you want. Even if you want my life... I have nomplaints!”","Nie Qingru’s anger receded and she calmed down after hearing his words. She glanced at him as if she was looking at a dog. “I didn’t save you back then to let you die in front of me. If you wanted to die, you shouldn’t have begged me to save you back then.”","Shadow quickly raised his head. “But I didn’tmplete your mission...”","“That’s enough!” Nie Qingru interrupted him. Her expression was still ugly, but at least she did not losentrol like before. She turned away and expressionlessly asked, “Do you know who saved her?”"]},{"number":3606,"title":"Chapter 3606: Who Other Than Master Wang!","paragraphs":["Chapter 3606: Who Other Than Master Wang!","Editor: Atlas Studios","Shadow couldn’t hide his emotions, but he didn’t dare to show them. He suppressed his surging emotions and said in a low voice, “It should be that Young Master Ye.”","“Who?” Nie Qingru did not wait for his answer and continued, “Ye Wangchuan?”","Her question was filled with certainty.","A sharp sneer appeared on her face, but the smile did not reach her eyes. Her eyes were like a desolate ice field that only had the nature of a beast left. “He does like my granddaughter.”","Silence.","Shadow lowered his head and did not dare to speak.","Nie Qingru’s face was as cold as ice. “Have you gone to the vault to see what is missing?”","Shadow felt so guilty that he almost bent his spine. “Yes. The antidote you put in the safe is missing. Also...”","He could not continue.","Nie Qingru did not let him go. He stared at him and asked, “What else?”","Shadow knelt on the ground and said, “Also... the photo and ashes.”","Nie Qingru could only hear a buzzing sound. Her nails dug into her palms and penetrated deep into her bones. “What did you say?”","Shadow understood what these two things meant and did not dare to repeat them.","Nie Qingru had heard it clearly, but she just could not accept the result. She gritted her teeth so hard that her molars creaked. She was so angry that she smiled. “Very good, very good! It’s really Ji Wusun’s child. I really regret not investigating Ji Qing in a moment of weakness. If I had known earlier that she had a child outside, I wouldn’t have kept this bastard!”","If you don’t get rid of the roots, they will grow again in spring!","In the end, her heart had been too soft back then.","Nie Qingru clutched her palm and almost fainted from anger. Fortunately, she was mentally strong and was used to being domineering. Even if she encountered setbacks, she would not lose her mind.","“Seal off all overseas flights and ports in Continent M immediately. From now on, don’t allow anyone to leave the country for the next 24 hours.”","Shadow suddenly raised his head. “Empress, isn’t this too forceful? The Privy Council... will not agree.”","Nie Qingru looked extremely calm. The stormy waves were all hidden under the calm surface. She said without any hesitation, “I will get the Privy Council to agree!”","“You...” Shadow wanted to persuade her.","Nie Qingru raised her hand to stop him. She closed her eyes for a moment before opening them again and saying firmly, “I will never allow anyone to take him away.”","**","In the boundless night, the black Buick blended into the Sichuan traffic and shook off the car chasing behind it. It drove steadily on the road.","Until they were sure they were safe.","Ji Lin’s tense muscles relaxed. He forced a smile and comforted the girl sitting in the back. “Miss Qiao, it’s alright now.”","Qiao Nian took off her rimless glasses and held them in her hand as she looked at the man in the driver’s seat. “When did you come?”","“The plane landed an hour ago. I asked Ji Lin to check your whereabouts and rushed over.” Ye Wangchuan drove with one hand and placed the other on the reverse wheel to reveal the black bangle on his thin wrist. The extremely simple bangle made his skin look extremely fair and did not look feminine at all.","It was as if he was a proud and noble person, watertight and extremely reliable.","Qiao Nian did not want to ask him how he had guessed she was in danger.","She knew that Ye Wangchuan had not guessed it. He had simply chosen to rush to her immediately...","On the other hand, Ye Wangchuan saw her fall silent through the rearview mirror and gently asked, “Why didn’t you ask me how I knew you were in danger?”"]},{"number":3607,"title":"Chapter 3607: The Person in the Photo Should Be Dead","paragraphs":["Chapter 3607: The Person in the Photo Should Be Dead","Editor: Atlas Studios","Qiao Nian suddenly relaxed, and her injured arm started to sting.","She lost her strength and leaned against the back of the chair. Her face was pale and her tone was a little lazy. “I don’t want to ask anymore. I’m tired.”","Ji Lin noticed the blood seeping out of her right shirt and was shocked. “I was wondering why I smelled blood. Miss Qiao, why didn’t you say you were injured?”","Qiao Nian looked at her right hand indifferently. “It’s a small injury.”","Ji Lin was about to say something when he looked at Master Wang, hesitating about what to say.","Ye Wangchuan did not speak, as if he did not hear them. He looked ahead as he drove. His thin lips were pursed into a line the entire time, and he did not say a word.","Ji Lin couldn’t figure out what Master Wang was up to. Usually, he would say something even when she drank a cold drink, but this time, he did not react when he heard that Miss Qiao was injured.","Unlike his usual style, the black Buick drove towards the airport at a very fast speed.","30 kilometers away from the airport, Ji Lin received a call.","“Got it.”","He hung up the phone with a solemn expression and looked up at the two people in the car. “Nie Qingru canceled all the overseas flights.”","Such a crazy move exceeded Ji Lin’s imagination. He could not help but look in Qiao Nian’s direction and ask, “Miss Qiao, what did you take from her? Why is she acting crazy?”","Qiao Nian was stunned for a moment. Her black eyelashes covered her eyes as she thought. “An antidote, a photo, and a box.”","She slowly took out the things she had risked her life to get and placed them in front of Ji Lin, gesturing with her chin. “Just these three.”","Ji Lin looked at the three inconspicuous items and could not understand what magic these things had to make the Empress of the reclusive families go crazy like this.","He first picked up the old photo. He didn’t know the person on it. “There’s such a person in Continent M? Why haven’t I seen him before?”","There was a shadow-like man beside Nie Qingru. He was very skilled and efficient. Everyone knew that she had a good dog.","Qiao Nian supported her chin with her hand and said casually, “This person should be dead.”","“Dead?!” Ji Lin raised his head in shock.","Qiao Nian took the photo from him and looked at the man smiling brightly in the photo.","“If I’m not wrong, this person has been dead for a long time. This is one of the few photos that that person left behind. Moreover, this photo has special memories, so she especially cherished it and kept it in a safe.”","She said it so casually that Ji Lin did not know what to say.","Qiao Nian was just saying it for herself.","She held the old photo between her fingers, slightly distracted.","She even thought that the reason why Nie Qingru treasured this photo so much was probably because it was taken by Nie Qingru herself.","This was because the man in the photo looked at the camera with love and freedom.","This kind of gaze meant that the person who took this photo had an extraordinary relationship with him. Nie Qingru could not possibly hide the photo taken by this man’s ‘girlfriend’.","The only possibility was that the girlfriend was herself!","Qiao Nian suddenly smiled and licked her dry lips. Her eyes were cold and dry, and she almost tore the photo."]},{"number":3608,"title":"Chapter 3608: Master Wang Is Angry?","paragraphs":["Chapter 3608: Master Wang Is Angry?","Editor: Atlas Studios","She had originally thought that the grudges of the previous generation were simply complicated, but did not expect the truth to be so melodramatic... It might even be more melodramatic than she had imagined.","However, she still could not figure out why Nie Qingru wanted to kill Ji Qing.","Even if the other person Nie Qingru loved was not her husband, there was no need to kill her only daughter.","What exactly happened back then? Why did Ji Qing have to die?","Thick fog surrounded her again. For a moment, she could not see where the road led. She only felt a chill in her teeth. She wanted to laugh, but she also felt that it was ridiculous.","Until a voice broke through the fog.","The street lamp in the darkness pulled her out of the coldness.","“If that person is dead, the box you took away might contain that person’s ashes. That’s why she reacted so strongly and insisted on catching you.”","Qiao Nian suddenly returned to her senses. Her gaze landed on him. She leaned forward and subconsciously grabbed him. “You mean... it’s impossible!”","She calmly gave a reason. “That box can’t hold a person’s ashes.”","Ye Wangchuan was still driving. No one knew where he was going. Upon hearing this, he only chuckled lazily and domineeringly. “Who told you all the ashes must be inside? What if she only has this much?”","Silence.","Qiao Nian sat back down and thought about this possibility.","Ji Lin was more direct. He took the box and opened it. “You’ll know after you take a look.”","The box itself did not have any mechanisms, probably because it was precious. Even Nie Qingru did not tamper with it.","Ji Lin opened it with a push. Seeing the dust inside, he looked at Qiao Nian in admiration. “Master Wang is right.”","There was really such a thing inside!","Qiao Nian also looked at it and then told him to close the box. Then, she rubbed her eyebrows and felt her eyelids twitch. Her expression became strange.","She had never thought about this before. She thought there was something confidential in the box, which was why Nie Qingru had set up so many traps to prevent anyone from touching it.","Ye Wangchuan asked her, “What are you going to do now?”","They happened to stop at a traffic light. He waited for the light to turn red, then looked back and asked her, “...Do you want to return it?”","Qiao Nian glanced at him in frustration. “Do you think she’ll believe I’m returning this to her? Don’t you think that as long as I appear, she’ll immediately turn me into ashes?”","In order to catch her, Nie Qingru had sealed off the airport and the port. It would be unreasonable if she still couldn’t catch her.","“You also know that she wants to catch you. Aren’t you worried?” Ye Wangchuan glanced at her and saw the blood on her arm. He smiled. “That’s true. You’re quite capable.”","For some reason, Qiao Nian detected anger in his tone. At least at this moment, she was quite afraid of him. She touched her earlobe awkwardly and explained, “At that time, I wasn’t sure which one contained the antidote, so I took both. Who knew there was a mechanism under one of them? I was already being very careful.”","It would have been better if she had not said anything. Ye Wangchuan said calmly, “Yes. If you had been any slower, I’d be collecting your corpse tonight.”","Qiao Nian was completely speechless.","Ji Lin did not dare to make a sound and tried his best to reduce his presence.","The red light quickly turned green. Ye Wangchuan looked ahead again and focused on driving, becoming mute again.","The atmosphere in the car was low.","Ji Lin did not even dare to breathe. He looked ahead and then to the side, not understanding why he was in this car.","He should be under the car, not inside..."]},{"number":3609,"title":"Chapter 3609: Master Wang, You Can’t Leave by the Port","paragraphs":["Chapter 3609: Master Wang, You Can’t Leave by the Port","Editor: Atlas Studios","Ye Wangchuan was angry, but he drove quickly and steadily. Upon entering the foggy harbor, he stopped the car, unbuckled his seatbelt, and said to the two of them, “Get out.”","Ji Lin was the first to get out of the car. He stood by the door and asked Qiao Nian, “Miss Qiao, do you want me to help you?”","“No need. I can leave by myself.” The girl was still wearing the clothes she had secretly exchanged for. She jumped out of the car easily and nimbly, looked at the brightly lit port, and turned to look at Ye Wangchuan. “Shall we leave from the port?”","Ji Lin wanted to say something but hesitated. “Master Wang, the old witch has sealed the airport and the ports. I’m afraid it won’t be easy for you to leave now. Why don’t you come back with me? I’ll think of a way to help you hide for two days...”","Ye Wangchuan walked straight ahead.","“It’s dangerous to stay any longer.”","Ji Lin could only chase after him. “But you and Miss Qiao really can’t leave now. I received news that Continent M is under full martial law. Even I can’t send you away at this time.”","Qiao Nian did not say anything. She clasped her hands and followed him.","Ji Lin grew anxious upon seeing the man in front of him was not listening to his advice. He turned to Qiao Nian and thought before saying, “Miss Qiao, please persuade Master Wang. The airport and port are the most dangerous places for you right now. Come back with me and I’ll think of a way. Even if Nie Qingru wants to lock down Continent M, it won’t be for long. As long as we can avoid being found out during this period, there won’t be a problem.”","Qiao Nian’s eyes were dark. She was speechless. She wanted to ask him: Can’t you tell that he’s angry with me?","However, Ji Lin looked at her as if she was his savior. It was as if he wanted to wag his tail at her, making Qiao Nian speechless.","“Miss Qiao...” Ji Lin thought she wanted to leave too and was about to analyze how dangerous it was for them to appear at the port.","Qiao Nian opened her mouth slowly. “I...”","The man in front seemed to have a pair of eyes on his back. He turned and said expressionlessly, “Ji Lin, what’s wrong? You don’t believe me?”","Ji Lin felt a chill down his spine. He could tell that Master Wang’s tone was serious. He opened his mouth and shook his head instinctively. “No. Of course, I believe you.”","Ye Wangchuan saw the figure from the corner of his eye. Seeing she was following behind leisurely without saying much, he felt suffocated. He pressed between his eyebrows to suppress his surging emotions and barked, “Then follow me!”","He turned and walked away.","Ji Lin had no choice but to follow.","Qiao Nian acutely sensed he looked at her for a second before looking away, as if he did not want her to notice.","Oh, so angry?","Qiao Nian looked at the man’s lean back and stopped, raising her hand to rub her swollen temples, feeling a headache.","It was inappropriate for her to hold him back at the port to explain anything. She could only touch her nose and continue to follow the two people silently.","Nie Qingru sealed the port very quickly.","There were a total of seven ports in Continent M.","The port that Ye Wangchuan drove to was the second largest one. It was also the central point where freight logistics converged.","While she completely sealed off the airport and all the ports, no matter how powerful Nie Qingru was, she couldn’t personally supervise every place.","Therefore, the specific implementation still depended on the people from the reclusive families under her.","Qiao Nian didn’t know how Nie Qingru convinced the old men in the Privy Council to agree. When they arrived at the port, they found many cargo owners negotiating with the people from the reclusive families."]},{"number":3610,"title":"Chapter 3610: Someone Is Here to Pick Them Up","paragraphs":["Chapter 3610: Someone Is Here to Pick Them Up","Editor: Atlas Studios","International shipping was not so simple.","Every cruise ship had the backing of a multinational corporation. Continent M’s sudden detention for a day undoubtedly disrupted the arrangements of these ferries.","Manpower costs and freight costs had to be increased.","How could the owners agree so easily?","Qiao Nian had foreseen the chaos, but she did not expect the port to be this chaotic.","At this moment, the people from the reclusive families were surrounded by close to 20 suppliers from various countries. Everyone was waving their hands and speaking their own language as they argued with him loudly. They chattered non-stop and were all agitated, their faces flushed red.","The person in charge, surrounded in the middle, also had a headache. Besides waving his hand to block others from approaching, he kept repeating, “No!”","Qiao Nian and the other two were not that impressed.","Ji Lin looked at the dozens of ferries moored at the port and stole a glance at Master Wang’s expression. Seeing that he was expressionless, he wasn’t sure if he was confident.","“Master Wang.”","As soon as he spoke, he saw a person shuttling through the noisy dock and approaching them from the dark night.","“Be careful.” Ji Lin immediately became vigilant. He stood before Ye Wangchuan and Qiao Nian and silently touched the gun hidden at his waist with his left hand, ready to draw it at any time.","Ye Wangchuan placed his hand on his shoulder and gently comforted him. “We’re on the same side.”","Ji Lin’s tense shoulders relaxed and he frowned. He subconsciously turned around to observe his expression. Before he could see clearly, the person walked up to them and greeted Ye Wangchuan directly. His attitude was very respectful. “Mr. Ye, Master told us that it’s inconvenient to talk here. Please follow me.”","Ye Wangchuan let out a “Mm” in a low nasal voice.","Ji Lin looked at him and then at the person before suspiciously asking, “Master Wang, do you know each other?”","Ye Wangchuan did not hide it from him. “A friend.”","Then, he turned to the girl.","Compared to Ji Lin, Qiao Nian was much quieter. Along the way, she basically did not speak. Now, it was as if she was not surprised at all. She just stood there and did not ask.","Ye Wangchuan felt even more suffocated!","If he did not talk to her, she would not be bothered, was that it?","He was clearly not a teenager, but Ye Wangchuan was still so angry at Qiao Nian that he almost laughed. He also felt it was stupid to be provoked so easily, but his heart still accelerated...","This time, Qiao Nian caught his lingering gaze and met his eyes.","Her clear eyes were filled with confusion and surprise as if asking him, “What’s the matter?”","Undoubtedly, she stepped on Ye Wangchuan again.","Looking away and taking a deep breath, he pursed his thin lips and said to the strange man, “Is there a doctor on the ship?”","“Yes, there is.” The person was stunned and looked at him from head to toe. “Mr. Ye, are you injured?”","After a short silence, Ye Wangchuan also felt his unilateral anger was childish. He immediately said, “No, my girlfriend suffered some external injuries.”","Only now did the person notice Qiao Nian. He turned to look at her for a moment before retracting his gaze. Then, he smiled and said, “We have a team doctor on the ship who can do a simple checkup and treatment. If your girlfriend’s injuries are serious, she has to go to the hospital.”"]},{"number":3611,"title":"Chapter 3611: So These Two Big Bosses Actually Know Mr. Cage","paragraphs":["Chapter 3611: So These Two Big Bosses Actually Know Mr. Cage","Editor: Atlas Studios","Ye Wangchuan nodded. “I know.”","That person looked at the surging waves and did not stand there to chat with them. “Then let’s go over. It’s almost time to set sail.”","“Mm.”","This time, Ye Wangchuan did not say anything else as he followed him.","...","The ship that the person talked about was actually a large ferry. With him leading the way, Qiao Nian and the other two did not encounter any obstacles along the way.","As they boarded the ship, Ji Lin couldn’t help but chat with the other party. “Are we going to set off now? Didn’t the reclusive families ban overseas ferries from leaving the port?”","The person revealed his white teeth and arrogantly said, “They issued a ban? Heh, and we can’t leave if they don’t let us? She can control the others, but she can’t control us! We can leave if we want!”","Ji Lin frowned. For a moment, he did not understand why the other party was so arrogant.","If they were in another place, Nie Qingru’s orders might not be so impressive and awesome. However, this was Continent M, the reclusive families’ lair.","If Nie Qingru did not have the power, it would be impossible for her to seal off the airport and the ports...","The man saw the disbelief in his eyes and patted his shoulder. “Don’t worry, we’ll definitely be able to leave.”","After saying that, he tilted his head and sized Ji Lin up with a strange expression. “But since you came with Mr. Ye, why don’t you know our background?”","Ji Lin felt very wronged. “...Ahem, I really don’t know.”","Fortunately, the man was not angry. Hearing this, he nodded slightly and introduced himself. “I’m Mr. Cage’s man.”","Ji Lin’s eyes suddenly widened, and his eyeballs almost fell out.","“C-Cage?”","“That’s right. Mr. Ye knows our master and is a good friend of ours. This time, he asked us to bring him out of the port. Our master asked us to ensure Mr. Ye’s safety.”","Ji Lin fell silent!","He was still wearing the snake ring Qiao Nian had given him. Then, the man in front of him told him that Master Wang and Mr. Cage had known each other for many years.","It seemed like he was the only extra person here.","However, he remembered mentioning to Master Wang several times on the phone that he wanted to book a military plane. At that time, Master Wang did not seem to have any reaction...","Ji Lin suddenly had an epiphany.","Therefore, it was not that his master could not get a military plane, but that he... was not worthy!","This realization hurt Ji Lin greatly for the next few minutes. He was so distracted that he did not hear what the other party was saying.","Until a crew member jogged over and said to that person, “Kimi, we’re about to sail.”","Ji Lin suddenly returned to his senses and hurriedly said, “I won’t go. I’ll go down if you’re setting off.”","“You’re not coming with us?” the man asked in surprise.","Ji Lin smiled. “I still have things to do here.”","That person nodded. “Alright, I’ll get someone to bring you down.”","He spoke to the crew and instructed one of them to guide Ji Lin off the ferry.","Ji Lin originally wanted to say goodbye to Qiao Nian and Ye Wangchuan. But after thinking about it, he decided not to and followed the crew member off the ship.","Then, he found a safe place and sent them a message, telling them he was going back first.","However, Ji Lin did not leave. Instead, he waited for the ferry to leave first.","There were still fierce arguments on the dock. The owners from all over the world were still shouting at the top of their lungs to let them go, but they were all rejected.","At this moment, Ji Lin saw the ferry emit a whistle. Following the sound of the water waves hitting the dock, the huge luxury ferry began to leave the port..."]},{"number":3612,"title":"Chapter 3612: Scum Thinks She’s a Cat Catching a Mouse","paragraphs":["Chapter 3612: Scum Thinks She’s a Cat Catching a Mouse","Editor: Atlas Studios","At the same time, the sails of the luxurious ferry were raised. The huge letter “K” on the white sails fluttered in the sea breeze.","At this moment, all the ferries in the port were forbidden to leave. The only ferry that left naturally attracted everyone’s attention.","Some were surprised, some were dissatisfied, and some were dumbfounded.","In short, no one expected that a ferry would be able to leave the port despite the reclusive families’ ban...","“What’s wrong with that ship? Why can they leave, but we can’t?!” Someone was so angry that he gritted his teeth and stomped his feet.","Those who had some insight and knew the inside story quickly shushed him. “Shut up, please. Don’t you see the logo on the sail? That’s the ferry of Continent F’s largest arms dealer, Cage. Of course, he can leave.”","Some people did not recognize the logo. They looked at the ferry leaving the port in a daze and muttered, “Who is that?”","**","At the same time, the black Rolls-Royce was speeding towards the port.","Nie Qingru spoke very little along the way. When they were almost at the port, she said coldly, “Are you sure that car is parked outside the dock?”","Shadow sat in the passenger seat and looked down. “I’m sure.”","Nie Qingru sneered three times. “I thought she was so capable, but it turns out she wants to escape through the open sea.”","If she caught her, she would definitely turn her into ashes to appease the hatred in her heart!","Shadow said softly, “If they want to leave Continent M, they can only choose a plane or a ferry. Now that these two places have been sealed by you, she probably only received the news that they are not allowed to leave the airport. She doesn’t know they are not allowed to leave the port either.”","Nie Qingru felt that Qiao Nian was not a rash person. Since she did not choose the airport, it was unlikely that she would not check if she could leave before coming to the port.","However, she was in a fit of anger and was not very rational. She did not want to delve into the small details and just thought what Shadow said was true.","Nie Qingru hurriedly lost her mind.","“Don’t blame me for being rude if she bumps into me!”","At this moment, the black Rolls-Royce drove into the dock and stopped at the innermost part of the harbor.","After the chauffeur parked the car, he turned around and said to the noblewoman in the back row, “Empress, we’ve arrived at the port.”","Nie Qingru took off her velvet gloves. Before getting out of the car, she sneered thoughtfully and said, “Where do you think this little rat will hide after realizing it can’t leave? It should be near the container that the rat should bring.”","Qiao Nian arrived at the dock before her. Calculating the time, she should have just realized she couldn’t leave.","With Qiao Nian’s personality, she could roughly guess that she would catch up. Then, it was time for the classic cat-and-mouse game.","Nie Qingru was the calm and unruffled cat, while the little b*stard was the mouse running around with its head in its hands. Once the mouse was caught, the cat had the right to decide whether it lived or died.","Shadow silently opened the door for her and waited for her to get out.","Nie Qingru snorted and stepped on the ground. “If she hadn’t touched that box, I would have given her a quick death for her mother’s sake. But she shouldn’t have taken what she couldn’t. This time, I’ll teach her humility!”","A thing that had not been taught by her mother was indeed not presentable!","Nie Qingru couldn’t hide her extreme disgust. After getting out of the car, she looked at the sea surface of the port from the corner of her eye. She originally thought she would see a quiet sea surface, but she was the first to notice the bright spots. A ferry was leaving the port!","Nie Qingru’s expression changed drastically as she pointed in that direction. “What’s going on over there!”"]},{"number":3613,"title":"Chapter 3613: Nie Qingru: Blow The Ship!","paragraphs":["Chapter 3613: Nie Qingru: Blow The Ship!","Editor: Atlas Studios","Shadow looked where she was pointing and immediately realized that a ferry was about to leave the port. In 10 minutes, it would completely leave the port.","He turned solemn. “That’s Cage’s ship...”","Nie Qingru’s expression was ugly as she said sternly, “I don’t care whose ship it is. Didn’t I say they’re not allowed to let any ferry go? Who let it go?!”","At this moment, the person in charge of the port rushed over. Upon seeing them, he carefully wiped his sweat. “Empress, Lord Shadow.”","Nie Qingru forcefully suppressed her anger. “What’s with that ship?”","The person in charge was at a loss. He looked at the sea and immediately understood what Nie Qingru was asking. He bowed and respectfully said, “That’s Mr. Cage’s ferry from Continent F. Elder Xue from the Privy Council let him go. Don’t worry, this ship is the only exception. The other ferries have not left the port.”","Nie Qingru quickly walked to the port and looked at the ferry out to sea from afar. On the deck, she saw an eye-catching figure.","“Qiao Nian!”","As she gnashed her teeth and shouted, Shadow looked at the figure on the deck in shock and saw the girl standing by the railing. The wind blew her shirt, making it flutter. The other party seemed to notice their gazes and looked over.","Her gaze was arrogant and decisive!","It was Qiao Nian!","Logically speaking, on the boundless sea, from a few kilometers away, they shouldn’t be able to see her face.","However, Shadow instantly confirmed that the girl standing on the deck was Qiao Nian, who had entered the vault alone and taken away the valuables.","The greatest failure in his life had also fallen into her hands...","Shadow couldn’t help but clench his fists. His back was as tense as a sharp blade, and he wanted to chase after her.","“Stop that ferry!” Nie Qingru commanded.","The person in charge was stunned. He looked at the ferry that had already left the port and said in a daze, “Empress, when you say stop it, do you mean...”","Nie Qingru’s blood rushed to the top of her head as she gritted her teeth. “Didn’t we bury cruise missiles at various ports? Shoot it down!”","The reclusive families controlled all aspects of Continent M, and the various airports and ports were also under their control.","There was nothing better than cruise missiles for port interception ambushes.","Therefore, it was not a big secret that cruise missiles were placed in various ports. It was just that no one expected that they would really need to use them one day.","The person in charge of the dock was stunned. For a moment, he suspected his ears were playing tricks on him. He stood rooted to the ground in a daze and looked at Nie Qingru cautiously. “Empress, are you joking? That ferry belongs to Mr. Cage. If we torpedo it down, it will be equivalent to becoming enemies with Mr. Cage. This is not appropriate...”","The biggest arms dealer in Continent F was Cage. Cage also had his own research and development team. Many of the high-end weapons on the market came from him.","Their reclusive families also maintained a friendly and cooperative relationship with him.","If they attacked and torpedoed the ferry, the intensity of their actions would be greater than sealing off all the airports and ports in Continent M.","This was no joke!","That Continent F weapons merchant was famous for being calculative and vengeful.","If they rashly did something like blowing up that person’s ferry, even if they went to Continent F to apologize and compensate him...","He might not even care about them.","However, Nie Qingru’s eyes were bloodshot. “I told you to blow the ship. Do you not understand?!”"]},{"number":3614,"title":"Chapter 3614: Empress, The Privy Council Wants You to Answer the Call","paragraphs":["Chapter 3614: Empress, The Privy Council Wants You to Answer the Call","Editor: Atlas Studios","The person in charge of the dock felt cold from head to toe. His entire body was drenched in cold sweat, but he still did not dare to stand out. He stuttered, “Empress, I, I don’t have this authority. If you insist on doing this, you have to discuss it with the elders of the Privy Council. I don’t dare to rashly activate the missile without a warrant...”","What he meant was that he did not dare to do it.","Nie Qingru’s killing intent took over.","That person was quite smart. Sensing her hostility, he gave his subordinates a look, and a skinny monkey-like dock worker quietly slipped away.","Nie Qingru’s chest heaved up and down as she tried her best to calm down. However, as soon as she saw the figure on the deck getting further and further away, she thought of what Qiao Nian had taken away.","She couldn’t calm down.","“You’re afraid of the consequences, right?”","“Empress.”","Nie Qingru’s deep eyes looked calm and unperturbed, but underneath them was a stormy sea. She stood proudly at the dock and said coldly, “I’ll bear this responsibility, no matter what it is. I want you to blow that ferry down immediately!”","She couldn’t leave any future troubles behind. She had to kill that little evil creature tonight.","No one could stop her!","The person in charge of the dock was shocked by her determined tone. For a moment, he did not know what to do... There was no room for him to refuse now.","Was he really going to blow Mr. Cage’s ferry?","At this moment, Shadow suddenly received a call. Seeing the caller ID, he walked to the side and picked it up. His expression changed immediately, and he hurried to Nie Qingru and handed her the phone. “Empress, it’s Elder Xue from the Privy Council.”","Nie Qingru’s eyelids twitched. She glanced coldly at the person in charge as if she could guess why the people from the Privy Council were calling her at this time.","She did not accept it. “I’m not answering. Tell them I’ll return after I’m done here.”","Shadow insisted, “Elder Xue wants to talk to you!”","Nie Qingru scrutinized him.","Shadow gritted his teeth and did not retreat. He still handed her the cell phone respectfully.","Nie Qingru’s eyes darkened. She knew Shadow wouldn’t insist for no reason. The people from the Privy Council must have said something, and Shadow thought she had to listen.","She slowly grabbed the phone and placed it next to her ear. Elder Xue’s calm voice came from the other end. He did not warn her or get excited. Instead, he said very calmly, “Your Majesty, we have already sealed all airports and ports according to your request. If you stop here, we will still be your loyal subjects. If you insist on disregarding the interests of the reclusive families and use missiles to blow Continent F’s Cage’s ferry, we will start the impeachment procedure at the same time. By then, you will no longer be the Empress of the reclusive families...”","The Privy Council existed to restrict the Empress’ power, and their greatest trump card was the impeachment process.","Under normal circumstances, the Privy Council didn’t have the right to initiate the impeachment process. The families wouldn’t agree to the Privy Council impeaching the Empress for no reason.","However, once Nie Qingru blew that ferry tonight, the Privy Council would tell her how much she would pay!","“The reclusive families believe in you, so you should set an example. We don’t care about your reasons to stop that ship, but if you sacrifice everyone’s interests to achieve your goal, the reclusive families will no longer need you.”"]},{"number":3615,"title":"Chapter 3615: Your Girlfriend Is So Young","paragraphs":["Chapter 3615: Your Girlfriend Is So Young","Editor: Atlas Studios","The reclusive families’ group was a huge corporation formed by hundreds of families. Nie Qingru could rule the entire reclusive families and use the Smith Bank under her to coerce them for her use... However, there was a limit to everything. She couldn’t cross the bottom line.","The call from the Privy Council tonight was to tell her where that bottom line was.","Nie Qingru had come this far, no one had dared to threaten her for a long time. But at this moment, facing the cold wind at the pier, she felt threatened for the first time.","“You want me to let her go?”","Elder Xue was calm. “We can’t offend Mr. Cage. It’s not in our interest.”","Nie Qingru clenched her fists as she looked at the figure on the deck getting further and further away from her. Suddenly, she sneered. “I didn’t expect to hear the same words 20 years later! Time really flies. What hasn’t changed is that I’m not strong enough.”","“You’re the Empress of the reclusive families...”","“Hmph!” Nie Qingru sneered. She didn’t comment. She had no choice but to lower her head under the threat. “I will remember today’s coercion.”","What she meant was that she was willing to let her go...","Elder Xue seemed to heave a sigh of relief. “The Empress is wise.”","Nie Qingru was provoked. The veins on her forehead bulged. She suddenly lost her composure and smashed the phone on the ground. Then, she suddenly turned to look at the ferry getting farther away.","The people on the deck seemed to have clairvoyance and knew what was happening on their side. As if sensing something, the corners of their lips curled up and they waved at them.","—Arrogance in capital letters!","Nie Qingru’s eardrums buzzed as she turned around and said in a low voice, “Let’s go!”","**","The ferry successfully sailed out of the port.","Qiao Nian watched from the deck as the people left without looking back. Her lips curled up. She raised her eyelids casually and lowered her hand.","From the moment Ye Wangchuan brought her on the boat and she saw the K symbol on the sail, she knew that Nie Qingru wouldn’t be able to keep her tonight.","However, she did not expect Nie Qingru to give up so easily.","It seemed that no matter what it was, it was not as important as the benefits in her eyes. Even the ashes of her most important person were nothing.","Qiao Nian suddenly lowered her eyes and stopped looking at the pier, feeling it was quite boring.","If a person only had benefits in their heart, they would only be a monster driven by benefits their whole life.","“What are you doing?”","The man’s lazy and casual voice came from behind her.","Qiao Nian turned around and saw Ye Wangchuan walking over. She suddenly felt much better. She leaned against the railing and said, “Nothing. I’m just looking outside.”","Ye Wangchuan looked past her and saw that Nie Qingru had already left with her men. They were no longer on the dock.","Ye Wangchuan retracted his gaze and looked at the girl’s arm. He pursed his thin lips and suppressed the dark emotions in his eyes. “Come with me. The doctor is waiting for you inside. You have to treat your wound to prevent it from getting infected.”","“Oh.”","Qiao Nian’s right hand hung down the entire night. No matter her emotions, she did not show them. Even though the wound on her right arm was deep and her muscles were torn, she did not show any sign of pain. She acted as if nothing was wrong the entire time. Besides not moving her right hand, no one could tell she was injured.","Even though Ye Wangchuan knew her tenacity, he still frowned and led the way without saying a word.","The team doctor of the ferry was waiting for them in the cabin. Seeing the girl’s beautiful face, he couldn’t help but be stunned.","“...So young?”","Ye Wangchuan dragged out a chair and indicated for Qiao Nian to sit. Then, he said to the doctor half-jokingly, “I don’t look old either.”"]},{"number":3616,"title":"Chapter 3616: No One Had Expected Her to Be So Badly Injured","paragraphs":["Chapter 3616: No One Had Expected Her to Be So Badly Injured","Editor: Atlas Studios","He was not old, but his superior temperament was too strong, making it easy for others to ignore his age. His appearance was too good, so it was difficult to notice that he was only in his early twenties.","The old team doctor touched his earlobe, smiled, and waved at Qiao Nian. “Little girl, come over quickly. Let me take a look at you.”","Qiao Nian walked over and sat down.","“Where are you hurt?” The old team doctor couldn’t tell where she was injured, so he simply asked her.","Qiao Nian turned sideways and said in a low and hoarse voice, “This arm.”","The old team doctor’s expression became a little more serious when he saw the blood seeping out of her shirt. However, seeing that there was not much blood on her sleeve, he still thought that it was a small injury.","“Then take off your jacket and let me take a look.”","“Mm.”","Qiao Nian was wearing a short-sleeved T-shirt over her shirt. This was her habit. She always liked wearing a T-shirt under the sweater.","When she took off her coat, the two people in the room realized how serious her injury was.","There was a centimeter-wide circular wound on her arm. It was only because of the cloth tied below that she was not bleeding. However, this also caused the blood flow in her arm to be unstable. The flesh around the wound was pale... One could feel the pain just by looking at it.","The old team doctor looked at her in disbelief. He couldn’t imagine how a young girl could look like nothing had happened despite the serious injury.","Ye Wangchuan’s eyes turned cold. His fingers curled and his eyelids twitched. He tried his best to suppress his emotions before saying to the old team doctor in a hoarse voice, “Then, I’ll have to trouble you!”","The old team doctor did not dare to underestimate him this time and replied with a serious expression, “Okay.”","He cleaned Qiao Nian’s wound first. Then, he used scissors to cut off the rotten flesh around the wound and put on the medicine. Finally, he wrapped the injured area with gauze layer by layer...","After doing all this, a cold sweat broke out on his forehead as he looked up.","The girl’s eyes were closed. Although her face was pale, she did not make a sound. She didn’t cry out even when he cut off the rotten flesh.","This endurance...","The old team doctor was used to seeing people unafraid of death in Continent F, but he still couldn’t help but admire her.","He put away his tools and said to Ye Wangchuan, “Your girlfriend... is not bad!”","Ye Wangchuan did not say anything. Instead, he looked at him and asked, “Are you putting her on a drip?”","The old team doctor thought about it and felt it made sense. “Sure, I’ll get her some anti-inflammatory medicine. You accompany her to get a drip later.”","He was efficient. After a while, he rummaged through the cabinets and found the anti-inflammatory water and infusion injection. He put an intravenous drip on Qiao Nian and smiled at Ye Wangchuan. “Take your time chatting. I’ll go out first.”","Ye Wangchuan said as he brushed past, “Thank you.”","The old team doctor waved his hand before leaving without looking back.","With the sound of the waves continuously hitting the hull in the background, Qiao Nian opened her tired eyes and leaned against the chair. She looked like she had lost interest in talking.","However, she still forced herself to perk up and glanced at the man who had pulled a chair over and sat beside her without saying a word. “You’re not angry anymore?”","Ye Wangchuan was so angry that he laughed. “What’s the use of being angry? Goddess Qiao won’t take it to heart.”","Qiao Nian choked and awkwardly placed her uninjured left hand on the back of the chair, thinking about how to explain it to him.","However, Ye Wangchuan pressed her against his shoulder and said steadily, “Sleep. I’ll keep an eye on the drip. I’ll wake you when it’s finished.”"]},{"number":3617,"title":"Chapter 3617: Master Wang’s Doting","paragraphs":["Chapter 3617: Master Wang’s Doting","Editor: Atlas Studios","Qiao Nian was still in a daze as she leaned against his firm shoulder. She had thought he wanted to clarify things and lecture her.","Now she realized he just wanted her to have something to lean on.","“You...” She was not used to relying on others.","Qiao Nian tried to move when a large hand pressed down on her head to stop her from moving. “I know you’re tired. Sleep. We’ll talk when you wake up!”","Ye Wangchuan felt the struggling head on his shoulder pause for a moment and then gradually relax.","Then, he unhurriedly continued, “There are too many people you want to protect, but no one is more important to me than you.","“If anything happens to you in your quest to find an antidote for Ji Lingfeng, I won’t let him off.”","—No one is more important to me than you!","Qiao Nian’s tense nerves were completely relaxed at this moment. The corners of her lips curled up, but she did not move. She quietly leaned on his shoulder and licked her lips, then said softly, “Actually... it hurts a little.”","She did not feel that this little pain was unbearable until now. In the past, she would endure it no matter how unbearable it was. Because no one would listen to her cry out in pain, she would not speak no matter how painful it was. There was no need for it to be meaningless.","But now, she suddenly felt that the pain was a little unbearable. At least, she suddenly wanted to say it.","For some reason, Ye Wangchuan’s anger was extinguished. He put his arm around the girl’s shoulder and softened his tone. “Sleep now.”","“Okay.” Qiao Nian seemed to give in and closed her eyes obediently.","She had thought that she would not be able to fall asleep after tonight’s tense situation. However, her endurance was far from her imagination. Her breathing pillowed on the faint smell of tobacco and peppermint, Qiao Nian gradually relaxed and her breathing became even...","Ye Wangchuan felt that the person leaning on his shoulder had fallen asleep. He was like a towering, unmoving mountain. He quietly slowed down the drip and sat back down, unwilling to wake up Qiao Nian’s sleeping form.","Someone came in halfway, but before they could say anything, they met a pair of cold eyes that shushed them.","No one was a fool. Seeing this scene, they smiled and left.","Everyone on the ferry knew not to enter the room and disturb them, so no one pushed the door open again.","Three hours later.","Qiao Nian’s infusion was over.","Ye Wangchuan looked at the empty bag and woke the sleeping girl before saying in a low voice, “I’ll take out the needle. Don’t move your hand.”","“Ah.” Qiao Nian’s eyes were half-closed, and she was still half-asleep. Her left hand was propped on the back of the chair, and her entire body looked dejected. It looked like she hadn’t even heard what he said clearly. “Yes, you do it.”","Ye Wangchuan glanced at her and noticed her half-closed eyes. Then, he looked at the IV tube on the back of her hand that had already begun to bleed. He quickly pulled out the needle and stood up to move his numb body before saying to the girl, “Don’t move. I’ll look for a cotton swab.”","He took the medical box from the old team doctor’s cabinet and found a cotton swab inside. He took one out, turned back, and pressed it on the back of Qiao Nian’s hand.","“Press it yourself.”","“Oh.”","Qiao Nian was still sleepy, but she obediently pressed the needle hole on the back of her hand with a cotton swab."]},{"number":3618,"title":"Chapter 3618: The Old Witch Doesn’t Want to Let Sister Nian Go","paragraphs":["Chapter 3618: The Old Witch Doesn’t Want to Let Sister Nian Go","Editor: Atlas Studios","There was some bleeding at the needle hole, and only a drop of blood emerged. In the past, she wouldn’t have cared about this small amount of bleeding. This time, she obediently used a cotton swab to stop the bleeding. Then, she looked up, her beautiful face eye-catching. “Are we going to Continent F with them next?”","Cage’s ship would definitely go to Continent F. He couldn’t sail to the independent continent.","It was not that the ferry couldn’t travel the distance, but that Cage’s identity as a big weapons merchant was special. It was easy to cause panic wherever he went.","His ship must not run amok.","“We’re almost at the open sea.” Ye Wangchuan walked to the window and opened it. It was dark outside, making it difficult to find them in the open sea. One could only hear the sound of waves hitting the shore.","Qiao Nian didn’t know how he could tell where they were in the darkness. Now that she was more awake, she thought of something and propped up the corners of her eyes. “Ji Lin said that pirates have been rampant recently. I can ask David to send someone to pick us up...”","Ye Wangchuan turned around and said meaningfully, “It’s too late.”","Qiao Nian frowned. Before she could ask, someone knocked on the door.","Ye Wangchuan said, “Come in.”","Someone came in.","Upon seeing them, the person’s expression turned serious. He nodded at Qiao Nian and walked up to Ye Wangchuan before saying coldly, “The pirates are here.”","Qiao Nian’s heart skipped a beat. She was surprised.","This ferry had Cage’s sails. Logically speaking, no pirate would be stupid enough to provoke a ship with the K symbol.","Unless... they were out of their minds.","Perhaps there was another possibility—someone had given them enough benefits to make them willing to take the risk!","Qiao Nian thought of someone.","Her eyes turned cold, and the corners of her mouth twitched mockingly. She felt a wave of heat in her heart for no reason, and the cold and dry feeling made her suddenly want to find something to do to divert her attention.","Qiao Nian’s right finger moved slightly, pulling her muscles near the wound. She immediately felt a sharp pain, reminding her that she was still injured...","It was rare for her to be so powerless. She cursed in her heart. Her face turned expressionless; it was as if she did not know who was behind this. Only her slightly furrowed brows revealed her bad mood.","The person did not notice Qiao Nian’s reaction as he spoke to Ye Wangchuan. “In the past, these sea locusts would always avoid us. I don’t know why they confronted us this time.”","He continued in a slightly irritated tone, “More than 20 pirate ships are gathered outside. They’re all small boats trying to surround the ferry. These small boats are nothing to be afraid of. I’m just worried that they want to sink the ferry.”","This was the sea!","The boundless sea.","Their ferry was not small, but even the largest ship could be swallowed by deep waters. Once the hull was damaged, it was much harder to deal with.","The boundless sea would immediately swallow the entire ferry. In the high seas, 20 to 30 ferries were sunk by pirates every year.","No one would be able to save them in time once that happened.","Qiao Nian clearly understood this and interrupted, “Can’t we fire?”","The man turned around and said seriously, “They took advantage of the night to sneak over. They stopped their engine 10 nautical miles away from us, then used manpower to row over, causing the brothers below to not notice their approach. At this distance, it’s too late even if we want to fire.”"]},{"number":3619,"title":"Chapter 3619: Master Wang Was Prepared","paragraphs":["Chapter 3619: Master Wang Was Prepared","Editor: Atlas Studios","The large ferry was equipped with weapons and ammunition. The pirates also knew this. They approached from 10 nautical miles away with the cover of night to avoid the range of artillery fire...","These ants had already closed in. Even if they opened fire now, it was too late.","This was also the terrifying and headache-inducing aspect of pirates!","They were like leeches attached to your legs. They had to suck you dry before they fell. Otherwise, you couldn’t shake them off.","Qiao Nian’s mind raced. She placed her left hand on her thigh and knocked lightly, thinking about how to resolve the current situation.","It was too late to call David or Guan Yan.","They had to solve the problem before the pirates could chisel the ship.","“Tell the pilot to turn southeast, as fast as possible,” Ye Wangchuan ordered calmly.","The man was a little confused. He wanted to say something but hesitated. “The pirates are driving speedboats. They’ve been modified. Even if we change directions, we won’t be able to shake them off.”","Qiao Nian looked up at Ye Wangchuan. “You want to stall for time?”","The man did not expect Qiao Nian to respond. He looked in her direction again and realized from her hint that although this method did not solve the problem, it was the best solution.","“I’ll go tell the people below.”","He thanked Ye Wangchuan and quickly went out to make arrangements.","Only Qiao Nian and Ye Wangchuan were left in the cabin. Qiao Nian looked at the man and was suddenly less anxious. “You have other arrangements.”","She spoke confidently as if she was sure that Ye Wangchuan had a backup plan.","Ye Wangchuan pursed his lips and smiled. “I wouldn’t have brought you on the boat if I didn’t have any arrangements.”","He invited Qiao Nian. “Let’s go. I’ll bring you up to watch the show!”","...","Qiao Nian followed him out to the deck. As the sea breeze blew, she saw the 20-odd speedboats and pirate ships surrounding their ferry under the spotlight. Only then did she feel the reality of Ji Lin’s words.","These pirates were very arrogant. They chased after and surrounded the ferry, shouting and whistling arrogantly.","The arrogant and provocative whistles sounded one after another as if this ferry was a huge prey they had surrounded. Sooner or later, it would be brought down by them.","They were enjoying the pleasure of driving people into a desperate situation, willfully laughing at the innocent ferry crew.","Qiao Nian’s eyes quickly turned cold. She leaned against the railing, straightened her back, took out a silver lighter with her uninjured left hand, and played with it.","“Doesn’t she feel guilty for allowing pirates to rob in the high seas for her own benefit?”","She laughed as soon as she finished speaking.","Then, she lowered her eyes, looking rather frustrated. “That’s true. How can she feel guilty? In her eyes, everyone is just an ant. How can the life and death of a group of ants be more important than her interests?”","Ye Wangchuan knew who she was talking about, but he could not bear to see Qiao Nian upset. He ruffled the girl’s hair, then pinched her face. Qiao Nian stiffened. As she looked at him with her dark eyes, Ye Wangchuan retracted his hand as if nothing had happened and continued from where she had stopped. “Anyway, you’ve already gotten the antidote. We can talk about the international waters when you get back.”","Qiao Nian nodded. She knew it was useless to flare up now. Thus, she suppressed her anger and tilted her head to ask him, “How do you plan to get rid of these people?”"]},{"number":3620,"title":"Chapter 3620 They’re the Ones Who Can’t Leave!","paragraphs":["Chapter 3620: They’re the Ones Who Can’t Leave!","Editor: Atlas Studios","“Who said I was going to get rid of them?”","Ye Wangchuan leaned against the railing like her. The sea breeze swept his hair. Only then did Qiao Nian notice he was wearing a black jacket today. His shoulders were broad and straight, sharpening his jaw. It was different from his usual elegant and noble style. It was a little cool.","At this moment, he met Qiao Nian’s gaze. A ripple appeared in the depths of his deep eyes, reflecting her shadow. He was a proud son of heaven and was wanton and arrogant.","“I asked Kimi to accelerate just to increase the distance between us and them. Otherwise, it’s easy to hurt the innocent when we fight later.”","What?","Qiao Nian instantly looked away and heard the sound of a spiral machine tearing through the air.","She jerked her head up and saw a dozen fighter jets roaring toward them from the southeast, almost as soon as she spotted the planes.","The sky fighter jets began to fire at the sea.","Bang! Bang! Bang!","Flames lit up the sky and tore open the dark sea, allowing light to enter—","The pirates who were arrogantly chasing after the ferry a second ago panicked. They stopped whistling and being arrogant.","Qiao Nian could hear them shouting at the top of their lungs, “Run, run!”","“Damn it, they have planes. Run!”","There were very few fighter jets in the open sea, and a carrier was needed for these fighter jets to take off. That carrier was what caused these audacious pirates to tremble in fear—a cruise ship.","“Run!”","The pirates cried for their parents and desperately ran around on the speedboat. However, the pursuit ability of the sky was definitely not something that could be compared to dodging at sea level.","There was a huge gap between the two sides.","With the sky lit with flames, Qiao Nian saw Ye Wangchuan’s cell phone light up. The man standing on the deck put the phone to his ear and casually accepted the call. “Hello.”","“Young Master Ye, those people...”","The side of his face was enveloped in flames, like an Asura. “Leave no one behind.”","His eyes were dark, and his thin lips curled up. He suddenly looked at the pirate ships in the night. His slender fingers held the cell phone, and his voice was dissipated by the wind. “Didn’t they rob our fishing boats not long ago? It’s time to teach them a lesson! Let them know that even in the open sea some ships can’t be touched! If they do, they have to pay the price!”","“Yes, Young Master Ye.”","The fighter jet chased after the pirate ships and threw out a tracking missile. It was a lightning-fast method to show all the pirates in the high seas.","The soaring flames lit up the pitch-black sea surface, and the waves set off raging waves. One after another, evil speedboats were blown up in the middle of the sea.","One ship, two ships...","About 10 speedboats sunk into the deep sea, and the others couldn’t escape.","When everything was over, the sea level returned to normal. Only then did the people on the ferry dare to look at the young man on the deck. Everyone’s eyes were filled with shock and fear.","Ye Wangchuan faced the breeze as he looked at the calm sea. There was no emotion in his eyes. No one knew what he was thinking.","Qiao Nian understood what he was doing when he said the pirates had touched his fishing boats. She didn’t try to be pretentious and just said coldly, “If it were me, I would do the same.”","These pirates had always been outlaws.","It was impossible to suppress them without using thunderous methods.","Only by doing what Ye Wangchuan did today could these people understand the rules!","At this moment, a helicopter flashed its propeller and stopped on the ferry’s tarmac. Then, Gu San jumped out of the driver’s seat."]},{"number":3621,"title":"Chapter 3621: Gu San Is Here Too","paragraphs":["Chapter 3621: Gu San Is Here Too","Editor: Atlas Studios","Gu San’s tough face instantly revealed joy upon seeing Qiao Nian and Ye Wangchuan. He quickly walked over. “Miss Qiao, Master Wang!”","He scratched his head and said in embarrassment, “Miss Qiao, I’m not late, am I? I rushed over after receiving Master Wang’s order. Fortunately, I made it in time.”","Qiao Nian looked at a certain someone again. “You already guessed that Nie Qingru wouldn’t let us go easily?”","From the moment he rushed over to save her to the point when he heard that the reclusive families had sealed off the airports and the ports, to rushing to the port without hesitation and having Cage’s ships receive him...","Now that Gu San had appeared and said everything was going according to his plan, even Nie Qingru’s reaction was within his expectations.","Qiao Nian suddenly remembered Qin Si’s joke—’Master Wang can kill by playing mind games.’","That really matched Qin Si’s evaluation.","He was simply a walking humanoid bug.","She could imagine Nie Qingru’s anger upon receiving the news.","However, Qiao Nian couldn’t help but laugh. In any case, she was quite happy herself. Especially when she thought about how Nie Qingru and the reclusive families weren’t happy, she was even happier!","* * *","10 hours later.","The helicopter arrived at the independent continent and stopped on the First Research Institute’s tarmac.","Feng Yu was already waiting for them by the helipad. Seeing that Qiao Nian had returned unscathed, he heaved a sigh of relief and became angry. “You really make yourself work hard every single day. Sooner or later, I’ll have a heart attack from you!”","“...It’s good that you’re fine.”","He was about to pat the girl’s right arm when someone grabbed his hand.","“Elder Feng.”","Feng Yu looked at Ye Wangchuan’s serious face. “Her arm is injured.”","Feng Yu was shocked. He suddenly looked at Qiao Nian, his temples throbbing, as if he had something to say, but he couldn’t utter it.","“Forget it!”","His eyes were filled with helplessness. In the end, he could only compromise.","“Even if I tell you, you won’t take it to heart. Next time, you’ll still rush into danger. Anyway, I’ll tell you that you’re still young and have a long time ahead of you. If you torture yourself like this every day, let’s see if you regret it in the future...”","Qiao Nian listened to his ramble on without stopping him. She only stopped at the door and said to him, “I’m going to the hospital.”","Feng Yu was stunned before immediately saying, “I’ll arrange a car for you.”","“Alright.” Qiao Nian did not reject his good intentions this time.","Feng Yu looked at her fatigued face and did not say anything more. He immediately got someone to arrange a car.","...","This time, Qiao Nian used the First Research Institute to enter the country. As long as she did not say anything, no one would know she had gone to Continent M and turned it upside down.","Feng Yu arranged an inconspicuous car for her. After Qiao Nian entered, the chauffeur received Feng Yu’s instructions and drove straight to the hospital where Ji Lingfeng was hospitalized.","It was still evening in the independent continent.","The sunset dyed the sky orange, and the clouds dragged out a long tail like the airplane exhaust.","Qiao Nian relaxed and rubbed her eyebrows before opening the window for some fresh air. Then, she thought of something and took her phone from her pocket and searched for a number on her blacklist.","Upon finding it, she slowly typed a message before sending it."]},{"number":3622,"title":"Chapter 3622: Sister Nian Sent Her a Message","paragraphs":["Chapter 3622: Sister Nian Sent Her a Message","Editor: Atlas Studios","The next second, the message was sent successfully.","A dark glint flashed across her eyes. Not giving the other party a chance to reply, she put the number back on the blacklist.","After doing all this, Qiao Nian put her phone back in her pocket and took out candy. She leaned against the seat, tore open the wrapper, threw the fruit candy into her mouth, and closed her eyes to rest...","**","Continent M.","Nie Qingru returned to her residence under the cover of night.","Everyone in the castle could sense her anger. No one dared to provoke her at this time. Even the servants serving tea walked softly, afraid of making a sound.","Nie Qingru took a sip of black tea but could not calm down. She tightened her grip on the teacup and threw it to the ground with a ferocious expression.","Smack!","The porcelain shattered with a crisp sound.","The servants held their breaths and groaned inwardly.","What was wrong with the Empress? Why was she so angry?","One had to know that this master was famous for being cold and aloof. Even if she was not a good person, because of her arrogance, she rarely revealed her emotions.","There was an unapproachable coldness about her, but she rarely showed such an angry side in front of the servants.","At this moment, Shadow walked in front of Nie Qingru and saw the broken teacup on the ground. It was from her favorite tea set.","He silently called for someone to clean it up before saying to the woman sitting on the sofa, “Empress, there’s news from the international seas that our people have been completely wiped out.”","A cold light flashed in Nie Qingru’s eyes, but she did not seem surprised. She sneered three times. “She’s really capable. Someone even protected her on the high seas!”","Silence.","Shadow knew he shouldn’t say anything at this moment, but out of a sense of responsibility, he still braced himself and said it. “It’s Ye Wangchuan’s work.”","Nie Qingru shot him a sharp look and frowned. Her face was as dark as water. It was obvious she was extremely dissatisfied with this news.","Shadow lowered his head. “Ye Wangchuan should have set off from the port long ago. He also expected that we wouldn’t be able to stop the ship and could only attack in the open sea. Therefore, he had already laid an ambush and waited for our people, burying them all in the sea. Now, the pirates in the open sea are all in danger. No one dares to provoke the relevant ships...”","This meant they would lose control of the high seas.","Nie Qingru clearly understood his meaning. The veins on the back of her hand bulged as she tried her best to endure it. Her already ugly expression became even more solemn. If it weren’t for some rationality holding her back, she might not have been able to maintain her elegant silence and would have directly flown into a rage.","“Good job, she’s really good! As expected of my good granddaughter. She knows how to anger me to death.”","Although she said that, she hated Qiao Nian in her heart.","Shadow didn’t know how to persuade her.","Nie Qingru didn’t need anyone’s persuasion. After being so angry that her scalp went numb for a short while, she picked up the cell phone on the table to contact the Privy Council.","Then, she saw a new message notification.","Nie Qingru looked at the sender with a cold expression and sneered. She raised her chin slightly and said in a gentler tone, “She even knows how to send me a message.”","The sender was Qiao Nian.","She was thinking about what Qiao Nian could possibly say to her.","However, upon seeing the message, Nie Qingru’s disdainful smile faded, and her face became cloudy.","[Q: I’m in the independent continent.]","Extremely concise.","Such an understatement."]},{"number":3623,"title":"Chapter 3623: Sister Nian: I Won’t Go In For Now","paragraphs":["Chapter 3623: Sister Nian: I Won’t Go In For Now","There were no unnecessary words. It seemed a statement of fact, but after combining it with the current situation, it seemed especially arrogant and provocative.","Nie Qingru imagined the girl curling her lips into a mocking smile, raising her eyebrows, and saying, “Are you quite disappointed? I’m in the independent continent.”","“Heh.” Nie Qingru’s breathing paused for a moment before she let out a breath of cold air. Her eyes were covered in frost as she squeezed out two words. “Death wish!”","**","Qiao Nian received a call from Ji Nan on the way to the hospital.","Upon arriving there, Ji Nan came out to pick her up and brought her to the ward. On the way, Qiao Nian also asked about his father’s health.","Ji Lingfeng’s health was not good.","He had been vomiting blood for the past two days. If not for Zhong Yiliu guarding him, Ji Lingfeng wouldn’t have survived the past few days.","Ji Nan clearly knew this. As they went up the stairs, he said to Qiao Nian, “It’s all thanks to Elder Zhong these few days. Otherwise, my father wouldn’t have been able to last until you returned.”","Qiao Nian walked in front, wearing her usual sweater with a flamboyant print on the front. She was wearing a black baseball cap with the brim lowered.","She looked no different from usual, so Ji Nan did not notice her arm injury.","The girl replied lazily, “Ah, got it.”","Ji Nan had wanted to ask her how to thank Elder Zhong, but Qiao Nian did not mention this. He couldn’t continue on the topic at this juncture.","They went up to the second floor in silence. When they were about to reach the ward, the girl suddenly stopped.","Ji Nan was a step away from her. He was stunned for a moment when she stopped. “Why have you stopped? We’re almost there.”","However, Qiao Nian did not move. She raised her baseball cap with her left hand and revealed her beautiful eyes as she looked at him and said, “Go on. I won’t go in. I’ll go ask Master Zhong about the situation.”","Ji Nan did not expect Qiao Nian to not visit. After a short moment of shock, he felt it was not strange that Qiao Nian. After all, the two of them had awkward personalities.","Hence, he nodded and did not insist on it. “Elder Zhong is in the next room. He requisitioned it as a temporary office.”","“Mm,” Qiao Nian replied. She waved at him with her left hand and went over without looking back.","Her back view was carefree.","Ji Nan watched her walk into the office before turning around and walking towards Ji Lingfeng’s ward.","Suddenly, he stopped in his tracks.","He turned around and looked in the girl’s direction. He seemed to have realized something and frowned fiercely. His expression also became uncertain.","Why did he feel that Qiao Nian’s right hand seemed today? She had also waved at him with her left hand...","He suddenly thought of something and wanted to chase after her to ask.","However, he hesitated, afraid that he was overthinking and would cause trouble.","After a short moment of hesitation, Ji Nan decided to wait for Qiao Nian to come back before asking about it. Then, he might as well return to the ward to see Ji Lingfeng and wait for her.","***","In Zhong Yiliu’s provisory office next door.","Qiao Nian did not know that Ji Nan had noticed that her right arm was injured.","As she approached the door, she heard voices from inside.","Like Zhong Yiliu and a doctor.","They were discussing Ji Lingfeng’s condition."]},{"number":3624,"title":"Chapter 3624: She Really Brought The Antidote Back!","paragraphs":["Chapter 3624: She Really Brought The Antidote Back!","A younger voice was saying, “The patient vomited blood again at 6:10 PM. This time, the blood test results are not optimistic. The amount of bacteria in his body is still increasing. If this continues, his internal organs will be corroded. It will be too late to detoxify the poison. The antidote can detoxify the poison, but it can’t repair his damaged internal organs. He’ll still be a dead man.”","“I know that even if you don’t tell me!”","This voice belonged to Zhong Yiliu. He was quite exasperated. Qiao Nian could tell from his tone that he was frustrated and helpless about the current situation.","The voices were getting closer.","The young doctor said again, “Elder Zhong, do you have the antidote? We really can’t wait any longer. If we don’t have the antidote, we can only give the patient’s family notice of the critical illness. The patient’s identity is special, so we have to mentally prepare the family in advance.”","In fact, during this period, the various factions in the independent continent had been thinking of ways to inquire about Ji Lingfeng from the hospital.","Xie Yun and a few elders of the Ji family had already ordered the hospital not to divulge the patient’s health, but they couldn’t withstand countless harassment.","As one of Ji Lingfeng’s attending physicians, his house had been filled with anonymous letters for the past few days. There were all kinds of transaction methods and overseas accounts inside. Those people had spent money to buy Ji Lingfeng’s specific medical report.","Of course, he did not dare to leak the secret.","He was just an ordinary person, after all. He was also afraid that those people would have other ideas to force him to compromise after not being able to get the information from him.","His son was only five years old and was still in kindergarten.","During this period, he did not dare to let the child go to school, afraid that something would happen.","However, this was not a solution for the long term.","He also wanted to resolve the matter quickly and give him peace even if there was a result.","He said, “...If there’s no antidote, the patient will only have about two more days.”","Zhong Yiliu walked out of the room and fell silent. He knew the young man was right, but he did not want to face failure.","He had never had anyone in his care die before.","Even if Ji Lingfeng had nothing to do with him this time, and even if a god would find it difficult to save him, he was still impacted and did not feel good.","“Let’s wait a little longer.”","“Elder Zhong.”","“I said, let’s wait a little longer,” Zhong Yiliu insisted.","The young man could not say anything else and compromised helplessly. “Alright then.”","Zhong Yiliu turned around and was about to enter when he saw someone waiting in the room. He was surprised. “Qiao Nian, you...”","Qiao Nian stood up and politely nodded at him. “I’m back.”","Zhong Yiliu’s eyes lit up. Ignoring the outsider around, he quickly walked towards her. “Since you’re back, the antidote...”","He had yet to finish speaking when Qiao Nian took out a porcelain bottle and placed it on the table. Then, she looked up and said to him, “I brought it back.”","Zhong Yiliu looked at the porcelain bottle quietly placed on the table and opened his mouth a few times before closing it again. When he looked at the girl again, his expression was indescribable.","“You...”","He didn’t know how Qiao Nian got the antidote from Nie Qingru. Just thinking about it, he could guess how dangerous it was.","But she really brought it back!","After the shock, Zhong Yiliu became happy. He did not hide his joy. He picked up the porcelain bottle on the table and could not control his excitement as he said to the doctor at the door, “Oh, hurry up and prepare. Let’s do a potion experiment on the patient first to test the effect of the antidote. If it’s feasible, let’s follow the plan we formulated previously and detoxify the patient as soon as possible.”"]},{"number":3625,"title":"Chapter 3625: Elder Zhong’s Eyes Are Vicious","paragraphs":["Chapter 3625: Elder Zhong’s Eyes Are Vicious","The young doctor did not expect the antidote to be delivered as soon as they needed it.","He did not dare to delay and hurriedly said, “I’ll inform the others in the team.”","Ji Lingfeng had a specialist medical team led by Zhong Yiliu, with seven or eight different specialists from various departments.","If Zhong Yiliu wanted to do a potion experiment for Ji Lingfeng, he needed to gather all the doctors from various departments to prevent any accidents midway. He could also carry out the surgery immediately.","Zhong Yiliu waited for him to leave before looking at the girl with undisguised joy. “How did you find this antidote? Did you rely on selling medicine?”","Qiao Nian did not hide it from him.","She briefly explained how she had used the genetic medicine as bait and how she had infiltrated Nie Qingru’s vault.","She hid the part about the danger and only said casually that she came back after getting the antidote.","However, Zhong Yiliu could tell the danger in her calm narrative. He did not say anything and only patted her arm. “It’s good that you’re back.”","However, just as he was about to touch her arm, the girl dodged his hand. Then, she stood up and said, “Go examine him first.”","Seeing how quickly she had dodged him, Zhong Yiliu, the old demon, after living for dozens of years, immediately wrinkled his nose and stopped her. “What happened to your hand? Are you injured?”","Qiao Nian did not expect him to see through her at a glance. “Uh, it’s a small injury. It’s not important. Let’s go check if the antidote is real.”","Zhong Yiliu stubbornly refused to move aside. His expression was serious, and he did not believe a word of it. “A small injury, then why did you hide just now? With your personality, you wouldn’t even frown if you were seriously injured. How could you dodge my hand and even change the topic?”","He did not waste any time and stretched out his hand showing rare anger. “Let me see your injury. Is it serious?”","Qiao Nian looked at him, but Zhong Yiliu refused to budge. They stared at each other for a few seconds, but Qiao Nian was still defeated.","“Tsk, I said it’s a small injury...” Her tone was firm as she helplessly returned to her seat. She pulled up her sleeve to reveal her bandaged right arm.","Qiao Nian’s movements were not fast. When her sleeve rubbed against the wound, her shoulders tensed and she tried her best to endure the pain. There was nothing unusual on the surface.","She revealed her fully bandaged right arm to Zhong Yiliu and said casually, “I said it’s a small injury.”","Qiao Nian pulled down her sleeve before Zhong Yiliu could check it.","“I’ve already dealt with it. It’ll be fine in a few days.”","Zhong Yiliu gave her a look. She didn’t even let him check. He knew she was lying.","Why couldn’t he check it if it was just a small injury?","Unless her arm was seriously injured and Qiao Nian did not want him to know. That was why she pulled down her sleeve so quickly and did not let him see.","“You just don’t take yourself seriously!” Zhong Yiliu was quite angry but couldn’t say anything about her.","Qiao Nian still looked nonchalant. Her eyelashes were slightly lowered as if she was not injured and Zhong Yiliu was being too serious. However, she still patiently comforted him. “I know I was wrong. I was careless this time... I promised someone else that I would pay attention next time.”","Zhong Yiliu was rendered speechless. He sized her up with a surprised expression as if he had seen a ghost. “Who else can make you reflect on yourself? That person must be capable.”"]},{"number":3626,"title":"Chapter 3626: Sister Nian Steps Out to Guarantee","paragraphs":["Chapter 3626: Sister Nian Steps Out to Guarantee","Qiao Nian avoided his gaze this time. She did not satisfy his curiosity and just coughed. “Let’s go over.”","Zhong Yiliu was only worried about her, he did not make things difficult for her. He did not ask further, seeing she was unwilling to mention the details. Before leaving, he said without looking back, “If your arm is not doing well, remember to look for me. I’ll check and treat it for you again.”","Qiao Nian’s heart warmed and she nodded.","“Hmph!” Zhong Yiliu was still angry. He snorted again. “How can the medicine outside be better than mine? It’s just that you don’t treat yourself as a girl. Your skin is thick. If you get a scar on your arm later, I’ll see who you can cry to.”","He sped up before adding, “But you found a boyfriend too. If you want to cry, he should be the one crying. I don’t care about you.”","Qiao Nian was caught between laughter and tears as she followed half a step behind him. She dug her ears as she listened to his nagging.","**","Ji Lingfeng’s attending physicians were all gathered outside the ward. Seven to eight people discussed whether the antidote and Ji Lingfeng’s physical condition were suitable.","Seeing Zhong Yiliu bringing a young girl over, they greeted him, “Elder Zhong.”","“Master Zhong.”","“President Zhong.”","Some called him Elder Zhong, others called him Master Zhong, and some called him President.","Zhong Yiliu did not care about his reputation in the outside world. He raised his hand to stop them from exchanging pleasantries and said concisely, “I believe you already know why I called you over.”","He looked at everyone and did not beat around the bush. “That’s right. We’ve found the antidote. Next, we’re conducting a blood detoxification experiment on the patient. You’re all experts from various departments. I called you here just in case. If anything happens, we resuscitate the patient with you around.”","The pulmonary specialist said hesitantly, “But Elder Zhong, the patient’s physical condition doesn’t allow us to use intense medical treatment...”","Zhong Yiliu’s face tensed, and he criticized him impolitely. “Pedantic!”","Then, he said in exasperation, “Why are you so stubborn at such a young age? You’ve been in a regular medical institution for so long that you have forgotten your original intention.”","The lung expert’s face turned red from the scolding. He was extremely embarrassed. “I’m sorry, Elder Zhong.”","“I know what you’re worried about.” Zhong Yiliu waved his hand, telling him to shut up. “But every surgery is risky. If we don’t dare to take risks for the patient, what kind of doctor are we?! As a doctor, I’ll always stick to my original intention—prioritize the patient’s life. Life is more important than anything else! His current physical condition is indeed unable to accept too intense medical treatment. Let me ask you, how long can he last if we continue to treat him conservatively? A day? A week? A month?”","The pulmonologist was completely speechless.","Ji Lingfeng’s various statistics were there. He couldn’t last a month, perhaps a day or two...","Just as Zhong Yiliu had said, if they did not carry out the detoxification experiment, Ji Lingfeng would only slowly die in the conservative treatment.","“But the patient’s identity is special...” Some experts were still worried and voiced their concerns.","At this moment, Qiao Nian stood up and said concisely, “I’ll communicate with his family. You just have to treat him. Regardless of the outcome, I guarantee that the Ji family won’t find trouble with you after this.”"]},{"number":3627,"title":"Chapter 3627: Auntie Xie, We Have No Other Choice!","paragraphs":["Chapter 3627: Auntie Xie, We Have No Other Choice!","A few experts were called over by Zhong Yiliu later. One or two were there from the beginning and knew Qiao Nian.","Seeing that Qiao Nian had promised nothing would happen to them, one or two pulled their companions’ hands, indicating that they should stop talking and trust Elder Zhong.","Although the other experts were frightened, they still chose to do their own final checkup for Ji Lingfeng in the face of Zhong Yiliu and Qiao Nian’s insistence.","After getting the latest indicators, they would immediately conduct an antidote skin test on Ji Lingfeng.","As it was a skin test, they did not inject too many antidotes into the patient’s body. They just wanted to see if his body could accept the antidotes and if there would be any resistance.","By right, this process was unlikely to lead to major problems.","At this moment, Qiao Nian found Ji Nan and Xie Yun and told them about the antidote. At the same time, Zhong Yiliu led the team of experts to finish Ji Lingfeng’s skin test.","A young nurse ran out to inform them. “The patient’s family members, get ready. The patient has finished the skin test.”","Ten minutes later.","An expert in a white coat rushed over and looked at Ji Nan and Xie Yun before saying seriously, “The patient has shown slight rejection towards the antidote. It might be dangerous if this continues. May I ask if you still insist on injecting the antidote?”","Xie Yun subconsciously grabbed Ji Nan’s arm and gritted her teeth upon hearing the words “rejection” and “dangerous”, not answering immediately.","She looked at Qiao Nian as if wanting her to answer.","“Nian Nian, we—”","Qiao Nian did not expect Ji Lingfeng to resist the drug either. She rubbed her eyebrows before giving Xie Yun a comforting look. Then, she said in a hoarse voice, “Auntie Xie, you’ve been guarding here for so long. You should know his physical condition by now. If we don’t continue to detoxify him, the poison in his blood alone can kill him. We have no other choice!”","Xie Yun met that pair of cold and rational eyes. Her heart sank and she suddenly stopped panicking. She pursed her lips before turning to the expert. “We’ll insist on the antidote.”","The specialist nodded and confirmed again. “You insist on the antidote? Alright, I’ll convey your intentions to Elder Zhong.”","He hurried out and hurried back in.","The entire process did not take more than a minute.","The lights in the operating room remained lit up for three hours. During this period, medical staff would come out from time to time to update them on the patient’s situation.","The first few times were all bad news.","Zhong Yiliu divided the antidote into three batches and injected them into Ji Lingfeng’s veins one after another. Each time, the amount was not large, as he had to take Ji Lingfeng’s fragile body into account.","Even so, Ji Lingfeng’s health was worse than everyone had imagined.","The first time the nurse came out, she said red bumps had appeared under Ji Lingfeng’s skin. It was suspected that he was allergic.","The second time the nurse came out, she said that after the second injection, Ji Lingfeng had a stroke and panted rapidly. She suspected that he had an asthma attack.","The third time the nurse came out, she said that Ji Lingfeng’s lungs were also starting to swell.","***","If it weren’t for Ji Nan and Qiao Nian, Xie Yun would not have been able to hold on. Every time the door opened, she was afraid of hearing ‘Sorry, the patient is gone’ the most.","Fortunately, after the initial danger, Ji Lingfeng’s situation improved.","The more the nurse reported, the more optimistic she became.","“The patient has received three injections of the antidote. The toxin indicator is decreasing, and the edema in his lungs is under control. The doctors are waiting an hour for the data. If the toxin indicator continues to decrease, the patient can be wheeled out.”"]},{"number":3628,"title":"Chapter 3628: Mom, Let Her Go Back and Sleep","paragraphs":["Chapter 3628: Mom, Let Her Go Back and Sleep","Xie Yun finally heaved a sigh of relief after persevering for three hours. Her legs were weak. If not for Ji Nan’s quick reflexes, she would have to support herself against the wall to stand.","However, Xie Yun smiled. “That’s great, that’s great.”","She was physically and mentally exhausted, but at this moment, the sunlight shone into the haze of the past half a month and pulled her out of the endless abyss.","After Ji Lingfeng was detoxified, even if there were minor side effects, he would at least be able to keep his life.","Xie Yun couldn’t describe how she felt at this moment. All her worries and waiting for the best returns made her happy from the bottom of her heart.","“Your dad’s okay,” she whispered to Ji Nan.","Then, she immediately walked up to Qiao Nian and bowed solemnly without a word. Her bow was at a 90o angle and was very cautious.","Qiao Nian was leaning against the wall with her legs bent, waiting for the results. She was playing games on her cell phone with one hand when the light in front of her was suddenly blocked. She looked up and saw Xie Yun bowing to her.","Stunned, she immediately put away her cell phone and tried to help her up with her left hand. “Auntie Xie...”","Xie Yun persisted in her bow. “It’s all thanks to you this time. Don’t treat me as an elder. This is my gratitude to you as a wife.”","Qiao Nian couldn’t move her right arm. She couldn’t dissuade Xie Yun with just one hand. From the corner of her eye, she saw a certain someone watching the commotion and said speechlessly, “Come help me.”","Only then did Ji Nan slowly approach and support Xie Yun. “Mom, don’t be like this. You’re scaring her.”","Xie Yun was not a pretentious person. When Ji Nan pulled her, she stood up. Her serious expression changed into a smile as she rebuked, “I’m thanking Nian Nian. I’m not like you. You don’t even know how to thank her for such a huge favor.”","Ji Nan was embarrassed. He covered his mouth and coughed into his hand. “How can my relationship with her be so superficial?”","Xie Yun glared at him fiercely, as if she was saying, “You’re still talking!”","Then, she turned back to Qiao Nian, restrained her smile, and said sincerely, “Nian Nian, I know you don’t like superficial thanks. I also know that the risk you took for Lingfeng this time can’t be repaid with just a word of thanks. I just... couldn’t control my emotions for a moment. Don’t take it to heart. I don’t mean anything else. I just wanted to thank you on his behalf. Thank you for not giving up on him...”","Qiao Nian was indeed not used to handling such a situation. Facing Xie Yun, whose eyes were red, she patted her arm and said, “I’m just doing what a junior should do.”","Xie Yun shook her head with red eyes.","How was this what she should do? So many people in the Ji family did not take the risk to find the antidote. She was the one with an awkward relationship with Lingfeng, but at the critical moment, she was so dependable.","Qiao Nian seemed to know what Xie Yun wanted to say and said before she could speak, “I don’t like to owe favors. Auntie Xie, just treat it as me returning the favor of him going to Continent M to see Nie Qingru for me.”","Before Xie Yun could speak, Qiao Nian’s gaze emptied, and her face became expressionless as she said calmly, “Didn’t he almost lose his life that time? I’m just paying him back!”","Qiao Nian had already said so much. Even if Xie Yun had a stomach full of things to say, she did not know where to start.","Ji Nan, who noticed she still had not raised her right hand, held Xie Yun’s hand and said, “Mom, she probably hasn’t rested all this time. Since Dad’s out of danger, we’ll guard here and let Nian Nian go back to sleep.”"]},{"number":3629,"title":"Chapter 3629: The Gazes of Two Men","paragraphs":["Chapter 3629: The Gazes of Two Men","Xie Yun belatedly saw the red blood vessels in the girl’s eyes and the fatigue under her eyelids. Feeling guilty, she hurriedly said, “Yes, Ji Nan is right. Go back and sleep. I’ll guard here. I’ll contact you if anything happens.”","“Okay.” Qiao Nian did not insist, mainly because she really was tired.","Strictly speaking, she had not slept for almost 24 hours and had relied on her endurance to hold on until now.","Xie Yun pushed Ji Nan . “Send Nian Nian off.”","Ji Nan took his car keys and walked forward. “Let’s go. I’ll send you back. My mother is watching over here. It’s fine for me to go out for a while.”","Qiao Nian lowered her voice and said, “Auntie Xie, help me tell Elder Zhong that I’ll return tomorrow.”","“Okay, don’t worry.” Xie Yun agreed.","Only now did Qiao Nian turn around to leave with one hand in her pocket.","On the way down, Ji Nan asked her about Continent M. Qiao Nian only talked about a few lighthearted things.","At the entrance, Ji Nan said, “Wait for me here. I’ll go get the car.”","A black Phaeton had been waiting outside for a long time. When they came out, it slowly drove forward and blocked their way.","The window of the driver’s seat rolled down, revealing the man’s noble side profile. Ye Wangchuan tilted his head slightly at the two of them before focusing on the girl. “Get in.”","Qiao Nian was stunned. “Why are you here?”","Then, she pulled down her baseball cap and naturally turned around to say to Ji Nan, “There’s no need to send me off. You can go back.”","As she spoke, she walked down the steps and opened the door to get into the car. Then, she fastened her seatbelt, rolled down the window, and waved at Ji Nan. “Go back.”","Ji Nan was still holding his car keys. Seeing that Qiao Nian had gotten into the car with ease and asked him to go back, he took a deep breath and looked at the person inside with a complicated gaze. “Send me a message when you get home.”","He did not have a sister before.","Ji Ziyin had never gotten along with him.","He also could not stand her pretentiousness, so they did not get along.","Ji Nan didn’t know what it was like to have a sister. In any case, at this moment, he did not feel the comfort of an old father. He only felt like someone had driven into his house and taken away their precious treasure.","However, he knew Qiao Nian’s relationship with Ye Wangchuan was much better than his. Even though he was upset, he still lowered his voice and blessed the man in the driver’s seat before the car drove away. “Take good care of her.”","Ye Wangchuan raised his eyebrows and met Ji Nan’s gaze.","Ji Nan did not back down as if he knew something. He looked at Qiao Nian’s right hand meaningfully.","Ye Wangchuan knew he had most likely realized Qiao Nian was injured. He nodded and said arrogantly and lazily, “You don’t have to tell me. I know.”","“It’s good that you know.” Ji Nan let go, indicating that they could leave. He did not want to see his precious being taken away.","Qiao Nian did not notice their exchange of glances. She rolled up the window and leaned against the seat tiredly. “I’ll sleep.”","Ye Wangchuan put a jacket over her and turned up the air conditioner. “Sleep. I’ll drive slower.”","Qiao Nian nodded slightly. Her eyelids were half-closed, and she had already fallen asleep.","...","Three days later.","Good news came from the hospital.","Ji Lingfeng was out of danger and was transferred to a VIP ward for observation. This also meant that the poison that had afflicted him was finally out of his system."]},{"number":3630,"title":"Chapter 3630: Gosh, What Happened These Few Days?","paragraphs":["Chapter 3630: Gosh, What Happened These Few Days?","All that was left for him was to recuperate his body that had been dragged down by the poison all these years.","Qiao Nian was relieved after receiving the news. She knew that with Zhong Yiliu around, Ji Lingfeng would surely recover.","The matter of the antidote had been resolved.","However, many things were waiting for her to deal with.","She had been resting at home for three days, and many people had come looking for her. However, Ye Wangchuan forcefully chased them away and told them to wait two days before coming back.","Many people in the independent continent knew his identity and knew he was not someone to be trifled with. Basically, if he politely invited people to leave, nobody would dare to go against him.","Qiao Nian was also forcefully detained in the villa to recuperate. For the past three days, besides changing her dressing, she was not allowed to move her right hand. She was almost treated as a cripple.","In addition, Gu San was back.","With him around, the food improved a lot.","Qiao Nian was treated as a patient. Gu San made soup for her daily and insisted on the principle of Chinese Medicine.","Qiao Nian drank either tubular bone soup or pig trotter soup every day. In short, she did not drink the same thing every day. It was all nutritious soup.","After three days of soup, her hand had not recovered, but she was about to bleed from her nose.","The nourishment was too intense, and her blood was restless. She was as aggrieved as she could be. However, this time, Gu San and Qin Si were united. They both thought she should take good care of her body.","In the afternoon.","Qiao Nian woke up naturally and put on a long T-shirt. Coming down the stairs, she saw a few familiar people downstairs.","Mo Dong was there too.","He looked up and greeted her warmly. “Miss Qiao, you’re down.”","Gu San saw her coming down and immediately ran to the kitchen. Qiao Nian knew what he was going to do. Her heart tightened and her head hurt.","She walked down slowly. Before Gu San could heat the soup, she said to the people in the living room, “I’m going out for a while.”","Qin Si, Bo Jingxing, and Mo Dong looked at the man sitting on the sofa, waiting for him to speak.","With a dark blue laptop on his lap, Ye Wangchuan looked up at the girl and calmly asked, “Where are you going?”","Qiao Nian remembered promising him she would prioritize her safety. It was rare for her to be patient. “The matter at Mingshui Mansion has been delayed for almost a week. It’s time for me to resolve it.”","Over the past few days, the Second Elder of the Ji family had come knocking on her door quite a few times, wanting to discuss with Qiao Nian how to deal with this matter.","However, they were all stopped outside by Ye Wangchuan and did not see Qiao Nian in person.","Since he could not see her, he had no choice but to go around and get Qiao Nian’s phone number. He called her in the morning.","They arranged to meet in the afternoon.","Qiao Nian was going out for this matter.","She had originally hesitated to explain to him that the matter at Mingshui Mansion could not be dragged on, but who knew that he did not have any intention of making things difficult for her?","“Put on another layer of clothes, and I’ll let you out.”","Silence.","Qiao Nian did not know why she was afraid of him.","However, this time, her arm injury made her unable to calm down. Hence, she did not say anything and nodded slightly. “Alright.”","With that, she turned around and went back up to put on more clothes.","Mo Dong was dumbfounded as he watched this scene. For a moment, he suspected that he was still sleeping. He rubbed his face and asked Qin Si, “What happened in the past few days?”","Why did he feel that his master had stood up?!","Miss Qiao was a little... obedient, as if she had been possessed.","Qin Si gave him a look that said, “What do I know?”","Mo Dong silently turned to look at the noble man on the sofa and coughed dryly."]},{"number":3631,"title":"Chapter 3631: How Are You Planning to Deal With Mingshui Mansion?","paragraphs":["Chapter 3631: How Are You Planning to Deal With Mingshui Mansion?","Before he could say anything, he was greeted with a calm and strong voice. “Did you spit?”","“Gosh, hahahaha!” Qin Si laughed out loud without giving him face.","Mo Dong’s face reddened. He did not dare to gossip with the person involved. He simply looked away and pretended that he did not exist.","After a while, Qiao Nian came down after changing her clothes.","Ye Wangchuan saw that she had only added a thick-knitted cardigan. It was one of the new clothes from B brand that he had gotten someone to place into her closet last time.","The color belonged to the smog blue that young people liked. The style had kept up with the trends, continuing the brand’s style.","It was young and energetic but did not lose the clean and cool feeling brought about by it.","Qiao Nian rarely tried colors other than black, white, and gray. Qin Si and the others were stunned when they saw that she was wearing different colors.","Only Ye Wangchuan looked up. His eyelids twitched slightly as he stood up and picked up the car keys on the table before saying to the girl, “I’ll send you there.”","Qiao Nian nodded and followed him without saying anything.","After the two of them disappeared from the entrance, they heard the sound of a car starting outside.","Qin Si held his forehead and chuckled. “Master Wang is also wearing dark blue today, right? In that case, they look quite like a couple walking together.”","Bo Jingxing pushed up his gold-rimmed glasses and glanced at him. “Boring.”","Then, he added, “They’re already a couple.”","Qin Si had never seen such a nonchalant person. “Yes, they’re all couples. You’re the only one who’s single.”","“I’m better than you. You have a girlfriend, yet you’re still hanging out with a single dog like me.” Bo Jingxing killed him in one strike. He got up and turned in his room’s direction. “I still have a video conference. Have fun.”","Qin Si was so angry that he went crazy. He grabbed a pillow and threw it at him. “Get lost, get lost. Hurry up and crawl back into your room!”","Bo Jingxing seemed to have eyes on his back. He turned around and grabbed the pillow, then threw it on the sofa beside him. He chuckled and walked away.","Only Qin Si and Mo Dong were left in the living room.","Gu San came out with a bowl of steaming bone soup and asked them, “Where’s Miss Qiao? Why is she missing?”","Qin Si put his hand behind his head and glanced at Mo Dong cynically. “Well, don’t you admire Sister Qiao? Why don’t you help your idol drink this bowl of bone soup?”","Mo Dong was speechless.","**","The Second Elder of the Ji family had originally arranged to meet Qiao Nian at the old residence.","Qiao Nian refused.","In the end, they arranged to meet at the café below the Intercontinental Hotel.","When Qiao Nian arrived, the other party had already arrived and had been sitting there for a long time.","Seeing Qiao Nian and Ye Wangchuan coming over, he immediately stood up. He did not go forward to greet them, but at least his attitude was much more respectful than before.","“Miss Qiao.”","He looked to the side and nodded slightly. “Young Master Ye.”","Ye Wangchuan sensibly called the waiter and walked to the next table. “You guys chat. I’ll go sit over there.”","Then, he said to the waiter, “I want an Americano without sugar. Give her a glass of plain water.”","Qiao Nian’s eyelids twitched, but she endured it.","The waiter quickly served two glasses of water.","Qiao Nian only received a glass of plain water. She watched as the waiter served coffee to the next table with a red face.","She couldn’t look away for a long time.","Until the Second Elder of the Ji family spoke. “Miss Qiao, how do you plan to deal with the matter at Mingshui Mansion?”","Qiao Nian did not stand on ceremony with him. She retracted her gaze and asked, “Have you found out?”","Previously, he did not mention the details on the phone. They had only arranged to meet."]},{"number":3632,"title":"Chapter 3632: So You Sold Me Out?","paragraphs":["Chapter 3632: So You Sold Me Out?","The Second Elder of the Ji family did not know why she had such a strong sense of oppression at such a young age. It was so oppressive that he could not breathe. He could only hold the edge of the cup with one hand and say, “I investigated it the day before yesterday. There are many forces involved in this matter. The 9 and 15 that I arranged for you previously were also instigated by someone to take your life when you were unprepared...”","He sighed and looked straight into the girl’s eyes before saying sincerely, “It’s my fault this time. I almost harmed you.”","Qiao Nian did not respond. She took a sip of water to moisten her throat and did not comment on it.","“What are you going to do about it?”","Her relationship with the Second Elder was different from her relationship with Zhong Yiliu and Feng Yu. Even if the other party was older and was an elder, it was impossible for him to receive the treatment of Feng Yu and Zhong Yiliu from her.","Just because he said he was sorry didn’t mean she would forgive him.","There was no such a good thing in this world.","Qiao Nian’s question was direct, causing the Second Elder to be slightly stunned. For a moment, he could not figure out what she was thinking. He hesitated and said slowly, “We’ve all discussed it. The temporary outcome is that too many forces are involved, so it’s not appropriate for us to fuss over every one of them. The best way is to capture one and punish them severely. Kill one to deter the others!”","He paused and looked at Qiao Nian. “Of course, that depends on you. Miss Qiao is the victim of this matter. We respect your thoughts.”","Qiao Nian had saved the Ji family’s face this time. Logically speaking, he had to give her enough face.","Qiao Nian gently knocked on the table with a finger. It was as if she was knocking on Second Elder’s heart. He felt inexplicably uneasy.","He waited restlessly for a long time.","Then, he heard the girl ask him.","“Which force are you going to punish severely?”","“Three Nine Gate.” He told her the answer he had already discussed.","Qiao Nian remained silent. It was as if she was not surprised that he would bring up the question. However, she did not stop tapping on the table, making the Second Elder even more confused about her thoughts.","“Miss Qiao, Number 15 is from Three Nine Gate. We decided to attack them because of this. Before you came out, Three Nine Gate even stopped us from picking you up at Mingshui Mansion. Therefore, overall, it’s reasonable for us to deal with them and it’s the least likely option for us to be criticized about.”","Qiao Nian’s tapping on the table paused for a second. Then, she slowly raised her head and looked at him with her dark eyes before directly asking, “What about the Chamber of Commerce Alliance? How do you plan to deal with them?”","The Second Elder was restless from the questions. As if she had poked at a secret, he avoided eye contact. “President Simon came to me the next day to apologize. Then, everyone discussed some collaborative projects. What the few of us old fellows are saying is... there are many forces involved this time. He’s only one of them. Since his attitude is good and he took the initiative to apologize, why don’t...”","Qiao Nian smiled. She leaned back in her chair and chuckled. Her gaze seemed to see through him, making the Second Elder unable to raise his head. “So you sold me out.”","The Second Elder blushed and frowned nervously. “Miss Qiao, that’s not what we meant.”","Qiao Nian interrupted him. “How much did you sell me out for?”","The Second Elder choked and stopped talking.","Qiao Nian nodded and propped her chin before impolitely saying, “Who gave you the courage to think you can sell me out? Do you think I should still cooperate and agree to your decision?”"]},{"number":3633,"title":"Chapter 3633: Domineering Sister Nian, Do I Need You to Give Me a Result?","paragraphs":["Chapter 3633: Domineering Sister Nian, Do I Need You to Give Me a Result?","The Second Elder really did not know whether to sit or stand. It was even more inappropriate for him to leave. He could only suppress his anger and say to the aggressive Qiao Nian, “We’re also considering the interests of the family.”","Qiao Nian did not even blink. There was not much emotion in her dark eyes as she asked him in a clear and logical manner, “So the interests of the Ji family have something to do with me?”","The Second Elder stuttered, “You...”","Qiao Nian did not give him a chance. She placed her left hand on the back of the chair and bit her lip as she smiled. “Don’t tell me you really think I’m helping you for the Ji family’s benefit?”","The Second Elder’s expression changed slightly. He couldn’t even maintain his basic dignity. Looking at the girl’s rather arrogant face, he lowered his tone. “Miss Qiao, whether you believe me or not, my intentions are for the family’s sake. The Patriarch is still hospitalized. I don’t know when he will recover. The Ji family can’t offend the Chamber of Commerce Alliance... I know this is unfair to you. We’ve also decided on destroying the Three Nine Gate to give you an explanation. This is already the best we can do...”","“Pfft.” Qiao Nian held her chin and looked straight at him. “Do I need you to give an explanation?”","“Qiao Nian!” The Second Elder was enraged.","Every time he spoke, Qiao Nian would slap him mercilessly. Every time she asked him a question, he would be embarrassed.","He was an elder, after all. How could he allow a junior to embarrass him in public?","He stood up expressionlessly and said stiffly, “Since you want to meddle in the Ji family’s matters, it means that you have feelings for the Ji family. We elders have already discussed this matter and will deal with the Three Nine Gate. It doesn’t matter if you agree or not. This is our decision...”","He stood while Qiao Nian sat.","Therefore, she had to raise her head slightly to look at him. Logically speaking, this should have decreased her aura. However, the Second Elder could feel her aura had turned cold. Even the way she looked at him was bone-chilling...","On the other hand, his aura seemed to have been suppressed, and he was half a head shorter.","At this moment, the man quietly drinking coffee at the next table placed his cup on the table and stood up. He was tall and had long legs. His narrow eyes glanced at him as if in greeting. In the blink of an eye, he placed his hand on the girl’s shoulder. “The doctor told you to remain calm.”","Qiao Nian was speechless.","Seeing Ye Wangchuan walking over and talking to Qiao Nian as if no one was around, an indescribable feeling in the Second Elder’s heart caused him to tense up. He glanced at them and said stiffly, “You guys chat. I still have something on. I’ll leave first.”","As he spoke, he took his things and was about to leave.","However, someone refused to let him go.","“Second Elder, why are you in such a hurry? Let’s sit down and talk.”","It was slow and noble as if the clouds above his head suddenly pressed down with a majestic pressure.","The Second Elder stiffened. He took a deep breath and tried to calm down. Then, he slowly turned around to face him. “What do you want to talk about?”","He did not wait for Ye Wangchuan to speak.","“Young Master Ye, let me remind you. No matter your relationship with her, this is the Ji family’s internal matter. It’s not for outsiders to interfere!”","“Pfft.” Ye Wangchuan clicked his tongue and looked at him indifferently. His eyes were clear. “When you asked her for help previously, you didn’t care about outsiders.”","It had to be said.","He knew how to hit a sore spot."]},{"number":3634,"title":"Chapter 3634: My Friend Needs You to Be Fair?","paragraphs":["Chapter 3634: My Friend Needs You to Be Fair?","The Second Elder’s expression, which had finally stabilized, almost froze again. “Young Master Ye, watch your words.”","“Do you think I’m giving you face?” Ye Wangchuan ignored him and said directly, “She participated in the treasure hunt for you, saved your face, almost got injured for you, and risked her life for you...”","The Second Elder frowned. “What are you trying to say?”","Ye Wangchuan lowered his hand and grabbed the girl’s uninjured hand. He forcefully pushed her fingers apart and intertwined them with his.","He held her hand firmly, then raised his head and continued in a slow tone, “You still think that she needs an explanation from you to get a fair result. Haven’t I given you too much face? Otherwise, why would you be so spoiled that you’re lawless and think you’re something? The person in my heart still has to beg you for a fair explanation!”","The Second Elder’s heart trembled for a second. He subconsciously looked at Qiao Nian as if hoping that Qiao Nian would persuade Ye Wangchuan not to do anything stupid.","Qiao Nian’s gaze had been on the man all this time. She only now realized the Second Elder was looking at her.","She was stunned for a second before realizing what the other party was thinking. She couldn’t help but laugh.","She laughed impolitely and unrestrainedly. After a few seconds, she suddenly retracted her smile, licked her lips, and tugged at the corners of her mouth, exuding a devilish charm not to be trifled with. She bluntly said to the Second Elder, who was still hoping for her help, “I’ve never cared about the Ji family’s life and death. Your interests have nothing to do with me! I only care about one or two people, but if you think you can rely on this to restrain me, that’s too laughable.","“I’ll make it clear to them. It’s best if they can understand. If they can’t, that only means they’re not worth my care.”","Qiao Nian said firmly, “I’m definitely going after the Chamber of Commerce Alliance!”","She turned to the Second Elder again, her eyes revealing a bone-chilling coldness. “As for you guys... you let me understand one thing.”","Silence.","The Second Elder looked at the thin lips opening and closing arrogantly. “... A dog that never has enough to eat should be woken up with a big stick.”","The Second Elder’s face turned ashen and red from Qiao Nian’s scolding. He pinched his palm and could not recover for a long time, but he did not dare to talk back.","Before coming, he had sworn that he could deal with Qiao Nian and persuade her not to pursue the matter.","But now, Qiao Nian’s reaction undoubtedly gave him a loud slap, telling him it was useless to use moral kidnapping to restrain her.","Just as she said, she did not care about the Ji family’s life or death.","However, she had been risking her life for the Ji family these past few days. She took many risks and even cut ties with the First Research Institute... Why did she not care about the family’s interests now?","The Second Elder complained incessantly in his heart. At this point, he had no choice but to regret it. He could only meet the girl’s gaze and remind her hesitantly, “Qiao Nian, you still have the blood of the old patriarch in you.”","It meant that she was still a member of the Ji family.","“Oh,” the girl replied. Her expression was casual and serious. “Then tell him to get up from the grave and perform blood-letting on me. If he asks me for it himself, I’ll return it to him.”","Ye Wangchuan glanced at her. The corners of his lips curled up as he pinched their clasped hands."]},{"number":3635,"title":"Chapter 3635: Sister Nian Is Going to Deal With the Chamber of Commerce Alliance","paragraphs":["Chapter 3635: Sister Nian Is Going to Deal With the Chamber of Commerce Alliance","Qiao Nian felt someone pinch her fingers and glanced at him. She didn’t say anything and just looked at the Second Elder again. As if tired, she said casually, “I’m not satisfied with your results. Go back and discuss with the others again. I’m not a patient person. Since you guys are so good at calculating benefits, you should be able to calculate which is more disadvantageous to you—offending me or Simon from the Chamber of Commerce Alliance.”","“You...” The Second Elder was not stupid. How could he not hear the threat in her words?","Qiao Nian was blatantly telling them that Simon might target the Ji family. If they offended her, she could also deal with them!","The Second Elder’s expression was ugly. His facial muscles were tense as he gritted his teeth. He was so angry that his mind was in a daze, but he had to face Qiao Nian’s choices...","She gave the Ji family two choices, but, in fact, there was only one answer.","The Second Elder did not want to admit it, but he had to. The Ji family was already in Qiao Nian’s hands, and their fate was in her hands. If they wanted to live well, they had to do things according to her wishes!","“I’ll think about it.” The Second Elder pulled a long face and waved his hand angrily. “I can leave now, right?”","These words were directed at Qiao Nian and Ye Wangchuan.","Ye Wangchuan looked up and made a noble and lazy gesture. “The door is over there.”","Silence.","The Second Elder’s face heated up again as he fled.","Ye Wangchuan waited for him to leave before letting go of the girl’s hand and sitting opposite her. He observed her expression. “You’re not angry?”","Qiao Nian raised her eyebrows at him. She sighed and said slowly, “At first, I was quite angry. Later, when you came over, I thought about it and felt there was no need.”","She looked at Ye Wangchuan seriously and said clearly, “My original goal was not to help the Ji family. Since I didn’t include these people in my scope from the beginning, they didn’t really let me down.”","“But they did let you down.” Ye Wangchuan’s tone was cold.","Seeing that he seemed to be angrier than her, Qiao Nian smiled, and the frustration in her heart disappeared. She said in relief, “That’s why I won’t give them a chance to do that to me again. Aren’t I giving them a final choice? They’re smart people and know what to choose.”","The elders of the Ji family were similar to Nie Qingru. With their own interests in danger, they were shrewd and would not make the second choice.","They would only choose themselves.","Even if they went back on their word, they would always be loyal to their interests!","The corners of Qiao Nian’s mouth twitched. She picked up the glass on the table and rubbed her fingers against it before taking a sip of water.","“I’ve given him many chances. If he doesn’t want it, then forget it.”","Ye Wangchuan knew who she was talking about and did not say anything.","Simon from the Chamber of Commerce Alliance... should be dealt with.","**","Things were indeed as Qiao Nian had expected.","After parting on bad terms yesterday, the Second Elder quickly called the other elders to the Righteousness Hall to discuss this matter.","Qiao Nian said she was giving them a choice, but in fact, she wanted them to choose an ally between her and Simon.","If this choice had been made in the past, these arrogant elders would still consider Simon. After all, Simon did not represent personal power, but the entire Chamber of Commerce Alliance.","But who in the entire independent continent would dare to look down on Qiao Nian now? Would they think she was nothing to be afraid of and would easily offend her?"]},{"number":3636,"title":"Chapter 3636: Only Received News Now","paragraphs":["Chapter 3636: Only Received News Now","Therefore, there was only one choice.","Initially, someone else did not give up and suggested talking to Qiao Nian again to persuade her to see the big picture.","Some people looked for Xie Yun and Ji Nan and mentioned this matter, hoping that they could come forward and talk to Qiao Nian. In the end, all of them were rejected.","Xie Yun and Ji Nan were still alright. At least, they had picked up their calls when they did not know at first.","Qiao Nian was much more impolite.","No one in the Ji family could contact her.","After that, they changed to an unknown number. Qiao Nian even replied with a message, telling them that if they called her again, they wouldn’t have to choose!","Although the elders of the Ji family were almost angered to death by her rebelliousness, they did not dare to call her anymore.","The night’s discussion resulted in the Second Elder contacting Simon from the Chamber of Commerce Alliance the next day and postponing the previous agreement.","This was undoubtedly forcing them to spit out the fat meat that was almost in their mouths. They had to spit it out willingly and firmly.","The Second Elder’s phone call was extremely aggrieved.","However, no matter how aggrieved, he had to follow Qiao Nian’s instructions and finish this call. He also had to express the Ji family’s attitude.","“...So President Simon, forget about the cooperation we discussed previously. Coincidentally, we didn’t have time to sign the contract, so it’s not troublesome.”","It was early in the morning. Upon hearing what the Second Elder said, Simon rubbed his brows and walked to the French window before asking in a serious tone, “So what do you mean? The Ji family is not cooperating with me. Are you saying... that you want to fall out with me?”","“President Simon, you know very well what you’ve done. Even if we want to fall out with you, there’s a reason! We’re all smart people. There’s no need to say it out loud. It won’t look good on either of us.”","The Second Elder knew that family scandals should not be aired in public. He couldn’t tell him that he had been forced into this choice by Qiao Nian. Thus, his tone was extremely cold.","“We agreed to the cooperation before we investigated it. Now that we’ve investigated it, we found it’s inconvenient for us to cooperate.”","“Heh.” Simon chuckled. It would be strange if he believed his nonsense. “Emperor Ji is still in the hospital and his fate is unknown. It’s not good for the Ji family to fall out with the Chamber of Commerce Alliance at this moment, right? Why don’t you reconsider it?”","The Second Elder felt stifled. He gave a fake smile and said, “There’s nothing to consider. This is our attitude.”","He did not want to continue talking to him. “President Simon, I’ve already expressed my attitude. I’ll hang up first.”","The other party hung up before Simon could say anything.","Simon pressed the tip of his tongue against his cheek. For a moment, he was so angry that he laughed. His blue eyes stared at the cell phone in disbelief.","After a few seconds, his expression turned cold. A violent feeling of things going out of control rushed up his head, and he uncontrollably smashed his phone into pieces.","Simon placed his hand on the floor-to-ceiling window, his chest heaving violently. He couldn’t control his emotions, but his throbbing temples reminded him that he did not have much time to digest them.","He forced himself to walk behind the desk, pick up the office line, and call in his assistant. “Come in and clean the office.”","He put the receiver back down and sat in the leather swivel chair. His handsome and mature face revealed a bewildered expression. He was thinking about why the sly old foxes of the Ji family had suddenly gone back on their word, and also about how much Qiao Nian had found out about him...","In the end, he thought about one thing—how Qiao Nian planned to deal with him!","Simon’s heart turned cold when he thought of the person he had provoked. He couldn’t understand why he had been so obsessed with dividing the Ji family and going after the Tsar’s blueprint back then."]},{"number":3637,"title":"Chapter 3637: President, an Asian Girl is Looking for You Downstairs","paragraphs":["Chapter 3637: President, an Asian Girl is Looking for You Downstairs","As Simon was feeling uneasy from the phone call...","Qiao Nian had just woken up and come down from the second floor.","Gu San greeted her and placed breakfast on the dining table for her.","Qiao Nian walked over, pulled out a chair, and sat down. Then, she casually grabbed a toast and bit into it. Her half-closed eyelids revealed she was still a little sleepy as she supported her chin with one hand and worked on the toast.","“Milk.”","Ye Wangchuan came over and placed the milk by her hand.","Qiao Nian looked at the steaming milk and yawned, then tilted her head and looked at him with her dark eyes. “What time did you sleep last night?”","Ye Wangchuan sat down beside her. “One in the morning.”","“Oh,” Qiao Nian replied.","No wonder she had received a semiconductor mutation equation solution from him at almost one in the morning.","In the living room, Qin Si asked her to play a game.","Qiao Nian had worked on the last equation left in Ji Qing’s USB drive until midnight last night. Her mind was still foggy. How could she be in the mood to play games with him?","“Play by yourself.” She rejected him mercilessly and ignored Qin Si’s howl as she slowly finished her toast and drank the milk. Rubbing her temples, she leaned back in her chair, thinking about whether to go to the research institute.","Yesterday she thought of a solution to the problem and wanted to study it with Feng Yu...","At this moment.","Ye Wangchuan suddenly asked, “What do you plan to do with Simon?”","Qiao Nian’s mind stilled for a moment. She placed her arm on the back of the chair and sat casually. Her slightly raised eyes were unrestrained. “Him?”","“Yes.” Ye Wangchuan did not stand on ceremony with her. “Do you want Mo Dong to deal with it?”","Qiao Nian understood what he meant. He meant that she did not have to do anything and he would deal with the Chamber of Commerce Alliance on her behalf.","However, she wanted to handle this matter herself this time.","“No need, I’ll do it myself.” Qiao Nian said calmly, “The Ji family should have spoken to him. There’s no hurry for now. I’ll leave him hanging for two days... I’ll look for him after I’m done with my work.”","...","Qiao Nian was really not in a hurry.","For the next two days, Simon waited uneasily for Qiao Nian to come after him. However, neither Bright Gate nor the First Research Institute were quiet and did not find trouble with him.","It seemed like a joke for him to be on full alert.","Moreover, he did not rest well for these two days. Not only did he fail to resolve the predicament in front of him, but he also exhausted himself.","On the third day, when his exhaustion was at its peak and he had already begun to let down his guard...","His assistant knocked on the office door.","Knock knock.","“President.” The assistant’s voice came from the door.","Simon stared at the computer but was not paying attention to the screen. He looked away absent-mindedly and said with a wooden face, “Come in.”","The assistant opened the door and walked to the desk before softly saying, “President, there’s a Miss Qiao outside wanting to see you. Because she doesn’t have an appointment, the front desk didn’t dare to let her up, but she insists on seeing you. So, the front desk asked me if you want to let her up...”","Before he could finish his sentence, the assistant saw Simon’s expression change drastically. He placed his hands on the table and almost stood up. His expression changed twice as he asked with a complicated expression, “What does she look like?!”","“Uh...” The assistant was stunned by the question.","Simon’s eyes were fixed on him. “Go and ask.”","The assistant quickly walked to the side and called the front desk to ask about the situation. After a while, he walked back and carefully said, “The front desk said she’s a young Asian girl. She’s wearing a baseball cap, so they can’t see her face clearly, but she should be good-looking.”"]},{"number":3638,"title":"Chapter 3638: Sister Nian Comes Knocking","paragraphs":["Chapter 3638: Sister Nian Comes Knocking","An Asian girl wearing a baseball cap; good-looking.","Simon matched all the information and could almost confirm who was looking for him downstairs.","His heart trembled.","Qiao Nian had come knocking!","He sat back in the swivel chair, almost speechless. He lowered his eyes in a daze and did not say a word.","The assistant looked at him and did not know what to do. He only dared to ask carefully, “President, do you want to see her?”","In his semi-conscious state, Simon heard his assistant’s question and pursed his lips mockingly. He only answered after a while. “... she already came looking for me. It’s not up to me to say no.”","The assistant did not understand what he meant and stood rooted to the ground, not daring to move.","Simon took a deep breath to compose himself and looked up at him. “Let her come up!”","Upon receiving the order, the assistant heaved a sigh of relief and said happily, “Okay.”","Then, he turned around and left the office.","Simon was originally powerless against the back of the chair and deeply anxious about what to do next. However, he immediately stood up to chase after the assistant.","How could he have forgotten?","In this situation, it was better for him to go down and pick her up personally.","However, before he could leave the office, he saw the girl walking out of the elevator in the corridor. She looked over and met his eyes.","Simon suddenly froze in place.","Before he could react, the girl walked towards him as if nothing had happened, one step at a time.","Every step was like a drumbeat pounding his heart, causing it to tremble nonstop.","However, he did not have much time to react.","Qiao Nian was in front of him in the blink of an eye. She raised her head slightly, revealing her young and flamboyant face under the baseball cap. She narrowed her black eyes and curled her lips, then casually greeted him, “President Simon, long time no see~”","Her tone was so casual.","However, Simon’s heart trembled. He could hear the decisiveness in it.","He looked at the assistant craning his neck to look over and pursed his lips. Then, he stepped aside to let the girl enter the office. “Miss Qiao, please come in.”","“Sure.”","Qiao Nian did not stand on ceremony with him and walked in.","Simon took a deep breath and followed.","* * *","His office was located on the top floor of a landmark building in the most prosperous part of the independent continent. The 270° circular glass design allowed him to look at all the streets and buildings around him.","This feeling of looking down on everyone was in line with Simon’s identity, and he liked it very much.","However, at this moment, he was not in the mood to enjoy the superior feeling.","Simon personally made a cup of coffee and brought it to the floor-to-ceiling window. He stared at the girl standing by the window looking at the scenery below and took a deep breath before handing her coffee. Then, he politely asked, “Miss Qiao, here’s a cup of coffee. Can you do mocha with no sugar?”","Qiao Nian tilted her head at him. Instead of taking the coffee cup, she bluntly said, “President Simon, do you know why I’m here today?”","Simon held up the coffee for a long time, but the other party had no intention of taking it. Although embarrassed, he could only take it back and say sincerely, “Miss Qiao, there’s a misunderstanding!","“It would be too insincere of me to say that I don’t know why you came looking for me, but there is indeed a misunderstanding.”","Simon said everything he had thought of in the past two days as if afraid that Qiao Nian would interrupt him.","“I admit that the people in Continent M contacted me and told me about the Tsar’s blueprint and the benefits of dividing the Ji family. They wanted me to ‘inconvenience’ you.”"]},{"number":3639,"title":"Chapter 3639: What’s In It For Me?","paragraphs":["Chapter 3639: What’s In It For Me?","He looked into Qiao Nian’s eyes seriously and continued, “I was indeed tempted and did so. But Miss Qiao, you should know very well that it wasn’t just our Chamber of Commerce Alliance that did it, but more than half of the forces in the independent continent. You can’t just pin it onto us! This is unfair...”","Simon sounded very sincere.","In fact, he had thought of completely denying the matter of Mingshui Mansion. But he rejected it as soon as this idea popped up in his mind.","Simon knew very well Qiao Nian was a smart person.","If he completely denied the Chamber of Commerce Alliance’s involvement in the Mingshui Mansion affair, Qiao Nian might not give him any face and would not have believed it.","He might as well tell a half-truth.","On one hand, he admitted his participation. On the other hand, he dragged everyone down with him...","“Miss Qiao, we’re willing to pay for our actions and make concessions and compensation on some projects. Compared to other forces, I think I have a good attitude. Why are you holding onto me for accountability?” he asked in confusion.","If it were anyone else, they might have been led astray by his series of actions. Unfortunately, he did not know Qiao Nian well. She never did anything she was not confident in.","Since she had come, she wouldn’t wrongly accuse him.","“You mean I went overboard?” The girl listened quietly before asking with a faint smile.","Simon’s expression turned cold. He knew when to stop. “Miss Qiao, I respect you very much. I definitely don’t mean that. I just don’t understand why you came looking for me today.”","Qiao Nian took a lighter from somewhere and played with it with lowered eyes, making it impossible for Simon to discern her emotions. “You said the Chamber of Commerce Alliance has only done what others have done. Then who released the news that I have the Tsar’s blueprint?”","Simon’s heart skipped a beat. He opened his mouth but could not say anything.","He couldn’t figure out how much Qiao Nian knew!","At this moment, the girl looked up and met his gaze. “I heard that before the incident at Mingshui Mansion, a faction contacted the other factions and proposed to kill me. You didn’t know either?”","“I...”","Simon averted his gaze, his heart already in a mess.","His sixth sense told him that Qiao Nian knew everything.","Under such circumstances, if he denied it again, he would lose the chance to confess and ask for mercy.","He had a vague feeling that Qiao Nian had something else on her mind besides settling scores with him...","He might still have a chance of survival.","Simon understood this and calmed down. Then, he looked at the girl and said elegantly, “Miss Qiao, you didn’t come just to say this, right? Just say what you have in mind.”","Swoosh.","The girl put away the lighter and looked at him in admiration, then directly said, “Then I’ll be straightforward. Who from Continent M contacted you? What did he tell you back then?”","Simon heaved a sigh of relief upon having guessed correctly.","He did not answer immediately. Instead, he looked at the girl seriously and asked, “What’s in it for me if I tell you, Miss Qiao?”","Qiao Nian raised her eyebrows but was not angry. “What benefits do you want?”","Simon did not stand on ceremony. “Of course, I want Miss Qiao to stop pursuing this matter!”","“Tsk.” Qiao Nian chuckled. She did not say yes or no. She just told him decisively, “What you’re giving me isn’t worth me dropping the matter.”","Simon’s expression was a little ugly, but he did not refute her.","Of course, he knew his request was too big, but he had no choice. He could only seize the opportunity to fight for a chance of survival."]},{"number":3640,"title":"Chapter 3640: A Mysterious Young Man","paragraphs":["Chapter 3640: A Mysterious Young Man","“Then what can you give me?” Simon was a smart person. He knew well that it was not beneficial for him to continue the stalemate, so he took a step back.","Qiao Nian raised her baseball cap with her left hand and turned around lazily. She looked away from the scenery outside the window and strode in. “I can promise you. As long as you step down from your position as the President, I can agree not to implicate the Chamber of Commerce Alliance.”","Silence.","Simon almost laughed in anger.","He stopped in his tracks and clenched his fists. His face was ashen as he replied, “This condition doesn’t seem beneficial to me. Why should I care about the Chamber of Commerce Alliance’s interests if I’m no longer the president?”","Qiao Nian turned around and met his burning gaze without saying anything. After a few seconds, she said indifferently, “This is something you should consider, not something I should consider. I’m not forcing you to accept it. You can choose not to reveal it. At most, I’ll investigate it myself.”","Simon stood rooted to the ground, his mind buzzing. His expression changed. “Miss Qiao, at least let me see some benefits... Your condition is too harsh.”","Qiao Nian sat on the sofa and smiled inexplicably. Then, she licked the corner of her lips and said impatiently, “You wanted my life, do I have to give you a good deal?”","Simon’s expression changed again.","Qiao Nian did not give him a chance to continue bargaining. She waved her hand and said, “I’ll repeat. You can disagree.”","Simon thought about it for more than half an hour.","Qiao Nian sat on the sofa with crossed legs and played with her phone.","She did not rush him.","Half an hour later.","Simon closed his eyes tightly and opened them again as if he had accepted his fate. A tired expression appeared on his face. “I agree to your conditions.”","Then, he woodenly said, “I hope you’ll keep your word and only make things difficult for me. In the future, you won’t make things difficult for the entire Chamber of Commerce Alliance because of this!”","The girl put away her cell phone and casually nodded.","Simon knew Qiao Nian well. Since she had promised, she would not go back on her word no matter how perfunctory she looked.","The weight on his heart was lifted. He said blankly, “A young man looked for me.”","Qiao Nian looked at them.","...A young man?","She knew very well that Shadow did not look young anymore. At least, no one would use the words “young man” to describe him.","The person who came was not Shadow?","Who was that?","She did not continue. Instead, she listened to Simon.","Simon sized her up and continued, “That person looks three or four years older than you, definitely not more than 30. He’s low-key and smart. He came directly to me for negotiation. He said he could help the Chamber of Commerce Alliance obtain the greatest benefits when dividing up the Ji family... I didn’t believe him at first, but then he took out Emperor Ji’s medical record. I only knew that Emperor Ji had been poisoned and wouldn’t live for long after looking at the medical record. Hence, I was tempted and reached an agreement with him.”","Everyone in the independent continent was asking about it.","However, none of the factions, including him, had obtained exact information about Ji Lingfeng’s condition.","That person showed him Ji Lingfeng’s medical report, which convinced him of the other party’s ability. Coupled with this god-given opportunity, the other party also offered tempting conditions.","He was a businessman. It was hard not to be tempted.","“After the incident, I tried to contact him, but he seemed to have disappeared from the independent continent. I don’t even know when he left the country.”"]},{"number":3641,"title":"Chapter 3641: What We Want to Protect Is More Important Than Our Lives","paragraphs":["Chapter 3641: What We Want to Protect Is More Important Than Our Lives","Simon looked at the girl, his blue eyes flashing behind his gold-framed glasses.","He adjusted his glasses before saying, “Miss Qiao, forgive me for being blunt. That person seems to have a grudge against you. And it’s no small grudge. He came after you from the beginning!”","“Oh?” Qiao Nian narrowed her eyes and scrutinized his expression as if trying to determine whether he was lying.","Simon straightened his back and allowed her to look. His heart was calm, and his gaze did not waver. “At this point, there’s no need for me to lie to you.","“That person gave me the feeling that he came for you. To put it bluntly, even if he didn’t have the Empress’ backing, he’d most likely have found trouble with you.”","He paused before continuing, “As for why he’s looking for trouble with you... I don’t know... Only Miss Qiao can think about how you’ve offended this person.”","Qiao Nian put down her legs and said casually, “I’ve offended many people. I don’t know which one you’re talking about.”","Simon glanced at her and said in a rare serious tone, “This person is dangerous. I advise Miss Qiao to investigate thoroughly.”","Qiao Nian tilted her head. “Are you using me?”","“Yes.”","Simon did not hide his motive. “If he hadn’t come looking for me for cooperation, I wouldn’t have ended up like this. After the incident, he ran away and left me to take the blame alone. If you were me, you wouldn’t have let him off either! But...”","His tone changed and his gaze met Qiao Nian’s again. “While I thought of using you to take revenge on him, I’m sincere. This person is dangerous and seems to have a deep hatred for you. Miss Qiao is a smart person. You won’t be at ease leaving such a person alone, right?”","Qiao Nian stood up and dusted her clothes without giving a clear answer. Then, she said, “... Let’s talk about it later. One or two more enemies won’t make a difference to me!”","Simon’s expression changed when the girl got up, picked up her things, and turned to leave. Just before Qiao Nian walked out the door, he clenched his fists and called out hoarsely, “Miss Qiao.”","Qiao Nian stopped in her tracks holding the door handle. She did not turn around. “Speak.”","“How do you know I’m willing to agree to your conditions?” Simon revealed his doubt.","He had been guessing how Qiao Nian planned to deal with him for the past two days.","He had thought of many possibilities.","For example, kidnaping him or threatening him with a gun to his head...","However, he did not expect such a calm conversation.","And yet, he had said everything.","Simon’s throat was dry. “How did you know I’d tell you... What if I didn’t?”","Qiao Nian did not understand why he was asking this. She turned around and saw the pain and loneliness on the man’s face.","She seemed to understand what Simon was asking. She pursed her lips and softened her tone. “Because everyone has something they want to protect. Something more important than their lives.”","Silence.","“I have something to protect, and so do you.”","What Simon wanted to protect was not his reputation and benefits, but the Chamber of Commerce Alliance that he built from the ground up. Qiao Nian had seen through this point and had never thought of using violence to solve this problem.","A sly old fox like Simon might not be willing to tell her the truth even if she threatened him with his life.","Only by using what he cared about as a condition would he tell her the truth.","Qiao Nian did not wait for his reaction. She turned around and left.","Simon was left standing in the office in a daze, watching her walk away. The corners of his mouth suddenly twitched as he shook his head and smiled. “I’m really old. I was actually seen through by a little girl in her early twenties...”"]},{"number":3642,"title":"Chapter 3642: Sister Nian Has a Way to Investigate People","paragraphs":["Chapter 3642: Sister Nian Has a Way to Investigate People","Old, old.","It was time to give up the seat to the young people.","Simon walked back to his desk. Then, he took a deep breath and picked up the office line to inform the board of directors he was holding an emergency meeting.","* * *","Qiao Nian did not walk far from the Chamber of Commerce Alliance building before entering a shop and ordering a glass of water.","Half an hour later.","Not far away, the roar of a sports car’s accelerator sounded from the roadside.","Guan Yan got out of a flashy red Ferrari convertible and walked towards Qiao Nian in her high heels.","Wearing a tight leather dress that outlined her curvaceous figure, her chestnut-colored wavy hair was even more charming and eye-catching, attracting the attention of many people of the opposite sex.","Qiao Nian was leaning against the back of the chair and taking a small sip of water. Looking up and seeing the flamboyant peacock, her saliva almost got stuck in her throat. Fortunately, she reacted quickly and swallowed it expressionlessly. Then, she silently placed the glass on the table and covered her face with her cell phone...","“Boss, I missed you so much!”","Guan Yan didn’t care how many gazes she attracted as she enthusiastically hugged the girl.","Then, she walked to the opposite side and pulled out a chair to sit down. After asking the waiter for a cup of iced black tea and placing her wallet on the table, she flipped her hair and asked the girl, “Who do you want me to investigate?”","Qiao Nian had almost been crushed by her chest just now. She finally regained her senses and rubbed her throbbing temples. Then, she said hoarsely, “A man from Continent M.”","What?","The waiter had just brought the drink over.","Guan Yan winked at the shy waiter, making him run away with a flushed face.","Only then did she turn around and look at Qiao Nian in confusion. “What is it?”","The back of Qiao Nian’s head seemed to be hit again and again by a wooden clapper. She frowned and pressed down the brim of her cap, revealing only her sharp jawline. “Help me investigate the people from Continent M who appeared in the independent continent within this month. I want a name list.”","Guan Yan took a sip of black tea and spat out the straw. “I’m afraid this isn’t a small number. I can get the entry list, but how are you going to find the person you’re looking for?”","At least 800 people entered and left the independent continent monthly.","The chances of Sun finding anyone suspicious from such a long list were too small.","Qiao Nian’s red lips curled up as she leaned back and smiled. She was quite arrogant, and she had the right to be so. “Who told you I’ll take my time?”","What?","“There’s a simple way to find this person.”","Simple? Guan Yan suspected there was something wrong with her ears.","How could it be easy to find one person among 800 people?","Qiao Nian looked into her eyes and said, “I just need to investigate their trajectory and see who has frequently appeared near the Chamber of Commerce Alliance and Simon’s residence recently.”","Guan Yan was stunned. She realized that Qiao Nian’s method was very feasible!","Qiao Nian’s right hand was still injured. She rubbed the edge of the cup on the table with her left and continued casually, “This is the independent continent, after all. That person can change the entry record, but he can’t change his trajectory. As long as we check the surveillance cameras at various intersections, we can definitely find him.”","Guan Yan held back the shock and muttered, “Sun, this method is not simple. It can only be done by you. If it were someone else... this method would basically be useless.”"]},{"number":3643,"title":"Chapter 3643: Sun, What Deep Grudge Does This Person Have With You?","paragraphs":["Chapter 3643: Sun, What Deep Grudge Does This Person Have With You?","Using the other party’s immigration photo to check the surveillance cameras...","Only Qiao Nian could use this method.","This was because there was no system in the independent continent that she could not hack into.","“If that person changes the immigration photo...” Guan Yan took a sip of water and suddenly remembered.","Qiao Nian had long thought of this. She smiled and said with a sharp gaze, “It’s simple. As long as the photo of someone on that list doesn’t have any trajectory in the road surveillance cameras, it can also prove which fake identity card he used. Then, I can pull up this fake identity’s immigration photo... If he even dealt with it, it would be even simpler. I’ll get Simon to check all his information and assets overseas. As long as he has appeared in the independent continent, he can’t have disappeared without a trace...”","Guan Yan couldn’t close her mouth. After a long time, she gave her a thumbs up and sighed with emotion. “Fortunately, Sun, you didn’t investigate me. Otherwise, you would have found out what color I am wearing today!”","Qiao Nian’s eyelids twitched as she glanced at her leisurely.","Guan Yan immediately shut up and got down to business. “Even Simon said this person has a grudge against you. Boss, how did you provoke him? Hiss, could it be that you abandoned him?”","“Don’t utter nonsense,” Qiao Nian reminded her impatiently.","Guan Yan was just joking. “Haha, I’m just saying. If you really abandoned him, he won’t take your life, but you’ll have to take responsibility.”","She placed her hands on the table and admired the girl’s attractive face. She clicked her tongue and praised, “Young Master Ye is really lucky.”","Qiao Nian felt her scalp tingle. She looked away and leaned back. Then, she crossed her arms and said, “Let’s get down to business. I really didn’t know I had such an enemy.”","“Isn’t it the Empress’s man?” Guan Yan frowned.","Qiao Nian shook her head. “I think Simon means this person has a personal feud with me.”","“We’ve offended many people, but be it in the illegal district or Continent F, there aren’t many people who have gone through so much trouble to do such a thing. Some of them have been obediently staying in their territory recently. Besides, even if they did it, no matter how sinister the people from the illegal district and Continent F are, they won’t dare to admit it... To be honest, the Mingshui Mansion’s method was too shady. No one in the illegal district or Continent F can do it!” Guan Yan fell silent after saying her piece. She was no longer in the mood to joke.","Qiao Nian was worried about such a cunning and scheming person remaining in the dark.","With this thought in mind, Guan Yan said, “I don’t have much on my hands these days. I’ll stay here until you’re done with your matters.”","Qiao Nian raised an eyebrow.","Guan Yan shrugged her shoulders with a relaxed expression, not giving Qiao Nian a chance to refuse. “Boss, don’t refuse. My boyfriend is still here. At least we’re in a relationship. I should pamper him. Wouldn’t I be too miserable if he dumps me later?”","“He’ll dump you?” Qiao Nian did not believe a word of it. She knew why Guan Yan was staying, but she did not expose her good intentions.","Guan Yan smiled as she joked. “Why not? With Young Master Qin’s looks, figure, and family background, many socialites are chasing him from the streets of Chang’an to Beijing. In the past year, his family has frequently urged him to get married. Who knows when he will have a fiancée? I don’t know how long I can be his girlfriend. I might even be dumped tomorrow.”"]},{"number":3644,"title":"Chapter 3644: She Won’t Be a Woman Who Depends on Men","paragraphs":["Chapter 3644: She Won’t Be a Woman Who Depends on Men","Qiao Nian looked at her quietly for a second. “What... are you thinking?”","“What do you mean?” After Guan Yan finished speaking, she looked at Qiao Nian’s expression and couldn’t help but restrain her cynical expression. The corners of her mouth twitched, and she smiled indifferently. “I don’t think much of it. Some people are born with wings. Me, for example! I can’t settle down. If he wants me to return to Beijing with him to get married, not to mention anything else, his family won’t allow it. The Qin family’s background is clean. It’s difficult for them to take someone like me. I’m also unwilling to give up the career I’ve worked for so many years just for a man.”","Hence, she thought of it simply.","If Qin Si liked her enough, they would be together.","They would separate when Qin Si got a fiancée in the future.","She couldn’t give up the Red Alliance and her business for Qin Si and let herself become a woman who could only rely on men.","No matter how intoxicating love was!","Therefore, they would take it one step at a time. They would go wherever they went.","“Fortunately, I’ve been rational since a young age.” Guan Yan raised her head, her eyes wandering. “I knew from the beginning that I wouldn’t be able to last long with him. Therefore, I’ve reminded myself not to fall for him. My feelings for him now are only so-so. I admit I’m not tired of him, but I might get tired of him one day...”","She might not be a scumbag, but she might not want to commit to giving a man a home.","In any case, Qin Si probably had the same mentality as her.","She had investigated him. Qin Si was a playboy. He was different from Young Master Ye. When the time came, they would be much more at peace if they split up.","Qiao Nian never interfered in other people’s relationships. Guan Yan didn’t care, so she couldn’t say anything. Thus, she changed the topic. “Did you bring your computer?”","Guan Yan was adept at controlling her emotions. She immediately stood up. “It’s in the car. I’ll get it for you.”","Qiao Nian nodded. After watching her leave, she picked up her phone, found Qin Si’s WeChat, and sent him her location.","The other end replied instantly.","[Qin Si: ?]","[Qin Si: Sister Qiao, why did you send me this?]","[Qin Si: You’re done?]","[Qin Si: I’ll get Master Wang to pick you up.]","Qiao Nian looked at his series of messages and thought for a moment.","She gave him another chance.","[QN: Guan Yan is with me.]","The message was sent successfully.","The other end was silent for a full three seconds, then he sent three consecutive messages.","[Qin Si: I’ll be right there.]","[Qin Si: Don’t let her go.]","[Qin Si: Sister Qiao, please. You must keep her there until I arrive!]","**","In the villa.","Ye Wangchuan watched as Qin Si threw down the game controller and hurriedly changed his clothes before leaving. He couldn’t help but ask him, “Where are you going in such a hurry?”","Qin Si pressed a hand between his eyebrows and tried to calm down. “Sister Qiao just sent me a message saying Guan Yan is with her. I’m going to meet them.”","A few days ago, his mother urged him to get married, and he confessed to his family that he had a girlfriend.","Who knew how his mother contacted Guan Yan?","After asking Guan Yan about herself, his mother told her he had a fiancée and was getting engaged soon. His family had already chosen a few suitable marriage partners for him.","He wouldn’t have known about it if his mother had not told him about it the night before.","Guan Yan did not even tell him this. How could he not be anxious?","Now that Guan Yan was in the independent continent, he wanted to explain it to her.","However, he asked Guan Yan out a few times but she did not meet him. It wasn’t easy for him to hear from her, so Qin Si naturally had to rush over.","He hurriedly took his car keys. “Master Wang, I’m leaving.”"]},{"number":3645,"title":"Chapter 3645: Sun, I Bet He Will Want Your Contact Number","paragraphs":["Chapter 3645: Sun, I Bet He Will Want Your Contact Number","“Wait.”","Ye Wangchuan stopped him and walked over with the scarf.","“I’ll go with you.”","Qin Si frowned, unwilling to bring him along. He muttered, “What are you going to do? It’s not easy for me to meet my girlfriend, and you’re still going along to be a third wheel.”","He spoke softly.","However, there were only the two of them present.","Ye Wangchuan wasn’t deaf.","He glanced at him. “I’m going to pick up my girlfriend. Can’t I?”","Qin Si pursed his lips and walked in front.","Ye Wangchuan followed behind. His stunning face raised an eyebrow as he added unhurriedly, “Or do you want her to stay there and be your third wheel...”","Another third wheel?","Qin Si reacted.","Gosh, that made sense!","With Sister Qiao there, Guan Yan wouldn’t even look at him.","He rolled his eyes, and his unhappy face disappeared. He immediately made an inviting gesture and gave way, smiling and saying, “Hehe, Master Wang, you can leave first!”","**","Qin Si stepped on the accelerator and finally arrived at the location Qiao Nian sent him 20 minutes later.","He parked by the roadside, exited the car, and went straight to the coffee shop.","In the coffee shop.","Guan Yan had almost finished her coffee and was watching the girl use the computer in boredom.","“Sun, you haven’t found out?”","“Face analysis in progress.”","Qiao Nian did not even look up.","The baseball cap covered most of her face, revealing only a good-looking outline. Her figure was broad as she sat there. Just her unique temperament alone attracted the attention of many members of the opposite sex.","Guan Yan noticed the gazes on them. She supported her chin with her hand, painted with Danko, and blinked her peach-blossom eyes at the girl busy hacking into the system. “Hey, Boss. A handsome man 45° to the left has been looking at you for the longest time. I bet he’ll come over and ask for your phone number. Do you want to take a gamble?”","Qiao Nian had just imported all the entry and exit information from the name list that Guan Yan had obtained into the system and was waiting for the facial recognition progress. She looked at the progress bar on the screen amid Guan Yan’s nagging, then leaned back and casually turned to look in the direction she mentioned.","Not far to their left sat a table of foreigners. About seven or eight of them. They were all dressed in suits and looked like elites. They should be white-collar workers who had arranged to meet nearby to discuss something.","The independent continent had countless companies, and the various large factions also needed these financial talents. For example, the Chamber of Commerce Alliance had nurtured many such high-level elites.","It was not strange to see such a young man around here.","Qiao Nian only glanced at him indifferently before retracting her gaze. She did not take that glance to heart, nor did she notice that when she turned around, a handsome blond man’s face with a high nose and deep facial features instantly lit up. He revealed a row of neat teeth to his friend as he smiled brightly.","Qiao Nian: “Not interested.”","She focused on the progress bar on the screen as she lazily leaned against the back of the chair with her relaxed shoulders. This time, she was really too lazy to even lift her eyelids.","Guan Yan’s computer was not slow.","Soon, more than half of the progress bar was filled.","Qiao Nian picked up the glass of water on the table and was about to take a sip when she felt a shadow pressing down on her.","Qiao Nian frowned. She put down the glass and turned her head.","“Hello, beautiful. Can we exchange phone numbers?” The speaker was one of the men at the table next to hers.","With blond hair and blue eyes, he was exceptionally young and looked rather sunny. He had a mouthful of white teeth and his smile was bright and sunny."]},{"number":3646,"title":"Chapter 3646: Stealing Someone Right in Front of Him","paragraphs":["Chapter 3646: Stealing Someone Right in Front of Him","Still...","Qiao Nian looked at Guan Yan, who was laughing so hard that her temples were throbbing. She pursed her lips and said expressionlessly, “I’m sorry, we can’t.”","It was quite impolite!","The young man was a little disappointed, but he still persevered. He took a pen and wrote his phone number on the napkin before handing it to Qiao Nian.","“This is my contact number. If it’s convenient, you can call me.”","Before Qiao Nian could refuse, he smiled and said, “I don’t think you’re from the independent continent. You’re here for vacation, right? I’ve worked here for a few years. I can be your tour guide and show you around.”","Guan Yan whistled and winked at Qiao Nian. “Sun, look at how enthusiastic the handsome boy is. Why don’t you accept him?”","Qiao Nian glared at her. The coldness in her eyes deepened, and there was obvious impatience on her beautiful face.","She did not like being disturbed, especially when she was busy with serious matters! Moreover, she had clearly rejected him just now. It was a little annoying for the other party to continue pestering her...","“I told you, I—”","“She has a boyfriend.”","At this moment, someone pushed open the door and entered. A clear, spring-like voice cut in, but it had a toughness that could not be rejected.","Guan Yan, originally sitting crookedly in her seat watching the commotion, felt a chill down her spine. She quietly sat up and coughed to pretend that she did not exist.","She was too unlucky. It wasn’t easy to get to watch such a show, but she was still caught. She hoped that Young Master Ye would not think she was the pimp. Otherwise, she would be in trouble...","Ye Wangchuan strode in. Just his good looks and temperament alone were enough to suppress all the men in this small coffee shop.","He walked up to the golden-haired young man hitting on Qiao Nian and took the napkin with the phone number written on it. His dark eyes swept across the numbers, and his thin lips curled up. “Heh, you like my girlfriend?”","What a polite question.","The blond young man’s face turned red. He was so embarrassed that he wanted to find a hole to hide in. “Over here, as long as we’re not married, we have the freedom to make friends.”","Qin Si happened to hear this when he went to greet Guan Yan. He looked at the man in surprise as if he was looking at a monkey.","What year was it? There was still someone talking to Master Wang like this.","Amazing.","This man had guts.","Qiao Nian massaged her temples, feeling extremely annoyed. “I didn’t give him my phone number.”","“I know.” He had seen the situation outside the shop. It was purely this man trying to strike up a conversation.","However, he was still provoked. He smiled, and his refined and noble handsome face was filled with hostility. “Can’t you see yourself clearly? Even if you don’t have a mirror at home, you have urine, right? You want to poach on my territory like this? Which one of us do you think is blind?”","The blond young man’s expression turned ugly after being humiliated. His friends at the table behind him also stood up to support him.","“What’s wrong with you guys? Are you bullying my friend? Why don’t you take a look at this place? Why? Do you want to fight?”","The speaker was tall and muscular.","As he spoke, seven or eight people at the table stood up. All looked displeased, as if they wanted to use numbers to bully others.","The staff was terrified, afraid they would fight in the shop.","Qin Si was so angry that he laughed. He pressed the tip of his tongue against his chin and chuckled. “Come on, who’s afraid?”"]},{"number":3647,"title":"Chapter 3647: Sister Nian Found That Person","paragraphs":["Chapter 3647: Sister Nian Found That Person","Ye Wangchuan was calmer than him. He threw the napkin into the trash can before the blond young man. Then, he turned his head and said expressionlessly, “I’ll give you three seconds to get lost. If you don’t leave, today I’ll take whichever hand you used to write this phone number.”","He spoke nonchalantly, as if he was saying that the weather was good today.","The blond young man and his friends were stunned by Ye Wangchuan’s aura. They couldn’t figure out who these people were.","In the end, they were not the thugs of the independent continent. Seeing that they had only asked for a phone number and caused such a commotion, the blond youth did not want to cause a scene that could not be resolved. Thus, he gritted his teeth and left with his friends.","The group left noisily.","Qin Si was still angry. “Master Wang, are you going to let them leave just like that?”","F*ck, he wanted to beat those people up.","What the heck.","Ye Wangchuan ignored him and walked to Qiao Nian’s side. Seeing that the progress bar on her computer had reached 100%, he began to analyze the results.","A message popped up on the screen.","[SEVEN, male, 26, from Continent M.]","A photo was attached to it.","The face in the photo did not look like it had been taken at the airport security checkpoint. It looked more like a fake one synthesized by high-tech AI.","Seeing the photo on the immigration certificate, Qiao Nian could tell at a glance that it was fake, but that was not the main point.","More importantly...","She tilted her head and said seriously, “Do you think this person looks very similar to the person in the photo I brought back?”","Ye Wangchuan frowned. He had not thought of it at first, but after her reminder, he realized that Qiao Nian was right.","“You mean...”","Qiao Nian was direct. “I’m saying that this photo is fake. The identity is fake, but the person might not be fake!”","Qin Si also came over to take a look. He did not understand. “What are you talking about? What do you mean?”","Qiao Nian pointed at the photo on the screen and continued to analyze it with Ye Wangchuan. “Look at the degree of falsification of this photo. He’s a smart person. Since he can tamper with the immigration records and get himself a fake identity, why didn’t he make this fake photo more realistic? Instead, he made it so obvious that it was fake.”","Guan Yan also listened and stared at the girl.","Qiao Nian was very confident. “This means his goal is to let us find out this is a fake photo. No one will trace a fake photo and continue to investigate. We will definitely ignore it and try to find another way. However... he’s smart and good at thinking in the opposite direction. What if he uses a real ‘fake’ photo in all the fake information?”","The photo was photoshopped.","But what if he photoshopped it with his own photo?","Who would have thought that the traces he had photoshopped were his real photo?","This was a kind of reverse thinking.","Using common sense to mislead others.","If Qiao Nian had not coincidentally found that old photo in Nie Qingru’s vault in Continent M, she would not have thought in this direction. She might have been misled by this person...","However, she had seen Nie Qingru’s precious old photo.","There was no connection in this world without reason.","How could it be so coincidental that a fake photo casually photoshopped would look similar to the man in Nie Qingru’s treasured old photo?"]},{"number":3648,"title":"Chapter 3648: Boss, What Kind of Hatred Does He Have With You?","paragraphs":["Chapter 3648: Boss, What Kind of Hatred Does He Have With You?","There was only one possibility—that person was related to the man in Nie Qingru’s old photo. They might be relatives.","“Let me check this guy out.”","Qiao Nian was a person who did what she said.","She immediately intercepted the “fake” photo on the immigration information and imported it into the Independent Continent’s traffic surveillance cameras to track faces.","Just as she thought.","10 minutes later, the results were out.","This face had been captured at several intersections near the Chamber of Commerce Alliance and Simon’s residence. This meant that this man had indeed appeared in the independent continent!","Guan Yan was dumbfounded upon seeing the results. “Sun, you even guessed that.”","However, Qiao Nian’s expression darkened. A little tired, she closed her eyes.","Guan Yan did not notice this and asked her, “But what grudge do you have with him? Do you remember this face?”","She knew that Qiao Nian was a little face-blind.","She typically did not remember people she was unfamiliar with.","Qiao Nian opened her eyes. They were dark, as if she had guessed something. Her voice was slightly hoarse. “I’ve never seen him.”","“Then he...” Guan Yan was confused.","At this moment, Ye Wangchuan took the notebook from the girl, closed it, and returned it to Guan Yan. Then, he changed the topic. “There’s soup brewed at home. I’ll bring her back. You guys can chat alone.”","Guan Yan was suddenly interrupted. Her red lips parted slightly. Just as she was about to say something, she met the man’s dark, deep, and slightly warning gaze.","Suddenly tilting her head and seeing Qiao Nian’s tired expression, she tactfully shut her mouth in agreement.","“You guys go first. I’ll take a screenshot of this person’s information and email it later.”","“Thank you.” Qiao Nian really did not want to continue on this topic. She stood up and said to Guan Yan while patting her shoulder, “I’ll tell you when I find out.”","Guan Yan laughed. She had no intention of blaming Qiao Nian if she did not tell her eventually. “Okay.”","...","Qiao Nian followed Ye Wangchuan out.","The November weather was a little cold outside the coffee shop.","“Wait a minute.”","Qiao Nian heard someone calling her from behind after coming out.","She stopped in her tracks, and right on the heels of that, she felt a warm scarf wrapped tightly around her neck.","The weather had suddenly become less cold, and her mood seemed to have been gently caressed by something, straightening her frustrated heartstrings.","Ye Wangchuan walked to her side and held her hand. He walked towards the car parked by the roadside with Qiao Nian and asked casually, “Has the matter with Simon been resolved?”","“Yes,” Qiao Nian replied distractedly, still thinking about the photo. “He doesn’t want to drag the Chamber of Commerce Alliance down with him. He plans to resign as President and bear the consequences alone.”","Ye Wangchuan guessed she would not really let the Ji family go against the Chamber of Commerce Alliance for Ji Nan’s sake. This outcome was within his expectations.","They walked to the front of the car.","Ye Wangchuan let go of her hand and opened the passenger door for her. “It’s cold. Let’s get in quickly.”","Qiao Nian paused for half a second before suddenly saying, “That person... If I’m not wrong, he should be related to Nie Qingru. He...”","She did not say it.","Because she wasn’t sure yet.","If the man in the photo was really Nie Qingru’s ex-lover, the young man who looked similar to him might be related to her.","This feeling was very annoying.","However, Qiao Nian wasn’t sure if things were as she thought.","Ye Wangchuan seemed to know what she was going to say. His gaze was calm as he interrupted her. “Nie Qingru is Nie Qingru, and you are you. The grudges of the previous generation have nothing to do with you. If he blames you for this, something must be wrong with his brain. Nian Nian, there’s nothing to be conflicted about. Do what you have to do.”"]},{"number":3649,"title":"Chapter 3649: If Others Have It, My Nian Nian Has To Have It Too","paragraphs":["Chapter 3649: If Others Have It, My Nian Nian Has To Have It Too","Qiao Nian glanced at him, her pent-up emotions suddenly swept away. She smiled and stuffed one hand into her pocket. “You’re right.”","“Of course.” Seeing she was in a better mood, Ye Wangchuan went around the car to the driver’s seat. “Get in, Goddess Qiao.”","Qiao Nian clicked her tongue and raised her eyebrows. She bent down to get into the car and pulled the seatbelt. “Are you jealous about what happened just now?”","Ye Wangchuan usually did not call her “Goddess Qiao”, unless he was slightly upset about something.","Qiao Nian fastened her seatbelt and lowered her eyes, wanting to say, “I didn’t even see what he looked like.”","Ye Wangchuan entered the car and closed the door at the same time. Before putting on his seatbelt, he turned on the air conditioner and turned up the temperature. Hearing what the girl said, he raised his eyelids and smiled with faux anger. “Do you still want to see what he looks like?”","Qiao Nian tilted her head at him again, then leaned back in the seat calmly and did not say anything. Just that eye-catching face alone was quite seductive.","Ye Wangchuan’s eyelids twitched, and the faint smile faded from his thin lips. He also felt that his reaction was too immature, but a rock was pressing on his chest. “That person looks ordinary.”","Qiao Nian blinked slowly. Her lips were dry as she stared at him. “Then why are you angry?”","Ye Wangchuan was speechless.","She continued unhurriedly, “I don’t think I’m blind... Why would I abandon my rich and good-looking boyfriend to hook up with him?”","Normal people wouldn’t give up on Ye Wangchuan for someone else.","Qiao Nian felt that she was quite normal.","She did not like to explain her words and actions to anyone, but this person was Ye Wangchuan. Qiao Nian did not find it difficult to explain.","“After speaking with Simon at the Chamber of Commerce Alliance, I’ve been checking the entry and exit records of the person he mentioned. I didn’t notice anyone around.","“That person suddenly came to talk to me. I immediately rejected him when he asked for my contact information. I didn’t expect him to not give up and even write his contact information for me.”","Qiao Nian’s tone was calm. “... Even if you hadn’t come over, I wouldn’t have taken that napkin. I would have told him I had a boyfriend and asked him to stop harassing me.”","The ups and downs in Ye Wangchuan’s heart were easily soothed. He pursed his lips, but he could not suppress his emerging smile. Thousands of stars fell into his eyes, reflecting the girl’s perverse but serious face. “I suddenly want to get married.”","Qiao Nian paused for a second and rubbed her eyebrows. She said speechlessly, “I didn’t say I didn’t agree to it. You were the one who insisted on waiting until the legal age.”","Actually, they could register overseas if they really wanted to get married.","She was already 20 years old and had the right to register her marriage overseas. She did not have to wait another year.","Ye Wangchuan smiled gently but forcefully. “Wait another year. If others have it, my Nian Nian will have it too!”","For example, a grand proposal ceremony.","A perfect wedding.","An unforgettable night.","Qiao Nian knew what he meant. She didn’t care about these things, but for the first time, she did not say anything to ruin the atmosphere.","Ye Wangchuan quickly changed the topic. “Where are you going now?”","“The First Research Institute.”","He started the engine. “I’ll drive you there.”","Qiao Nian was a little tired, so she nodded and leaned back in the seat. She took out her cell phone and sent Feng Yu a message telling him she was on the way there."]},{"number":3650,"title":"Chapter 3650: I Originally Wanted to Give Her a Rose at Her Funeral","paragraphs":["Chapter 3650: I Originally Wanted to Give Her a Rose at Her Funeral","At the same time.","The high seas were covered in black clouds in extreme weather.","The sea looked dark and dangerous in an environment without light. Visibility at sea level was less than a hundred meters. Even experienced sailors did not dare to be careless in this damned weather.","The wind and waves were strong, and most of the guests were hiding in their cabins. Only a few figures were on the deck.","A man in black clothes, black pants, and a hood was leaning against the railing holding a beer bottle and looking at the sea. He made small talk and drank leisurely.","Not far from him, two crew members were complaining about this extreme damn weather.","“...The dark clouds are getting lower and lower. It looks like there might be thunderstorms at night.”","“The wind and waves are so strong. It would be terrible if we encountered thunder and rain again. I hope God doesn’t let us be too unlucky!”","“Tsk, we’re lucky. A few days ago, someone took care of a large pirate organization in the open sea. Otherwise, it would be likely to encounter them in this damned weather! At least we don’t have to worry about encountering pirates this time...”","“Who do you think the person that everyone in Continent M was looking for was... I heard from my cousin that a big shot blocked all planes and routes for 10 hours that day. It caused a huge commotion. In the end, not long after, the terminal was mysteriously unsealed.”","“That’s the business of the big shots. How can civilians like us know?”","...","The young man, drinking with his arms against the railing, lowered his head and chuckled. He suddenly said as if he was mocking him, “They tried to capture someone.”","A few crew members hiding in a corner and chatting immediately noticed him.","Everyone looked at each other. They did not understand why this person would come to the deck to drink in this damned weather.","Seeing no one speaking, the young man turned around, revealing a young and gentle face under the hood. There was a smile on his lips, but the smile did not reach his eyes. “But that person ran away.”","What?","What on earth was this person talking about!","The young man did not care if they could understand him or not. It was as if he only wanted to speak. “That person also dealt with the pirates on the high seas and gave the big shot you mentioned a loud slap!”","“Pfft.” As he continued his monologue, he suddenly laughed, looking quite happy. “Well done! I’ve wanted to do this for a long time. Unfortunately... it’s not the time yet. She happened to help me give them a tight slap. I should thank her for avenging me, but I can’t thank her in person, nor can I successfully send a bouquet of flowers to her grave to thank her.”","According to his original plan, Qiao Nian would have died.","He should dress up for the funeral and present the legendary figure with a beautiful flower. It must be a delicate rose.","Because only the dazzling red was worthy of someone like Qiao Nian.","The pale chrysanthemum was not suitable for her, and the pure white was not a color that the dirty blood flowing in her body was worthy of!","Unfortunately, he failed to realize his plan. Instead, he let the other party notice his tracks...","But so what?","This game had just begun. It was too early to say who had lost.","“Who are you?” a crew member asked boldly.","The young man watched as a small fish in the sea was swallowed by the black waves. He looked up and said, “SEVEN.”","While everyone was still looking at each other, he suddenly threw down the beer bottle and started walking towards the cabin..."]},{"number":3651,"title":"Chapter 3651: Could It Be That She Still Wanted to Kill Her Grandmother With Her Own Hands?","paragraphs":["Chapter 3651: Could It Be That She Still Wanted to Kill Her Grandmother With Her Own Hands?","Continent M.","Nie Qingru had yet to clean up the mess after what happened a few days ago.","Because of her impulsive actions, in the past few days, not only had the Privy Council been looking for her, but people from the aviation and sea transportation departments had also been looking for her, making Nie Qingru unable to bear the disturbance.","She only got rid of the people from the Privy Council in the evening. As soon as she reached home, she threw down her large hat, revealing a sinister face. She asked the person who followed her in, “Is there any news from the independent continent?”","Shadow said softly, “Ji Lingfeng has already undergone surgery. If I’m not wrong, he should be out of danger. Elder Zhong is still taking care of him at the hospital. He even transferred some special medicine from the Pharmacy Association...”","“Hmph.” Nie Qingru sat on the sofa and sneered. “He’s lucky.”","If not for the fact that the evil creature was willing to take the risk to obtain the antidote for him, the grass on Ji Lingfeng’s grave would have grown more than a foot tall!","Nie Qingru thought of the things taken away and felt unhappy. “What about her?”","Shadow raised his head slightly. “Qiao Nian hasn’t done anything recently. She has been staying at Bright Gate’s base and hasn’t gone out. Today, she went out to see Simon. I don’t know what they talked about, but she left the Chamber of Commerce Alliance not long after. It seems they didn’t quarrel. However, not long after she left, Simon gathered the core members of the Chamber of Commerce Alliance for an internal meeting and proposed to resign. This should be Qiao Nian’s doing!”","Nie Qingru couldn’t hide her disgust. “It’s normal for her to do this. Isn’t the direct descendant of the Ji family like this? Whoever offends them will definitely be killed.”","Shadow remained silent.","Nie Qingru probably found it boring. She bent down and picked up the bottle on the table. She opened the cork and took a glass for herself. She poured a glass of tequila and held it in her hand. “Where is he? He’s not back yet.”","Shadow had been by her side for decades. Even though Nie Qingru did not specify who it was, he still understood who Nie Qingru was asking about.","“Don’t worry, Young Master is on his way back. He’s coming back by sea. He’s capable enough. Qiao Nian won’t be able to detect his existence so easily.”","“Mm.”","Nie Qingru took a deep breath, almost emotionless.","Just as Shadow was hesitating to ask her to call the other party, he received a call.","Shadow knew the rules. He covered the receiver and said, “Empress, I’ve to answer this call.”","“Go.” Nie Qingru swirled the wine expressionlessly, her mind elsewhere.","Shadow walked to the side and picked up the call. The other party spoke, and his expression turned ugly. He returned in less than two minutes and said to Nie Qingru, “Something happened.”","Nie Qingru had just drunk a mouthful of wine. The strong brew was unpleasant when it entered her throat. Hearing the panic in Shadow’s voice, it did not seem comfortable.","She put down the glass and asked coldly, “What is it?”","Shadow gritted his teeth before saying, “Qiao Nian found out about Young Master! According to the information we received on the high seas, she seems to want to keep him there.”","“What?!”","The usually unshakable Nie Qingru suddenly stood up. Her molars were clenched tightly, and her face was twisted in disbelief. “How did she find out about the Xicheng? No, what does she want?! It’s not enough to take the antidote from me, and Qixing’s death isn’t enough... What does she want?! Does she really want to kill her grandmother for Ji Qing?!”","Nie Qingru’s chest heaved up and down. Anger poured into her, causing her head to buzz non-stop. It was as if she had returned to decades ago."]},{"number":3652,"title":"Chapter 3652: Sister Nian Has Tracked That Person","paragraphs":["Chapter 3652: Sister Nian Has Tracked That Person","Back then she had no strength to resist fate. She could only be like a fish on a stick, waiting to be slaughtered.","However, she was no longer in her early twenties. She was no longer the woman who could only cry and do nothing.","“Send someone to pick up Xicheng immediately.” Nie Qingru made a prompt decision. “We must take Xicheng away before her people arrive.”","“Yes.”","Shadow did not dare to be negligent and hurried to do it.","Nie Qingru took a deep breath and suddenly called out to him with a pale face, in a muffled voice, “Do you think I’m not ruthless enough, that I’m giving her a chance to anger me again and again? If I had been ruthless from the beginning, she wouldn’t have had the chance to force me to this point...”","Shadow did not dare to answer. He just looked at the tired woman quietly. “I don’t know.”","Actually, he knew in his heart.","Nie Qingru might not have been ruthless to Qiao Nian in the beginning, but it was not because she was willing to let Qiao Nian off. It was purely because the Empress thought that a girl in her early twenties would not cause much trouble, so she only asked Yu Qingliu to embarrass her.","They did not expect Qiao Nian to have such a powerful force behind her, nor did they expect her to be more difficult to deal with than they had imagined.","Until today.","However, Shadow was unsure if he could kill Qiao Nian from the beginning... If Qiao Nian was not prepared, there was still a chance.","However, there were no ifs or hypotheses in this world.","“Empress, don’t worry. Young Master Xicheng will be fine!” He comforted Nie Qingru and quickly went to find someone.","Nie Qingru also picked up her cell phone from the sofa. With a solemn expression, she found a number and dialed the other party.","Beep...","The call went through.","However, unluckily, the signal at sea was not good, and it was even harder to get a signal in rough weather.","When her call went through, perhaps affected by the high seas storm, the mechanical female voice sounded after only one ring.","“I’m sorry, the number you dialed is not in the area.”","Nie Qingru frowned and gripped her cell phone tightly. The light and shadow outlined her pale face and made it difficult for her to breathe.","**","First Research Institute, Feng Yu’s office.","The girl crossed her legs on the sofa, waiting for Feng Yu to return. She was on a call with someone.","“Qiao, can you find a reliable person to help me next time? Are you sure this thing is reliable?!”","In the video, Jian Jin expressionlessly shifted the camera a little to the side. A man with a head of bird feathers entered the camera arrogantly. His emerald green hair was messed up by the sea breeze, and he looked like a parrot baring its fangs.","Obviously, he had heard Jian Jin’s merciless ridicule and exploded. “How am I f*cking unreliable? Little kid, it’s the 21st century. Why are you still judging people by their appearance?!”","“Little kid, my ass!” Jian Jin raised her leg and kicked him.","Slim Waist Control dodged nimbly and scolded mercilessly, “F*ck, just say what you want to say. Don’t f*cking touch me. Can you afford it if my face is messed up?”","Jian Jin’s temples throbbed wildly. She was almost annoyed to death by this guy. She turned to look at the girl on the video call and couldn’t help but say, “Why don’t I throw him into the sea? I’ll bring back the person you mentioned. I don’t need him to hold us back here.”","Qiao Nian looked at them and was convinced. She said, “Slim Waist Control is good at tracking. It’ll be easier to find the person if you have him.”"]},{"number":3653,"title":"Chapter 3653: Sister Nian Wants to Shoot the Ship Down Too","paragraphs":["Chapter 3653: Sister Nian Wants to Shoot the Ship Down Too","“Okay.” Jian Jin looked at the man baring his fangs and brandishing his claws. She pursed her lips and reluctantly agreed.","“Heh! What kind of look is that!” Slim Waist Control happened to see the corners of her lips curling down and raised his head in anger. “You don’t believe in me?”","Jian Jin couldn’t be bothered to argue with him. She took her phone and walked to the other side to continue talking to the girl. “Qiao, what do you want to do when we find him?”","On the other end of the video call, Qiao Nian propped up her chin. Under her baseball cap, her eyes were bright and arrogant. “She wanted to shoot down my ship before... Coincidentally, I have the same thought!”","Jian Jin gasped. “You mean...”","Qiao Nian said concisely, “When we find him, we’ll sink his ship into the sea. Then, we’ll use the lifeboat to save the passengers one by one. I’ll bear all their losses, including the cost of the ship! I only want to catch that person.”","Jian Jin instantly understood what she meant.","That person left the independent continent by water and carefully chose a half-fishing and half-commercial cruise ship.","There were many ordinary people on the cruise ship.","It was almost impossible for them to board the ship without alerting these people... Therefore, Qiao’s method was simple and crude.","She would sink the ship without hurting anyone. She would cover all the losses and ensure the safety of the ordinary people.","It was in public waters.","It was normal for accidents to happen in this area of the sea.","Jian Jin had been in the illegal district for so long that she was numb to it.","However, she knew that Qiao Nian wasn’t such a person. She had her principles and bottom line. She wouldn’t break her bottom line for a certain purpose.","Although this would be more troublesome than the other methods, Jian Jin did not complain. She nodded. “Okay, I promise to catch him for you.”","“Thanks.”","Qiao Nian thanked her softly.","Jian Jin smiled and high-fived her through the screen. “You’re making us seem like we’re strangers. If you have time... come to the illegal district to play sometime. Big Boss Lu misses you too.”","Qiao Nian still couldn’t meet Lu Zhi calmly. She rubbed her eyebrows and said with a headache, “We’ll see.”","“Alright, it depends on your time.” Jian Jin knew how much had happened between the two of them before. She also knew that Qiao Nian had yet to come to terms with Lu Zhi, so she did not force her. “I won’t talk to you anymore. I’ll let them know first.”","“Okay.”","After Qiao Nian finished speaking, she saw that Jian Jin had hung up the video call. The screen had lost its light and turned dark.","She was still waiting for Feng Yu to return and was not in a hurry to leave. She found a plug-in to charge her cell phone and used Feng Yu’s computer to open the local area network in the open sea to track it...","She had been investigating SEVEN’s route out of the independent continent in the car.","Fortunately, she found a lot of traces through that photo. With a little speculation, she found the vehicle he took when he left and the road map when he left the independent continent.","Qiao Nian called Jian Jin.","The high seas had always been Jian Jin’s territory.","Although this was a no-man’s-land, Lu Zhi loved to interfere in this kind of no-man’s-land. Otherwise, how could he be called the king of the gray area?","It could be said that Nie Qingru and this person were unlucky.","Qiao Nian made a call. Jian Jin happened to be working in a small fishing village not far from the sea area she mentioned. Moreover, Slim Waist Control was with her."]},{"number":3654,"title":"Chapter 3654: Problem with the Satellite Signal","paragraphs":["Chapter 3654: Problem with the Satellite Signal","Qiao Nian asked the two of them to intercept the ship.","She tapped open the satellite positioning map and quickly locked onto a few speedboats through the LAN scan.","It was Jian Jin’s speedboat.","In the southwest direction of the sea.","The ferry carrying SEVEN was moving towards Continent M at a steady speed.","This ferry was used for both business and fishing, so it did not sail very fast.","Qiao Nian silently calculated the speed of the two vessels and estimated that Jian Jin and the others would catch up to the ferry in about two hours.","Two hours later...","The ferry was about to reach the border between the high seas and Continent M.","Emotions surged in her eyes. She used the mouse to pull the map to the intersection of the two seas. Through the satellite map, Qiao Nian immediately realized that something was wrong.","—There were other vessels!","She saw about five or six cruise ships rushing towards the dual-use ferry... Given that speed, those cruise ships were meant to pick someone up!","Nie Qingru...","Qiao Nian narrowed her eyes and moved quickly. She immediately pinpointed the location of the ships and searched for the person behind them.","As expected, those ships belonged to the reclusive families. Nie Qingru must have sensed something and knew she wanted to keep her people alive.","Qiao Nian’s expression was slightly cold. Her lips curled into a smile that was quite impatient. Then, she picked up her phone and called Jian Jin again.","“The people from the reclusive families are there too. Hurry up and end the battle!”","“Why are they here?”","“I’m not sure.” Qiao Nian cut to the chase. “Remember what I said. You have to leave within half an hour of the attack, whether you find the person or not!”","She knew Nie Qingru well and did not want to drag Jian Jin down.","Jian Jin wanted to say something else. “But Qiao...”","Qiao Nian was determined. “Listen to me. I have a way to prevent her from finding out about you. In short, we’ll retreat in half an hour.”","After saying that, she ignored Jian Jin and hung up. She took a photo of the map on the computer and sent it to her. Then, she sent the accurate latitude and longitude of the fishing ship and the location she had predicted to arrive in two hours.","Jian Jin replied to her message.","Qiao Nian then calmly told her that the signal would be lost for two to three hours and asked her to be prepared.","Jian Jin replied with an “OK” emoji.","Qiao Nian returned to the computer and looked sideways at the satellite network in the high seas area. She narrowed her eyes and sat down, then her left hand quickly typed on the keyboard.","She only had one hand to use.","However, it took less than 10 minutes to successfully cut off the satellite network on the high seas and all the network signals at even the major borders!","The lack of network signal meant that some unprepared ships would lose their tracking direction. It would be difficult to track the exact location of the dual-use ferry they were looking for under such circumstances.","This was the effect Qiao Nian wanted.","She watched as all the red dots on the high seas satellite map disappeared. She placed her left hand gently on the keyboard and raised her eyebrows, waiting for Nie Qingru’s reaction.","**","“What?!”","“You said we lost contact with Xicheng in international waters?”","Nie Qingru smashed the glass on the ground, causing red wine to splash and stain the expensive carpet.","However, no one cared about this now.","Nie Qingru walked to Shadow, her breathing heavy. She grabbed his collar and asked through gritted teeth, “Tell me, what happened?!”"]},{"number":3655,"title":"Chapter 3655: Those People from the Privy Council Won’t Let You Off","paragraphs":["Chapter 3655: Those People from the Privy Council Won’t Let You Off","Shadow tightened his neck and said with difficulty, “Empress, we have lost contact not only with Young Master Xicheng but also with all the ships in the high seas.”","Nie Qingru loosened her grip slightly.","Shadow could breathe a little. “Someone took down the satellite network, causing all the signals in that area to be cut off. It’s difficult for us to find the detailed location of Young Master Xicheng’s ship through the satellite signals.”","The veins on the back of Nie Qingru’s hand bulged. Without hesitation, she squeezed out a name: “Qiao Nian.”","Shadow raised his head and looked at her. His eyes showed emotion, but he did not dare to say anything.","The current situation was obviously caused by Qiao Nian. Only she had the ability and courage to cut off the entire high seas satellite network.","“I’ve already asked the hackers of the reclusive families to decipher the Trojan Horse program as soon as possible and restore the satellite positioning signal in that sea area.","“It’s just that... you know her ability. I reckon the Trojan Horse program won’t be deciphered for a while.”","The Red Alliance’s Sun’s renown was not for nothing.","Qiao Nian released a few programs on the market. Be it Trojan Horse, virus, or iris verification, all of them were top-notch technology.","The hackers they cultivated were not bad.","However, compared to a hacker king like Qiao Nian, who came from an unorthodox background, the difference was not only in strength but also in her treacherous thinking when designing Trojan Horses.","Qiao Nian’s viruses had never been that complex. It was just that no one could guess her thoughts.","She always placed the loophole in deciphering the virus in an unexpected place. This was the most difficult part...","“Her target should be Young Master Xicheng.”","“Of course, I know what she wants to do!” Nie Qingru couldn’t breathe properly, so she naturally couldn’t control her temper.","In a rare moment of lost composure, she paced around, but the situation in front of her forced her to be unable to calm down and think of a solution.","Nie Qingru suddenly stopped halfway. “No, I can’t wait anymore!”","Shadow saw her rush over with a sullen expression and anger in her eyes. “Use my name to pressure Beijing.”","“Empress?”","“Put pressure on them in the business dealings and make my request. Tell them that if anyone touches that ship, I will destroy the business cooperation project I agreed to at all costs!”","With Smith Bank in her possession, she naturally had the capital to say harsh words.","If Nie Qingru insisted on tampering with the bank settlement system, not to mention how much she would lose, she would definitely cause huge losses to many companies in Beijing.","She was threatening the other party to stop even if it would cause collateral damage.","Of course, Shadow understood her plan, but he reminded her. “Empress, if the Privy Council finds out, I’m afraid...”","Elder Xue and the others were already extremely dissatisfied with the Empress.","If the Empress insisted on destroying the business cooperation, who knew how much trouble the Privy Council would cause?","They weren’t in a good situation in the Privy Council.","Although the conservatives, led by Elder Xue, appeared to be on the Empress’ side, in reality, Elder Xue only set out for the benefit of the reclusive families and did not listen to the Empress.","The radical faction they once firmly controlled gradually became loose after Leonard’s death. They began to lean towards neutrality and no longer followed the Empress’ orders.","As for the Church...","The archbishop had never taken them seriously. There were not many conflicts between the two sides, but the neutral faction led by the archbishop was a tough nut to crack. None of them were to be trifled with."]},{"number":3656,"title":"Chapter 3656: It’s Too Late to Find Out About the Signal Now","paragraphs":["Chapter 3656: It’s Too Late to Find Out About the Signal Now","In this way, their authority in the Privy Council had been greatly weakened.","This time, Elder Xue was also extremely dissatisfied with them. Now, if the Empress were to do something that would disappoint those old fellows from the Privy Council at this juncture...","No one knew how the Privy Council would deal with the Empress.","“I know what you’re thinking, but I won’t leave Xicheng alone.” Nie Qingru’s eyes darkened, and he shut up. “Do as I say!”","Shadow lowered his head. “Yes.”","Nie Qingru watched him leave again. This time, she took a deep breath to prevent losing control of her emotions.","She turned around and went upstairs rationally. She first contacted the people who were going to pick Xicheng up.","Nie Qingru’s thoughts were clear.","On the one hand, she wanted to pressure Beijing and threaten the people Qiao Nian cared about to hold that lunatic back. Then, she would get the others to rush to the sea area to save Xicheng as soon as possible.","Nie Qingru didn’t know what Qiao Nian wanted to do. This unknown anxiety of losing control of the situation made her every step upstairs especially heavy...","However, she knew that no matter how heavy her heart was, she could not fall.","She couldn’t accept something happening to Xicheng in the open sea and that it had to do with the Ji family!","**","At this moment, dark clouds pressed down on the high seas, and a drizzle fell.","Under the continuous drizzle, people felt frustrated.","On the deck, the busy crew complained about the rain and continued to worry about the possibility of thunderstorms at night.","None of them knew that they had become the center of the storm.","The two forces were about to clash fiercely in this sea area with them at the center!","After leaving the deck, Di Xicheng did not return to his room. Instead, he took a breather and smoked on the narrow walkway of the cabin.","The hair hanging down from his brow bone was wet and stuck to his face. His pale skin was very fragile, and his eyes hidden under his hair were almost evil.","His thin lips bit on the cigarette, but he did not smoke it. He held it in his mouth and leaned against the narrow edge of the walkway, looking like he was about to jump into the sea.","Such a strange person with such a strange temperament... made those who were originally interested in his appearance not dare to approach him.","He was leaning against the wall as if nothing had happened. Hearing a crew member coming out from the narrow aisle of the pilothouse below, he cursed in a low voice, “F*ck, I’m so unlucky today! It’s fine if it rains, it’s fine even if it’s a thunderstorm, but the satellite signal has failed. I don’t know when it will be restored. Otherwise, it’ll be terrible if we lose the navigation route in this damned weather!”","When the young man in the black hoodie heard this, he raised his eyes slightly and held the cigarette between two fingers. He looked at the person who walked out and asked in a low voice, “When did you lose the signal?”","The crew member did not expect someone to be smoking outside in this weather. Seeing that he was asking him, he did not hide anything. “About an hour or two ago.”","Then, the crew member asked him for a cigarette.","Di Xicheng gave him a stick out of respect.","The crew member lit it and puffed out a smoke ring. Then, he tilted his head with a relaxed expression and said, “I’m telling you, don’t tell the others. The captain doesn’t want us to say it for fear of causing panic among the guests.","“We’re in the open sea. This sea area is just like this. Small malfunctions from time to time are the norm. Usually, it’s not a big problem. This time, it’s just a signal cutoff. It might recover after a while.”","The crew member sighed. “I just feel that it’s too unlucky to encounter a signal malfunction in this damned weather, so I complained a little. Brother, forget it. Don’t be afraid...”","As he spoke, he patted the young man’s shoulder to comfort him, not noticing the slight change in the other party’s expression."]},{"number":3657,"title":"Chapter 3657: Who Said Sister Nian Is a Reasonable Person?","paragraphs":["Chapter 3657: Who Said Sister Nian Is a Reasonable Person?","Di Xicheng tried to calm down. “You said our ship has lost signal for almost two hours.”","The crew member took a puff of his cigarette and turned around to look at him with a smile. “What’s with your expression? Scared? Didn’t I tell you not to be afraid? This place is like this. Sigh. I wouldn’t have told you if I had known you’d be afraid! If the captain finds out, he’ll definitely be angry with me. Don’t tell anyone... We didn’t lose the signal ourselves. I suspect a problem with the satellite signal in this sea area.”","At this point, the crew member became annoyed. He took a deep puff of his cigarette and held the butt with his hand. “What a damnable weather! I hope there won’t be a rainstorm tonight and the signal will be restored sooner!”","Di Xicheng had already guessed what the ‘lost satellite signal’ was about. He turned around and walked into the cabin with a wooden face.","“Hey, brother. Where are you going?” The crew member called out from behind upon seeing him walking back without saying a word.","Di Xicheng turned a deaf ear and walked faster.","At this moment, a crew member exclaimed, “Ah, what’s that! Pirates?”","Di Xicheng was about to push the door open and enter when he heard the surprised voice behind him. He couldn’t help but stop in his tracks and turn around.","The crew member was so frightened that his expression changed drastically. Not caring about smoking anymore, he threw the cigarette on the ground, leaned on the railing, and stretched his neck to size up the pirates. “Didn’t they say that a big boss attacked the pirates in this area a few days ago? The pirates have stopped much? Damn it, where did these pirates come from?”","Di Xicheng walked over and looked at where he was looking.","The weather was bad, and visibility was extremely low.","In the misty black fog, they could see laser lights passing through the fog from afar. About four or five speedboats were quickly gaining on them...","The sound of the speedboats breaking through the waves was getting closer and closer.","The crew member cursed and did not waste any more time before anxiously saying, “I’ll inform the captain!”","...","Di Xicheng was left on the narrow aisle.","His temples bulged as he looked coldly at the speedboat team about 5 minutes out.","A beast-like sneer escaped from his throat.","“Qiao Nian!”","He rarely underestimated someone.","But he had misjudged this time!","However, Di Xicheng was not someone who would give up without a fight.","He knew better than anyone that the speedboats chasing after him from outside Continent M could not have been sent by Nie Qingru to pick him up.","He was not frightened by the sudden situation in front of him. He quickly composed himself and turned around to return to his room.","Every step Di Xicheng took was fast and steady.","In his opinion, there were still five minutes for him to do something.","He was certain that the other party would not go too far. At the very least, they would capture him alive... If so, they would have to negotiate with the people on the ship.","What he needed to do was to seize the time when the two sides were negotiating to escape.","He entered his room and packed everything he needed quickly, preparing to leave.","However, at this moment, he heard a woman’s voice.","“Take the boat down!”","Silence.","Di Xicheng’s eyes suddenly widened. Before he could do anything, he felt the ship being hit. The place where he was standing shook...","Even though he thought he had calculated everything perfectly, he couldn’t help but curse at this moment.","“F*ck!”","**","Jian Jin found the dual-use ferry based on the location Slim Waist Control sent and immediately set on.","Before catching up, she told her subordinates about the plan."]},{"number":3658,"title":"Chapter 3658: I’ve Seen This Person, He’s on the Ship","paragraphs":["Chapter 3658: I’ve Seen This Person, He’s on the Ship","The people she brought were all good picks from Tian Chen.","The person in charge of target shooting was very skilled, only sinking the bottom warehouse of the ship and damaging the hull, allowing seawater to pour in to sink the ferry.","They wouldn’t hurt people.","“Prepare the lifeboats.”","Jian Jin watched as the small ferry in front of her began to tilt and sink. She immediately waved her hand and arranged for her subordinates to start getting people out.","“Yes.”","Her subordinates began to release the lifeboats into the water in an orderly manner. At the same time, they drove the speedboats to save those who had chosen to jump into the water to survive.","Slim Waist Control looked at this scene and grabbed a handful of his emerald green hair. He clicked his tongue and said, “Boss’s single shot costs at least nine digits. You guys are really prodigal.”","Qiao Nian said that she would bear all the losses.","This shot was a threat anywhere. It was simply the most expensive fireworks in the world.","Jian Jin crossed her arms and glanced at him impatiently. “Qiao didn’t spend your money. What are you doing here? You’re acting like a woman!”","Slim Waist Control hated it the most when people said he was like a woman. He retorted, “Yes, you’re like a man. You’re most like a man! I’ll give you the Best Man Award when I get back...”","“Look at the time. Qiao said we could stay for half an hour at most. Since she spent so much money to sink this ship, let’s not waste her money.” Jian Jin turned around and ignored him.","Although Slim Waist Control was unconvinced, he knew the situation and did not argue with her anymore.","More than half of the small ferry had sunk into the water, and many people had already jumped into the water.","When they realized that the “pirates” had no intention of hurting anyone, they consciously approached the lifeboats.","They watched as people were scooped up one after another.","As Slim Waist Control narrowed his eyes and searched around, his expression became solemn. “There’s no such person.”","Jian Jin was holding a tablet with the photo Qiao Nian sent her on the screen. The composite photo was blurry, but she could roughly tell what the man looked like.","While Slim Waist Control searched for him, she was doing the same on the lifeboats.","She also realized that the person they were looking for was not among the people who had been saved.","“Could the information Qiao gave be wrong?” Jian Jin was puzzled.","More than half of the people had been saved. The rest were exposed on the sea surface. They could roughly see what they looked like.","She did not notice anyone suspicious.","Jian Jin couldn’t help but wonder, “That person isn’t on this ship...?”","However, Slim Waist Control was unusually serious. “Impossible.”","Jian Jin was angry and wanted to ignore him.","Slim Waist Control continued, “Sun is never wrong. Since she said the person is on this ship, he must be here. There’s no mistake!”","Jian Jin took a deep breath and felt that it made sense.","She was an efficient person. Coupled with the fact that they did not have much time, she simply looked around and grabbed the collar of a man who looked like a crew member. She pulled him up and showed him the photo on the tablet before impatiently asking, “Have you seen this person?”","The crew member was frightened and his face was pale. He looked at the photo on the tablet from the corner of his eye and gasped. “Uh, isn’t this... Isn’t this the person on the deck?”","“You’ve seen him?” Jian Jin heaved a sigh of relief.","The crew member took a deep breath and hurriedly said, “I’ve seen him... I’ve seen him. This person is quite strange. Previously, when the weather changed, he was drinking on the deck and even said a few strange words.”"]},{"number":3659,"title":"Chapter 3659: No, We Have to Leave!","paragraphs":["Chapter 3659: No, We Have to Leave!","Jian Jin didn’t care about this and interrupted him. “Where is he now?”","The crew member fell into the lifeboat and shook his head. “I don’t know. I only know that he was still on the ship before you came. I saw him smoking in the aisle with a colleague of mine... I don’t know where he went after that.”","Jian Jin’s expression darkened.","When they shot down the ferry, he was still on the ship. What was going on now? Had he disappeared into the sea?","Their conversation fell into Slim Waist Control’s ears. He had the same expression as her. He frowned in disbelief. “What’s going on? He turned into a butterfly and flew away?”","Jian Jin rubbed her eyebrows and snapped, “I don’t know.”","Slim Waist Control looked down at the time on his watch and said impatiently, “No, there are only five minutes left.”","Sun had said that regardless of whether they could find him or not, they had to evacuate this place within half an hour.","It had taken them 10 minutes to sink the ferry, 15 minutes to save the passengers... and now they had less than five minutes.","Time was tight. If they couldn’t find him, they could only retreat.","Jian Jin took a deep breath and took off her coat. Without another word, she said, “I’ll go into the water and find him!”","Before Slim Waist Control could stop her, she jumped into the water and disappeared into the sea...","He grabbed a handful of hair and grumbled in annoyance. Then, he took off his jacket and hurriedly informed the others before also jumping into the sea.","**","Because of the bad weather, visibility in the water was low.","If he could still see about 100 meters above the sea, then after entering the water, Slim Waist Control realized he could only see within two to three meters of his reach.","With such visibility, not to mention finding someone, it was already good enough that he did not get swept away by the undercurrents.","He tried to find Jian Jin’s location. Not finding her, he couldn’t hold his breath and could only float to the surface.","When he broke out of the water and breathed in the fresh air, he saw Jian Jin emerging from the water a few meters away.","He swam over and did not say anything nasty. “No, we can’t find anyone in this weather. We have to go up.”","“Mm.”","Jian Jin had been down there herself and knew there was no way to find anyone at the bottom of the sea.","She wasn’t a stubborn person. She agreed and climbed onto the nearest speedboat with Slim Waist Control.","Their subordinates handed each of them a towel to wipe their faces. The water trickled down their bodies, and the wind began to blow, disturbing the sea surface.","No matter how unwilling Jian Jin was, she could only say coldly, “Get ready. Let’s go.”","Slim Waist Control casually wiped the water off his body and looked at the dozens of people they had saved. No matter how hard he looked, he could not see the face they were looking for.","He really couldn’t figure out where that person could hide under such circumstances.","Could it be that he could really fly?","He looked at the time. It was already the time Qiao Nian had mentioned.","They couldn’t stay any longer.","Sun never wasted words. Since she told them they had to leave within half an hour, there must be a reason for it. They had to leave.","Slim Waist Control could only help the others tie the rescue boat to the speedboat and prepare to retreat.","...","Waves broke on the surface of the sea.","The speedboats came and left quickly.","There was no movement on the calm sea surface for a long time. After five minutes of silence, there was no sound either. Only now did the person hiding at the bottom of the sea surface in a sorry state appear."]},{"number":3660,"title":"Chapter 3660: Come Back First","paragraphs":["Chapter 3660: Come Back First","The young man was still wearing a hoodie, but he did not have the leisurely arrogance to cover his head. At this moment, his entire body was soaked and he looked as miserable as could be.","Fortunately, he was carrying a leather bag and a small oxygen tank.","He probably had this trump card a long time ago, which was why he had such a small oxygen tank beside him. Although this oxygen tank could not last long, it helped him avoid the most critical search.","Looking at the destroyed ferry and the empty sea surface, Di Xicheng couldn’t imagine what would have happened to him if those people stayed for a few more minutes and his oxygen was exhausted or if the weather was better today and the visibility at the bottom of the sea was higher...","In short, he wouldn’t have been able to avoid the other party’s search like he just did.","He wasn’t in such a sorry state yet, but he knew very well that he would have to float on the surface for an unknown period until the people from the reclusive families came to pick him up.","In this weather, floating alone in the cold seawater, even if he was saved, he would at least lose a layer of skin.","“Qiao Nian...”","Di Xicheng’s lips, which had turned purple from the cold, uttered a name.","He floated on the sea for about two hours. All the blood in his body was frozen and he was about to lose consciousness... Finally, he heard the sound of a steam whistle.","Before Di Xicheng lost consciousness, he saw a few familiar faces pulling him up from the sea with his blurry vision. They called his name nervously.","“Young Master Xicheng.”","“Young Master Di.”","“Young Master Di, wake up. Doctor, quickly get the doctor here!”","Hearing the shouts, Di Xicheng struggled to move his lips, which were already numb from the cold, and just stared blankly at the rainy sky.","The dark clouds completely pressed down.","The weather was unbelievably cold.","He could no longer feel his lower body. Fortunately, Nie Qingru’s men had arrived quickly, so he did not freeze to death.","Di Xicheng could hear the chaotic footsteps on the deck, but he no longer had the strength to pay attention to this.","He could only think of one name.","Qiao Nian.","He had never suffered like this in his life.","Qiao Nian had almost taken his life this time and even made him look so miserable. Their grudge was set in stone.","This was the first time he was so excited to kill someone. It had nothing to do with the grudges he had been obsessed with in the past. He was like a lion in the wilderness that was eager to kill. He suddenly realized that someone in this world could compete with him.","His blood boiled, and his capillaries clamored crazily, hoarse with desire...","“Young Master Di, it’s a call from the Empress.” Someone squatted down and carefully put the phone to his ear with fear, not daring to look at the twisted and excited expression on his face.","The person on the other end of the cell phone probably asked if he was alright and what had happened.","Di Xicheng was exhausted. He relied on his willpower to not fall unconscious. Hearing the voice on the other end of the call, he did not care much. His hoarse voice carried a terrifying madness. “I’m fine. I just... found a fun opponent... It’s really interesting.”","...","Continent M.","Nie Qingru’s castle.","Hearing the crazy voice on the other end of the call saying something like “interesting opponent”, Nie Qingru’s eyelids twitched violently.","“Come back first.”"]},{"number":3661,"title":"Chapter 3661: She Should Teach an Ignorant Junior a Lesson","paragraphs":["At the same time, someone came in and walked to Nie Qingru’s side. Seeing that she was on the phone, he stood at the side respectfully and waited.","Nie Qingru said in a low voice, \"We’ll talk about it when you’re back safely!\"","She hung up.","Her facial muscles tightened and trembled. She glanced at her subordinate standing obediently at the side from the corner of her eye and walked straight to the sofa.","\"Speak.\"","The man lowered his head and said humbly, \"Empress, our people have finished the investigation. Someone sank the ferry Young Master Di was on. Everyone on the ferry was saved, leaving only Young Master Di behind. The other party probably didn’t find him and retreated in time. Now that the satellite signal in the high seas has been restored, we can’t find any traces of ships nearby...\"","The open sea was wide.","If they wanted to investigate, they could only check for traces of a ship in the accident area.","Once it exceeded a certain range, it was difficult to define whether those ships were the ones they were looking for or just passing by...","Nie Qingru had already walked to the leather sofa. At this moment, she staggered and grabbed the armrest to stabilize herself. The veins on the back of her hand bulged, and her graceful face looked extremely lost. \"You mean... she sank the ferry?!\"","The man with his head lowered did not dare to look up. \"Yes, that’s the result of the investigation.\"","\"Ah!\"","Nie Qingru slapped the armrest heavily, and her face twisted uncontrollably. \"Very good! As expected of my good granddaughter!\"","No one in the living room dared to speak. Even their breathing became lighter.","Nie Qingru forcefully suppressed her anger, but it still rushed from the soles of her feet to her head. She was so angry that smoke rose from her head, and her lips trembled uncontrollably.","She was almost certain that Qiao Nian had found pirates to sink their ferry to take revenge on her.","She had only done this once, but her good granddaughter took revenge on Xicheng for the same thing and returned the same thing to her!","She was even more ruthless and thorough than her.","\"Hehe.\" Nie Qingru sneered. She was also angered. \"Inform Elder Xue and the others of the Privy Council that I have something to discuss with them.\"","His subordinates did not dare to delay and immediately went to do it. \"Yes, Your Majesty.\"","Nie Qingru looked at their back as they left. The hatred in her eyes was like a poisonous snake lying dormant, ready to bite at any time.","She then contacted Shadow and asked him to pick Xicheng up at the pier and arrange for the best hospital and specialist doctor to go with him.","After Nie Qingru was done, she tidied up her fox fur coat, put on velvet gloves, and elegantly walked out of the castle villa.","She entered the car and instructed the chauffeur, \"To the Privy Council.\"","As the Empress of the reclusive families, she would never allow herself to be slapped in the face again and again. Otherwise, where would she put her face in the future?","Therefore, she had to discuss with the old fellows in the Privy Council how to give Qiao Nian a resounding counterattack!","Nie Qingru was confident that she could convince those old people.","Things had already developed to this point. It was no longer just about her, but also about the face of the entire reclusive families.","This time, she was determined to teach the younger generation an unforgettable lesson!","**","Qiao Nian was still waiting for news from Jian Jin and the others in Feng Yu’s office.","Upon receiving Jian Jin’s call, she was not surprised. She was still in the mood to comfort the disappointed person. \"It’s okay. We didn’t catch him this time. We’ll catch him next time.\"","\"But Qiao... It wasn’t easy for you to find this person’s whereabouts. You let him escape this time, it won’t be easy to catch him next time!\""]},{"number":3662,"title":"Chapter 3662: Sister Nian Doesn’t Seek Big Boss Lu’s Help","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian crossed her legs and placed her hand on her baseball cap before casually saying, \"If he’s so easy to catch, I’ll suspect I’ve found the wrong person. At least now I can confirm that he’s the one stirring up trouble in the independent continent.\"","This person was very scheming. To fool a sly old fox like Simon and escape unscathed, he was no ordinary person.","Qiao Nian was already mentally prepared that Jian Jin would return empty-handed this time.","\"You don’t have to take it to heart. My goal this time was only to give him a warning. It’s best if we can catch him, but it doesn’t matter if we can’t. I’ve already conveyed my intentions.\"","\"Yes.\" Jian Jin’s tone calmed down a little. After a moment of hesitation, she said, \"I’m afraid the reclusive families in Continent M won’t let this go.\"","\"There’s no room for reconciliation between me and her. Even if today’s incident didn’t happen, she wouldn’t have let me off either. So, I don’t care about this.\"","Then, Qiao Nian said, \"Don’t worry, I’ve already erased all traces of your visit. They won’t be able to trace it back to you. Arrange for those people to stay behind and let Slim Waist Control deal with the aftermath.\"","Jian Jin knew this was the only way to completely remove Tian Chen from this matter. She gritted her teeth. \"Yes, I understand.\"","Given her personality, she definitely had to do it to the end.","However, Tian Chen was not her company, after all. She had to think for Lu Zhi.","Nie Qingru and the reclusive families were not to be trifled with. It would be very troublesome if Tian Chen were involved... Jian Jin still felt bad. \"I’ll help you investigate that person again. His name is SEVEN? I’ll see if there’s such a person in the black market.\"","Qiao Nian’s slender and fair fingers tapped the table lightly with narrowed eyes and a frown. \"Don’t interfere in this matter anymore. Also, don’t tell Lu Zhi.\"","\"Actually, Qiao... As long as you ask Big Boss Lu, he won’t mind getting involved. He just doesn’t know how to express himself. He’s actually...\" Jian Jin struggled to express herself.","Qiao Nian interrupted her. \"I know, that’s why I didn’t ask for his help.\"","\"...You.\" Jian Jin wanted to ask why, but she couldn’t bring herself to. She had a feeling Lu Zhi had not said anything yet. As an outsider, she couldn’t expose this on his behalf.","Unexpectedly, she heard the girl’s calm and rational voice. \"Because I’m unable to give him what he wants.\"","Jian Jin was shocked, and her voice tightened. \"Y-You know?\"","\"Yes,\" Qiao Nian replied readily. Her eyelashes drooped slightly. \"I didn’t think in that direction at first, but I guessed it after thinking about it.\"","Jian Jin thought about it and realized that it was normal. Lu Zhi was too obvious. However, Qiao had always treated him as a friend whom she had experienced life and death with.","She wanted to ask Qiao Nian what she was thinking, but she felt there was no need.","Qiao Nian’s current attitude meant everything...","Qiao Nian also wanted to take this opportunity to make things clear. \"I don’t like to owe people favors. In the past, when I didn’t know, I could ask him for help because we’re friends. There’s no need to calculate things too clearly between friends. The next time he looks for me, I’ll help him back. But since I know his thoughts, I can’t ask him for help anymore. Jian Jin, do you understand?\"","Jian Jin smiled bitterly. \"I understand. What’s there not to understand? I just feel that Big Boss Lu is a little pitiful. He clearly knew you first, but in the end... he has low EQ. Otherwise, Bright Gate’s Young Master Ye wouldn’t have been able to woo you.\""]},{"number":3663,"title":"Chapter 3663: Investigate Nie Qingru’s Past","paragraphs":["If Lu Zhi’s EQ had been higher, and if he had taken the initiative...","If he hadn’t forced Qiao to like his posts all day long without making it clear that it was meant for her eyes... he wouldn’t have chased after her for so many years without her even noticing that he was wooing her.","Jian Jin was already mentally prepared and very open-minded. She immediately smiled and changed the topic. \"Since you don’t want to trouble him, I won’t tell him. As for helping you in the investigation, I want to do it myself. It doesn’t involve Tian Chen’s power... Don’t worry about me.\"","Qiao Nian couldn’t win against her. At this moment, footsteps came from the door. She guessed that Feng Yu had returned, so she stood up and hurriedly said to Jian Jin, \"I’ll call you later.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, she heard the sound of the door being opened.","Feng Yu entered the office and saw Qiao Nian waiting for him. He turned around and said a few words to his assistant, asking him to leave first.","He untied the scarf around his neck and walked in. \"Nian Nian, why are you here? Why didn’t you tell me you were here? If I had known, I would have come back earlier.\"","Qiao Nian nodded, put her phone back in her pocket, then looked up. \"I have something to ask you.\"","Feng Yu hung the scarf on the hanger and turned around with a smile. \"What’s the matter? Just say it.\"","\"Have you heard of SEVEN?\" Qiao Nian asked him directly.","\"SEVEN?\" Feng Yu was stunned for a moment. He frowned and thought for a long time before remembering. \"Isn’t this the name of a brand? I remember a shop with this name in the independent continent. I’ve encountered their items a few times at the auction previously.\"","Qiao Nian smiled. \"That’s my brand.\"","Feng Yu looked at her in surprise.","Qiao Nian did not hide anything from him. \"I work with an elder for that brand. She runs a corporation and has many businesses under her. Jewelry is one of them.\"","Yuan Yongqin was a business genius.","Cheng Feng Corporation had grown bigger and bigger under her leadership. In just a few years, it had almost surpassed the wealth accumulated by many people for generations.","She had never limited her vision to one place. She used Qiao Nian’s connections to expand the company brands under the corporation to places like the illegal district, Continent F, and even the independent continent.","Moreover, Yuan Yongqin was very good at public relations.","Their high-end jewelry and clothes were recognized by the noblewomen in the illegal district and the independent continent.","Many noble ladies had a few sets of high-end jewelry from SEVEN in their jewelry boxes. This was also why Feng Yu encountered this jewelry brand at the auction.","After a short moment of surprise, Feng Yu relaxed and looked at her in confusion. \"Since this is your brand, why are you suddenly asking me this?\"","Qiao Nian looked away. \"I’m not asking about the brand. I’m asking about a person.\"","What?","Feng Yu was even more confused.","\"A person? You mean someone called SEVEN?\"","\"Yes.\" Qiao Nian took a photocopied photo from her bag and handed it to him. \"Do you know this person?\"","Feng Yu took the photo from her. He frowned when his gaze landed on the smiling young man. He looked up and asked her, \"Who is this?\"","\"I don’t know either.\" Qiao Nian met his gaze frankly. \"This is the photo I found in Nie Qingru’s vault. I made a copy. She hid this photo very well, and he looks to be a very important person to her. That’s why I asked if you know this person.\""]},{"number":3664,"title":"Chapter 3664: Sister Nian Gradually Approaches the Truth","paragraphs":["Feng Yu seriously looked at the person in the photo and returned it to the girl before slowly saying in a deep voice, \"I’ve never seen this person before, but I’ve heard a little about her. It can be considered gossip...\"","Qiao Nian showed that she was all ears.","Feng Yu took a deep breath and continued, \"It’s said she used to have a longtime boyfriend. They had a deep relationship. Later on, for some reason, she married your grandfather and gave birth to your mother. During this process, that man seemed to have disappeared without a trace and I never heard any news about him again... There were some rumors that when that man heard she was married, he was very sad and left far away. He never returned.\"","\"He’s dead,\" Qiao Nian suddenly said softly.","Feng Yu was still immersed in his memories when he heard the girl’s calm words. He trembled as he looked at her in shock. \"You said...\"","\"This person is dead.\" Qiao Nian was calm as she looked into his eyes. \"And it looks like he’s been dead for a long time.\"","\"This!\" Feng Yu couldn’t describe his shock. He didn’t know what expression to make. \"There’s really such a person?! I thought this was just gossip. After all, no one has seen her so-called boyfriend...\"","Nie Qingru really did have a boyfriend she loved back then, but he passed away early. What secrets were hidden in the past?","Qiao Nian noticed the change in his expression and looked at him seriously. \"Do you know that person’s name?\"","Feng Yu came back to his senses and recalled seriously. \"I’ve only heard the gossip once. I don’t know the details... I think I heard that person’s surname is... Di. As for his name... I really don’t remember.\"","He could remember this surname because he was curious at that time and asked how to write this word. He had a deep impression of it.","After answering the girl’s question, he seemed to have remembered something. He looked at Qiao Nian worriedly. \"Is this photo related to the SEVEN you asked me about?\"","He thought of a possibility and immediately felt that it was ridiculous.","\"You already said that this person died a long time ago. Why are you still asking about him...\"","\"It’s nothing. I met someone who might have something to do with him recently.\" Qiao Nian put away the photo and restrained the dark glint in her eyes, returning to her usual casualness. \"I wanted to ask someone else, but not many people in the independent continent know about her past. I don’t trust anyone else, so I came to your office and waited for your return.\"","Feng Yu nodded to show that he understood. After some thought, he added, \"Actually, you can ask Emperor Ji. He might know some inside information.\"","To put it bluntly, this was a Ji family matter and involved family secrets.","No matter how close he was to Nie Qingru in age, he was still an outsider.","In addition, when Nie Qingru was all-powerful back then, he was still a small fry with no background in the independent continent and knew very little.","Although Ji Lingfeng was a generation younger than them, he controlled the Ji family for so many years. At the very least, he knew a little about the past. Perhaps he knew more than him.","Qiao Nian got what she wanted. She took her bag and turned around. \"He’s still in the ICU. Let’s talk about it later.\"","Ji Lingfeng had just gotten rid of the remaining poison not long ago and had to stay in the intensive care unit for some time under surveillance before he could be transferred to a normal ward.","Even if she wanted to ask him about the person, she had to wait for Ji Lingfeng to recover.","Qiao Nian did not intend to stay anymore and waved at Feng Yu. \"Dean, I’ll go back first.\""]},{"number":3665,"title":"Chapter 3665: Sister Nian: It Might Not Be That Simple","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian returned home after leaving the First Research Institute.","Ye Wangchuan was making soup.","\"You’re back?\" He walked out of the kitchen upon seeing her.","He was wearing a thin sweater. The collar was wide open, making his collarbone look fair. He was so handsome that he did not look like someone who knew how to cook.","Qiao Nian glanced at it once and then again. She put down her bag and spread out on the sofa. \"Yes. It smells so good. What did you cook?\"","Ye Wangchuan was still holding a spoon. Hearing this, the corners of his mouth curled up, and a deep smile flashed across his narrow eyes. \"Pig trotter soup.\"","Silence.","She had been drinking all kinds of soup for the past few days and was about to vomit.","Ye Wangchuan could tell that the girl’s expression immediately became awkward. He put the spoon back in the kitchen and walked out with a smile. \"Gu San said that you have to drink more soup.\"","Qiao Nian’s neck stiffened. \"... But I don’t have to drink it every day.\"","\"It’s fine. Drink as much as you want later.\"","Ye Wangchuan walked up to her and stuck his tall legs in front of her. He opened his palm and handed her an orange candy, saying lightly, \"If you feel uncomfortable, eat a candy.\"","Qiao Nian glanced at him and slowly took the candy. She peeled off the wrapper and threw it into her mouth; it tasted familiar and sweet.","Tense for the entire afternoon, Qiao Nian finally relaxed. She leaned back and took the initiative to tell him about Di Xicheng. \"I’ve found out that person’s whereabouts.","\"I wanted to stop him on the high seas, but I didn’t expect him to escape.\" She had a headache at the mention of this.","Supporting her forehead with her hand, she said rather irritably, \"With Nie Qingru’s personality, it’s impossible for her not to retaliate. Let’s see what she does next.\"","\"Actually, I know even if you don’t tell me.\"","Qiao Nian felt the sofa beside her sink instantly. She turned her head and saw Ye Wangchuan sitting down beside her.","She raised her eyebrows. Her body was still relaxed, as if used to being so close to him. She did not feel disgusted at all.","\"Who told you that?\"","\"You caused such a big commotion on the high seas. The illegal district, Continent F, and the independent continent have all received news. Even Beijing has heard the commotion this time...\"","Ye Wangchuan didn’t hide it from her. \"Old Master just called me an hour ago. He said that Continent M is threatening them with business dealings to manage what happened in the high seas. He asked me if you were doing something there.\"","At first, Qiao Nian was too lazy to move. Now, she frowned and sat up straighter. \"She went after Elder Ye?\"","\"Not just grandfather. Also Grandpa Jiang... This time, she caused a huge commotion. She probably thought you would catch that person, so she tried to threaten you to let him go from Beijing in advance. After receiving the news, she probably stopped contacting Beijing and stopped the cooperation.\"","Ye Wangchuan’s eyes were cold and handsome. He was elegant and spoke at a moderate pace. He had the demeanor of someone nurtured by a large family.","\"You don’t have to take this to heart.\" He could roughly see the unhappiness on Qiao Nian’s face and comforted her. \"Interrupting trade between both sides is a big deal. As long as she’s not crazy, she won’t easily make such a move that will cause both sides to suffer. She called Beijing previously because she was forced into a corner by you and didn’t get any concrete news. That’s why she contacted the Old Master... Now, she’s given up on this idea.\"","Qiao Nian’s tightly furrowed brows did not relax. Her dark eyes were heavy as if she was thinking about something. She pursed her lips and said after a while, \"... It might not be that simple.\""]},{"number":3666,"title":"Chapter 3666: Does Miss Qiao Have Any Plans?","paragraphs":["Seeing that she understood the situation, Ye Wangchuan gently patted the girl’s shoulder and said in a low but firm voice, \"Then, I’ll come back to trouble you when something happens!\"","Qiao Nian remained silent, thinking about what Nie Qingru would do next.","At this moment, Qin Si, Gu San, and the others returned with Guan Yan. There were more people at home now.","Dinner changed from stew to hotpot delivery.","Bo Jingxing had also returned from outside before dinner.","With so many people around, this hotpot meal was especially lively.","Qin Si had been taking care of Guan Yan along the way. He looked like he had settled down.","Qiao Nian had something on her mind and did not eat much. Most of the time, she watched them eat and listened to their conversation.","Bo Jingxing was going back to Beijing in a few days and asked Qin Si if he was leaving.","It wasn’t easy for Qin Si to meet Guan Yan, so he naturally refused. In the end, Bo Jingxing was going back alone.","It was dark outside.","The meal was about to end.","Guan Yan drank some wine that night and found it inconvenient to drive, so she slept in the guest room.","Gu San went to help her tidy up the room.","Qin Si couldn’t stay idle. After some fidgeting, he ran to help Gu San tidy up the room.","Only Guan Yan, Qiao Nian, Bo Jingxing, and the others were left at the table.","Bo Jingxing pushed his gold-rimmed glasses up his nose bridge and suddenly leaned back in his chair. \"Miss Qiao, do you know that Continent M proposed to cut off trade with Beijing this time?\"","Ye Wangchuan had gone to make ’hangover soup’ for Qiao Nian and was not there right now.","Qiao Nian held her wine glass and rubbed her fingers against the edge. Hearing this, she looked up in his direction. \"Just say what you want to say.\"","She did not like to beat around the bush.","\"Okay.\" Bo Jingxing roughly knew her personality, so he was not shy and looked at her directly. \"Continent M and the Ninth Branch have many chip and semiconductor cooperations. If they suddenly stop supplying, the Ninth Branch will be negatively affected. As one of the people in charge of the Ninth Branch, I want to ask if you have any solution...\"","Not waiting for Qiao Nian’s answer, he adjusted his glasses again. Under the light, his eyes behind the glasses were like a vixen, alert and clear.","\"I’m different from Wangchuan and Qin Si.","\"I don’t like to put my personal feelings into business. Perhaps my question might affect our relationship... However, not only do I have to be responsible for myself, but I also have to be responsible for the others in the Ninth Branch. Therefore, I have to ask you if you have a way to deal with it.","\"If not, be it as a friend or as a good friend of your boyfriend, I’ll think of another way to solve the current problem... Of course, the premise is that I have to figure out your next plan first.\"","Guan Yan was already half drunk. She could only see Bo Jingxing’s lips open and close as if he was saying something serious to Qiao Nian.","However, she had drunk too much. Bo Jingxing’s voice was like a mosquito buzzing in her ears, making her temples throb.","Guan Yan gulped down some water and pressed her fingers against her forehead. Unable to take it anymore, she stood up and said to them, \"I’ll go back to my room.\"","Then, she staggered to her feet and walked towards the guest room.","Qiao Nian heard Qin Si come out of the guest room and help her up, asking why she was not waiting downstairs obediently.","Relieved, she answered Bo Jingxing’s question wholeheartedly.","\"I don’t have a plan.\""]},{"number":3667,"title":"Chapter 3667: Master Wang Cooked \"Hangover Soup\"","paragraphs":["Bo Jingxing adjusted his glasses again and waited calmly for her to continue.","As expected, Qiao Nian frowned. Her beautiful and eye-catching face was clear as she sat up straight and placed her hand on the dining table. \"But if that day really comes, I’ll take responsibility.\"","Continent F had the strongest prowess, so it was the most convenient for her to do things there.","However, Continent F wasn’t good at researching chips and semiconductors, nor did they have these resources.","In this regard, besides Continent M, only the illegal zone could meet the conditions.","The illegal district wasn’t big. It wasn’t like Continent F, which had a lot of land and resources and could dig for gems. It was a rough place.","Due to geographical reasons, the illegal district preferred to develop high technology. Only technology did not need vast land to obtain enough tempting wealth.","Qiao Nian could guess that Bo Jingxing wanted her to help pull strings in the illegal district.","She wasn’t angry. \"I’ll help facilitate the collaboration between the Ninth Branch and the illegal district. Of course, you have to discuss the specific conditions yourselves.\"","Bo Jingxing raised the cup to cover his lips and smiled, his eyes bright. \"Thank you.\"","Qiao Nian wasn’t angry, but she felt that she was not on the same side as him. After nodding slightly, she stood up and turned to leave. \"Contact me when the time comes.\"","Bo Jingxing had long expected this outcome. He did not feel terrible. He watched the girl get up and leave. Then, he took off his glasses and rubbed his eyebrows.","He did not want to mention this either. However, as the person in charge of the Ninth Branch, he needed to ask clearly so that he could know what he should do next.","However, Bo Jingxing wasn’t worried that Ye Wangchuan would find out.","He knew that Qiao Nian wasn’t the kind of person who would gossip behind others’ backs. Only the two of them would know about this conversation.","**","In the kitchen.","Ye Wangchuan had just brought out the ’hangover soup’ when he saw Qiao Nian entering the living room.","He walked over with the steaming porcelain bowl, placed it on the table, then squatted down and asked softly, \"Why are you here? Are you feeling unwell?\"","Qiao Nian rarely touched alcohol. She had been forced to drink a lot by Guan Yan tonight, so her stomach was not very comfortable. However, she shook her head and looked a little tired. \"I’m fine.\"","Ye Wangchuan touched the girl’s forehead. It was cold. He frowned and handed her the warm soup. \"Sit up and drink this. It’s warm.\"","Qiao Nian was helped up by him and took a sip of the ’hangover soup’. The spicy soup entered her throat and rolled into her stomach, slightly relieving the spasming feeling.","Qiao Nian felt a little better, and her brows relaxed a little.","Ye Wangchuan supported her with one hand and fed her with the other. His actions were meticulous and gentle. \"Only you can make me serve you like this.\"","His tone was half-joking and half-teasing.","However, Qiao Nian was already a little drunk and did not have much strength left. She didn’t hear what he was saying clearly.","Ye Wangchuan looked at her obedient appearance as she lazily leaned against him and drank the soup. His thin lips curled up. \"I’ll send you back to your room to sleep later.\"","\"Mm.\" Qiao Nian narrowed her eyes as if she had heard him and replied vaguely.","Ye Wangchuan waited for her to finish most of the bowl until she was unwilling to drink anymore. Then, he placed the bowl on the table and helped her to her room.","...","On the second floor.","Qiao Nian’s room.","Ye Wangchuan placed Qiao Nian on the bed and tucked her in. Then, he went to the bathroom to wash a towel with cold water. He wrung it out and wiped the girl’s face.","Qiao Nian was not particularly drunk. She could feel the cold touch on her face, and it was quite comfortable to lower the temperature of her burning skin.","She raised her delicate and fair chin slightly and grabbed the man’s wrist before asking hoarsely, \"Ye Wangchuan?\""]},{"number":3668,"title":"Chapter 3668: So What Did She Do?","paragraphs":["\"Tsk.\" Someone chuckled in the darkness. His voice was very pleasant. \"How much did you drink? If I had known, I wouldn’t have let you touch the wine.\"","Qiao Nian was actually conscious. However, after talking to Bo Jingxing, her thinking abilities were impaired by the alcohol.","She could still hear his voice. It seemed helpless and doting.","Her eyes were extremely bright in the darkness, and she called out his name again in a low voice. \"Ye Wangchuan?\"","\"I’m here.\"","This time, the person in the darkness responded quickly.","Qiao Nian felt him pull her hand away. The cold towel brushed past her cheek, and he said with a smile, \"What a drunkard.\"","The cold touch left her face, and Qiao Nian vaguely heard him say, \"Wait for me. I’ll get another towel.\"","She didn’t know what was wrong with her heart, but she paused for half a second as if someone had knocked her silly. Then, Qiao Nian instinctively grabbed him, agilely pulled him onto the bed, flipped over, and half-knelt on it, squinting to see the person’s face.","\"Ye Wangchuan?\"","Silence.","Ye Wangchuan didn’t expect her to suddenly grab him and get him onto the bed. By the time he reacted, he could already feel her breath on his neck. The faint alcohol smell was not unpleasant, and the girl’s voice was hoarse as she called his name.","He believed that he had better self-control than ordinary people. At this moment, his breathing stopped for a second before subconsciously grabbing the girl’s wrist and saying in a clear and cold voice, \"Nian Nian, do you know what you’re doing?\"","After saying that, he couldn’t help but laugh in the dark.","Qiao Nian was obviously drunk.","He actually asked a drunk person if she knew what she was doing. This was a kind of mental confusion... Qiao Nian was clearly the one drunk. But why did it seem like he was also drunk?","He chuckled, about to get up and pull her up.","Unexpectedly, he heard Qiao Nian’s casual voice. \"I know. That’s why I’m asking if you’re him.\"","Ye Wangchuan stilled. In the darkness, he tried to see if she was drunk.","The next second, he felt the faint alcohol smell approaching him.","It sounded like a mutter and a promise.","\"I’ll take responsibility.\"","Silence.","In this world, only one person always said she was responsible for him.","She was the only one who said this seriously every time.","Ye Wangchuan could feel the self-control he was so proud of being shattered into countless pieces at this moment. He also let go of her wrist.","In the darkness, he was willing to submit to her.","**","Noon the next day.","Qiao Nian rubbed her eyes before getting up from the bed. She changed out of her wrinkled clothes before going to take a shower.","Warm water rushed down.","Fragments of memories flashed across her mind, but they quickly disappeared disconnectedly.","Qiao Nian’s mind was still sluggish. Not thinking too much about it, she finished showering and changed her clothes.","She had just walked to the head of the bed to grab her cell phone when she saw Qin Si’s message flashing on the screen.","She wondered why he sent her a message so early in the morning.","After reading the message, the corners of her mouth twitched. Her head hurt even more now, and she did not want to go downstairs to face the others.","This was because of the message’s content: [Qin Si: Sister Qiao, you’re awesome. What did you do to Master Wang last night? Master Wang’s lips have a bitten mark.]"]},{"number":3669,"title":"Chapter 3669: Master Wang’s Call","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian stared at the message. About to walk out, she suddenly slowed down.","A few blurry images appeared in her mind. They were not clear, but if she was not wrong, the bitten mark on Ye Wangchuan’s lips couldn’t possibly be from a second person.","So the culprit... was her!","Qiao Nian saw that Qin Si’s name on the dialog box had changed to [Typing]. She covered her eyes and turned back, not wanting to go downstairs.","At this moment, Ye Wangchuan called her.","Qiao Nian looked at the flashing caller ID on the screen and mentally prepared herself before slowly picking up the call. \"Hello.\"","\"You’re awake?\" The man’s voice was like a spring breeze. It was obvious that he was in a good mood.","Qiao Nian couldn’t bear to face him after what she did last night. She pulled out a chair and sat down, then lowered her eyes and coughed. \" Ahem , that.\"","\"Mm?\"","\"I was drunk yesterday.\"","After saying that, she felt like a scumbag who had abandoned him after having an affair.","Even as this thought flashed through her mind, she coughed and said seriously, \"But I admit to everything I did.\"","The man chuckled. \"Oh, so what did Goddess Qiao do last night?\"","His voice was still cold as ice. His tone was neither anxious nor impatient. It was as if he was waiting for her with ease.","Qiao Nian could hear the ridicule in his tone. The awkwardness caused by Qin Si’s WeChat message eased a lot.","She rubbed her eyebrows and suddenly said, \"Forget it.\"","Ye Wangchuan did not follow her thoughts. \"Huh? What?\"","Qiao Nian straightened up. She was wearing a thick knitted sweater for the past few days. The pattern was bright and clear, making her beautiful eyes stand out.","\"You’re my man. So what if I drank too much and kissed you? I did not touch anyone else. They can’t control me.\"","She was expressionless, but her aura was obvious.","Ye Wangchuan noticed the girl’s tone returned to normal. Although he was a little regretful that he could not tease her more, upon hearing Qiao Nian’s domineering announcement, his thin lips curved uncontrollably and he said calmly, \"Yes, you’re right.\"","**","In the living room downstairs.","Qin Si was still waiting for Qiao Nian to come down so he could gossip.","After waiting for a long time, she finally came downstairs. Just as he was about to open his mouth, he received a warning glare from Master Wang.","\"Yesterday, Auntie Qin called me again to ask when you’re going back.\"","Ye Wangchuan shook the glass calmly and glanced at him leisurely. \"When do you plan to leave? Do you want to go back with Bo?\"","\"Hehe.\" Qin Si wasn’t an idiot. He still had this kind of judgment.","He understood that Ye Wangchuan was warning him not to tease Qiao Nian. Although he was pouty, he understood the principle of being a coward when his weakness was in others’ hands.","\"Well, Master Wang, tell my Mom that I still have some matters to settle here. I’ll go back after some time.\"","\"But aren’t you free now?\"","\"I have something to do.\"","\"Oh?\"","Ye Wangchuan glanced at him again.","Qin Si immediately replied with a look that said \"I understand. I’ll shut up.\" Then, he obediently shut up.","Ye Wangchuan picked up his cell phone. \"This won’t happen again.\"","Qin Si watched as he urged him to go home. He weakly greeted Qiao Nian, who had just walked down the stairs. \"Good morning, Sister Qiao.\""]},{"number":3670,"title":"Chapter 3670: F*ck, You’re Not Planning to Take Responsibility?","paragraphs":["\"Good morning.\"","Qiao Nian went to the fridge and grabbed a bottle of ice water. She unscrewed the cap and was about to take a sip when someone took it away and replaced it with a bottle of warm milk.","Ye Wangchuan’s calm and gentle voice came from behind. \"You drank alcohol last night. Don’t drink ice in the morning. You’ll get a stomachache. I heated up milk for you. Drink this to warm your stomach.\"","Qiao Nian felt the warmth in her hand and raised her eyebrows. In the end, she did not say anything. She tore open the lid and drank it as she walked.","Guan Yan had just come out of the guest room and saw this scene.","She saw that the water in Sun’s hand had been snatched and he had stuffed a bottle of the detested milk into her hand. Sun was not angry and even drank it obediently.","She rubbed her eyes to make sure she was sober. Then, she walked to the sofa and teased them.","\"It’s so early in the morning and there’s already the sour smell of love. Tsk tsk, how enviable!\"","At this moment, Qin Si also poured her a glass of hot water and handed it over with a smile. \"If you’re envious, we can do it too.\"","Just as he leaned over, Guan Yan immediately slapped him away in disdain. \"Just talk. Don’t get so close. I’m not deaf yet. I can hear you loud and clear.\"","Qin Si was not angry. He handed her the glass and gestured for her to drink it.","Guan Yan felt awkward for two seconds and could not resist. She frowned at him before taking the glass of water. Then, she took a sip to hide her discomfort.","Why did she feel that Qin Si was getting more and more persistent, as if he had decided on her? He was getting further and further away from her original intention of parting on good terms after playing.","At this thought, Guan Yan immediately felt that it was troublesome. She glanced over with her peach-blossom eyes and said, \"Then... you’re not going back to Beijing?\"","Qin Si also happened to ask, \"How long are you planning to stay in the independent continent?\"","They spoke almost at the same time.","They looked at each other.","Qin Si was the first to react. His eyes burned. \"I told my family that I’ll stay for a while longer. I’ll leave when you leave.\"","Guan Yan’s throat seemed to be blocked by cotton. She frowned and wanted to say something, but did not know how to. \"You...\"","Qin Si: \"I what?\"","Guan Yan looked like she had seen a ghost. \"Don’t tell me you want me to take responsibility?\"","Qin Si was stunned for a moment before reacting. His gaze locked onto her, and his expression changed. \"You’re not going to take responsibility?\"","In the past, he was the only one who was not responsible for others.","In his words, he was young and rich, and his family background was prominent. He could play around, but why did he have to be tied down to a person’s future? Therefore, he did not reject girls, did not take responsibility, and did not get married.","Guan Yan felt a chill run down her spine. She immediately stood up and replied confidently, \"Of course not! Have you ever seen a scum lady take responsibility? If I take responsibility, can I still be considered a scum lady?\"","Qin Si stood up and grabbed her wrist, wishing he could strangle her. His eyes were red, but he could not say a word.","F*ck! Was he played for nothing?!","If word got out, he would be laughed at by Zhang Yang and the others!","Unexpectedly, Guan Yan was magnanimous upon seeing his resentful expression. She even blinked her beautiful peach-blossom eyes and almost repeated what he said in the past. \"Didn’t you know what kind of person I was from the beginning? I’m young, beautiful, and rich. My life is so long. Why should I be responsible for a man? Baby, you’re not pregnant with my child. Don’t make it sound like I’ve done something to you...\""]},{"number":3671,"title":"Chapter 3671: Bo Jingxing Returned to Beijing First","paragraphs":["\"You...\" Qin Si’s face was flushed. Angry, he grabbed her wrist and did not let go.","Guan Yan couldn’t escape. She turned to look for help and saw the girl sitting on the sofa, making small talk and drinking milk. She asked for help.","\"Boss...\"","Just as she spoke, Qiao Nian raised her eyes and gestured for her to stop, saying coldly, \"You can settle your own matters.\"","Guan Yan was silenced. She tried to shake off Qin Si’s grip and acted like a hooligan. \"I didn’t say I would take responsibility. If you want me to be responsible, then break up. I’m not responsible!\"","Qin Si was so angry that his lips trembled. He held onto her tightly and refused to let go. \"It’s not up to you!\"","Guan Yan was about to retort. Why is it not up to me?","Then, from the corner of her eye, she saw Bo Jingxing coming out of his room carrying a suitcase. She did not want everyone to know about this, so she could only swallow it unwillingly. \"I’ll speak to you another day.\"","\"Not any day. There’s no room for negotiation!\" Qin Si was unyielding.","Guan Yan held her breath again. She wondered if she should argue with him, but she endured it. \"Let go first. Your friend is out. He seems to be leaving.\"","Qin Si turned around and saw Bo Jingxing coming over. Although he did not look too good, he reluctantly let go of Guan Yan’s hand but did not allow her to get too far away from him.","Then, he greeted Bo Jingxing. \"What time is your flight?\"","Bo Jingxing saw them tugging at each other but did not ask about their private matters. He adjusted his glasses and said, \"Two hours later, at eleven.\"","Qin Si nodded. \"I’ll drive you.\"","He immediately thought of something and turned around. \"Sister Qiao, are you going?\"","Bo Jingxing did not expect him to ask Qiao Nian. It was too late to stop him. He was about to open his mouth to smooth things over. After all, what he had talked about last night was a little too much. Qiao Nian might not understand him.","Unexpectedly, before he could speak, the girl said nonchalantly, \"Anyway, I have nothing to do in the afternoon. Let’s go.\"","Bo Jingxing was stunned. He lowered his hand and looked at the girl in surprise. His voice was dry. \"There’s no need to go through so much trouble...\"","Qiao Nian had already finished her milk and placed the empty bottle on the coffee table. With one hand in her pocket, she looked up at him. Her eyes were clear and bright, arrogant but not cold. \"Aren’t you returning? Coincidentally, I have a few things I want you to bring to my family.\"","Bo Jingxing paused for a few seconds before nodding. \"Okay.\"","\"Wait. I’ll go get it.\" Qiao Nian went upstairs.","Bo Jingxing looked at her back view before lowering his head and pressing his eyebrows. Then, he laughed and shook his head.","Qiao Nian did not say anything or mention anything. Her attitude was the same as before. However, he felt that he was in the wrong.","At least, in style and demeanor, he was not as carefree and calm as a girl who had just turned 20.","**","Bo Jingxing was on a private plane to Beijing. There was no need for special security checks.","However, because of the flight route, he still needed to go to the airport.","Qiao Nian and the others sent him to the plane and watched as the plane taxied and took off on the runway, soaring into the sky. They only returned to the villa after it disappeared from their view.","With Bo Jingxing gone, the villa should have been quieter with one less person.","However, because Guan Yan and Gu San were both there, Qiao Nian did not feel peaceful at all."]},{"number":3672,"title":"Chapter 3672: Public Display of Affection","paragraphs":["On the contrary, because Qin Si and Guan Yan seemed to be each other’s nemesis, they quarreled all the way back. It was so noisy that her head hurt. It was as if there were 500 ducks.","Fortunately, they restrained themselves upon getting home and reached a temporary agreement.","Even if Guan Yan had to move here during this period of time, the matter of her staying in the guest room and returning to Beijing with Qin Si would not be discussed for now.","Qiao Nian went to the First Research Institute in the afternoon to look for Feng Yu to search for information about the Di family from 40 years ago.","But she found nothing.","Most of the files in the First Research Institute were related to research. There were also some members’ information and news reports.","However, the First Research Institute was not an intelligence agency. It had existed for a long time, and it was difficult to tamper with the archives.","However, finding information about a person who had nothing to do with the First Research Institute was undoubtedly like finding a needle in a haystack.","Qiao Nian had already expected that she might not be able to find any useful information, so she was not disappointed.","After leaving the First Research Institute, she went to the hospital to visit Zhong Yiliu and asked about Ji Lingfeng’s recovery.","Ji Lingfeng regained consciousness but could not part with the ventilator for the time being. He couldn’t talk for long periods and was relatively weak.","In the end, Qiao Nian did not go to the ward to see him, nor did she disturb Ji Nan and Xie Yun. She quietly left the hospital.","The lights of the independent continent had just lit up.","Qiao Nian finally returned home after running around for the entire day.","She had just untied her scarf and before she could relax, she saw Gu San rushing over to welcome her.","\"Miss Qiao, something happened in Beijing.\"","Silence.","Qiao Nian’s thoughts were half a beat slower, and her hands slowed. She tilted her head and narrowed her dark eyes as if digesting his words.","Gu San was anxious and, upon seeing this, he did not have time to explain much to her. \"Elder Ye video called. Master Wang is talking with him. Do you want to go over and participate?\"","\"Okay.\" Qiao Nian returned to her senses. She took off her scarf expressionlessly and placed it on the cabinet before striding in.","She had already guessed what had happened.","Hence, she was not surprised when she saw Ye Maoshan, Jiang Weishang, someone from the Wei family, and someone from the Wen family on the screen.","Qiao Nian calmly walked to Ye Wangchuan’s side. \"Did Nie Qingru make a move?\"","Ye Wangchuan turned around and saw the girl standing half a step away. Her eyes were cold, and so was her face. She looked like she had just returned from outside. Her sweater was still stained with the cold outside.","He pulled her over and covered her hand. His voice was gentle. \"Is it cold outside?\"","He did not care that the people in the video call could see it. All he could see was Qiao Nian.","Qiao Nian’s slightly cold fingers warmed up. He even carefully rubbed them gently to warm them up. That feeling not only melted the coldness, but it also melted the violent and irritable emotions rising in her heart...","Qiao Nian watched as Ye Maoshan coughed and pretended not to see it. She quietly struggled and lowered her voice. \"Let’s get down to business.\"","Ye Wangchuan glanced at her with a faint smile. \"You’re the business. Nothing’s more important than you.\" His leisurely tone seemed neither fast nor slow, as if he could carry the sky even if it collapsed."]},{"number":3673,"title":"Chapter 3673: Nie Qingru Really Went After Beijing","paragraphs":["There were so many people watching. Qiao Nian wanted to respond, but the others were watching. She did not have such a hobby.","She pushed him away and sat down. Her beautiful eyes looked at the big shots from Beijing on the screen and seriously asked, \"Elder Ye, did something happen over there?\"","Ye Maoshan covered up his dry cough and avoided eye contact. \" Ahem . Something indeed happened, but it’s not a big deal.\"","He tried to comfort her, but Qiao Nian was not a fool. So many people couldn’t be in this video for a small matter.","She pursed her lips and looked indifferent, as if she knew something. \"Just tell me. I’m mentally prepared.\"","\"Well...\"","Ye Maoshan hesitated as he looked at the young man behind her, as if asking for Ye Wangchuan’s opinion.","Ye Wangchuan had previously mentioned the complicated relationship between Qiao Nian and Nie Qingru. Now that he saw the old man at home looking over, he smiled slightly and said, \"Grandpa, you can say it.\"","Ye Maoshan sighed heavily before looking at the girl. \"I originally planned to hide it from you... But since it has already happened, I can’t hide it from you anymore.\"","\"Please go ahead.\" Qiao Nian sat up straight.","Ye Maoshan looked at her with a complicated gaze. After a while, he said, \"You should have guessed that Continent M has stopped trading with Beijing.","\"We only received this news today. Both sides haven’t officially discussed it. We also received the news in advance and gathered to discuss countermeasures. If nothing goes wrong, after this news is officially leaked tomorrow, we still have to talk to Continent M...\"","Ye Maoshan spoke calmly as if there was still room for negotiation, but everyone present knew that even if they talked to the other party, the outcome would not be optimistic.","After all, those from the Continent M were not to be trifled with. Since the news had already spread, it meant they had already discussed it.","It was very difficult for Beijing to reverse the other party’s decision.","The \"talk\" was more like a show for both parties to not make things too ugly.","\"I asked Wangchuan if he had any good countermeasures. I don’t mean anything else...\"","Qiao Nian’s eyes darkened. She pursed her lips and thought for a moment before saying, \"I have a few ways in the illegal district.\"","\"You mean Tian Chen?\" Ye Maoshan had already thought of this. His expression was solemn. \"To be honest, I’ve talked to the person in charge of Tian Chen in Beijing. They might not be willing to get involved in this mess.\"","Anyone with eyes could tell that Nie Qingru and the reclusive families were putting pressure on Beijing this time. They even wanted to slap Beijing.","Under such circumstances, any force that did not want trouble was unwilling to cooperate with Beijing... Tian Chen was located in the illegal district and had close relations with Continent M. Naturally, they were unwilling to get involved in this mess.","Qiao Nian shook her head. \"It’s not Tian Chen.\"","She had never thought of asking Lu Zhi for help.","\"I’m talking about a few companies in the black market that use high-end technology components in the illegal district. They have a lot of stockpiles that can support Beijing’s demand for such consumables during this period. I can get this batch of stockpiles!\"","Ye Maoshan did not expect Qiao Nian to really have a way. He immediately thought about the feasibility of the matter and felt that it would work. He couldn’t hide his joy. He stood up and took two steps before hesitantly saying, \"I heard that there are rules in the illegal district that forbid foreign companies from buying components.\""]},{"number":3674,"title":"Chapter 3674: Old Master Jiang Discovered Sister Nian’s and Master Wang’s Identities","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian nodded and straightforwardly said, \"That’s why I plan to buy it in the Red Alliance’s name. Then, I’ll get someone to transport the goods to Beijing by sea.\"","Ye Maoshan almost said, \"This is a good idea!\"","What he was most worried about was that these high-tech components were not easy to obtain. For everything else, what Beijing had domestically was not bad either. It was undoubtedly a dream for Continent M to rely on anything else to restrain Beijing’s development.","\"Rare earth...\" Ye Maoshan started.","Except for the chip components, another thing he could not let go of was the rare earth resources needed for aerospace materials.","Unexpectedly, just as he started, the young brat continued unhurriedly, \"I have a few mines, we can ship them over from Continent F.\"","When he casually said, \"I have a few mines\", not to mention Old Master Ye, even the people from the Wen and Wei families were dumbfounded.","Among them, Jiang Weishang was probably the one who suffered the greatest impact.","Jiang Weishang was asked by Old Master Ye to participate in this call. Before Qiao Nian came, he was also confused. He only knew that Continent M was coming aggressively this time. He was originally worried.","Unexpectedly, what Qiao Nian and Ye Wangchuan said made him forget his worries. He only remembered Qiao Nian saying, \"I know a few companies in the black market.\" And then Ye Wangchuan said, \"I have a few mines.\"","Jiang Weishang had always vaguely felt that Qiao Nian was not as simple as she looked on the surface but never thought that someone who had just entered university would know people in the illegal district or the black market.","Moreover, judging from his old friend’s attitude, he seemed to have known about it.","For a moment, Jiang Weishang did not know if he should be shocked, angry, or if a more complicated emotion lingered in his heart.","He couldn’t even blame Qiao Nian for hiding it from him.","Ye Maoshan discussed the specific ways with Qiao Nian and the others before cutting off the video signal. Only then did he notice his especially silent friend.","He remembered that he was the one who insisted on dragging Jiang Weishang to participate in this video call. He couldn’t help but ask with concern, \"Weishang, are you alright?\"","Jiang Weishang was sitting in a wheelchair. His white hair was combed neatly, revealing a serious face.","Hearing this, he forced a smile and shook his head. \"I’m fine.\"","Ye Maoshan wanted to say something but hesitated. \"Are you angry that Nian Nian...\"","Jiang Weishang immediately interrupted him. \"I’m not angry.\"","Ye Maoshan stared at him, not knowing what to say.","Jiang Weishang let out a shaky breath. After calming down, he looked at him and said bitterly, \"Really, I’m not angry. That child did not deliberately hide it from me. The small pills she brought me previously... I should have guessed it. It’s just that I’ve always been unwilling to think in that direction.","\"She’s just a 20-year-old child. Where would she come into contact with those places in the illegal district... I only need to think to know that it’s because we were absent for 18 years. When I think of this, my heart feels like it’s being stabbed. What right do I have to be angry with her?","\"I’m just angry at myself for not being able to protect my granddaughter and making her suffer in her young age!\"","Ye Maoshan wanted to pat his shoulder, but he couldn’t do anything through the video call. He could only comfort him in a low voice. \"Don’t overthink. There’s still a long way to go. As long as we treat Nian Nian well from now on, one day, we can smooth over the bad things she experienced in the past.\"","\"I know.\" Jiang Weishang composed himself but couldn’t just forget about this impact. Then, he reluctantly said, \"I’ll hang up first.\""]},{"number":3675,"title":"Chapter 3675: I Just Didn’t Expect Her to Care About Someone","paragraphs":["\"Okay.\"","Jiang Weishang really didn’t know what to say. He hung up the video call with a heavy heart. When the nurse came over to wheel him for rehabilitation treatment, he was distracted.","At this moment, his cell phone vibrated and lit up to show Qiao Nian’s message.","Jiang Weishang grabbed his cell phone and quickly turned it on. Then, he read the message.","[Q: I didn’t say those things before not because I didn’t want to tell you, but because I didn’t know how to bring it up. I’m sorry.]","Jiang Weishang looked at his granddaughter’s message. What else could he not understand? He asked the nurse to stop and solemnly typed a reply. He reminded Qiao Nian to be careful outside and not worry about him. He would take good care of himself. Also, Beijing would do its best. He did not want her to force herself to solve the problem.","After successfully sending the message, he quickly received Qiao Nian’s reply.","Jiang Weishang was suddenly enlightened.","He gathered his emotions and thought about it. Then, he thought of his eldest son, who knew nothing, and his youngest son, who was a disappointment and could not be a good uncle.","The more Old Master Jiang thought about it, the angrier he became. He decided to make a call.","He gave Jiang Zongnan a harsh scolding first.","Then, he called Jiang Zongjin’s company and scolded him. His clueless sons were confused. Old Master Jiang finally felt much better and followed the nurse for rehabilitation.","He finally understood.","The Ye family was right.","He still had to take good care of his body. As long as he was alive, he could help take care of Nian Nian when she got married and had children in the future.","Otherwise, what could those troublesome kids at home do?","As Old Master Jiang thought about this, he recalled the wedding venue and ceremony that Ye Maoshan had talked to him about.","Jiang Weishang wasn’t in a hurry. Qiao Nian was still young, and he was not willing to let her get married so early.","He had changed his mind.","Nian Nian said that she was in the country.","However, seeing the background, they did not appear to be in Rao City. In addition, Ye Wangchuan was also there... Old Master Jiang felt that he had to put the wedding on the agenda.","Since he wanted to bring this up, he would not let his granddaughter suffer.","It was not about the money.","But his granddaughter must have the best wedding!","With this thought in mind, Old Master Jiang called the Ye family and arranged to meet in a few days to discuss the wedding.","**","Qiao Nian did not know that her grandfather was already planning her wedding.","After hanging up the video call with Beijing, she relaxed and leaned against the sofa. She rubbed her swollen temples and asked hoarsely, \"Is Nie Qingru crazy?\"","Beijing wouldn’t be the only one to suffer a loss if they cut off their trade project. Continent M would also have to pay a considerable price.","Nie Qingru had never done business at a loss, but this time, she was not very rational.","\"Her reaction can only mean that our previous guess was right. The thing you took from the vault is very important to her. It’s far more important than all your previous conflicts. It’s enough to provoke her into losing her mind...\" Ye Wangchuan walked over and touched her forehead with his slender fingertips. He gently pressed her acupoints. His technique was much better than Qiao Nian’s.","Qiao Nian relaxed and allowed the faint mint fragrance on his body to surround her. Her sharp eyes relaxed, and her tone was casual. \"I just didn’t expect her to care about someone.\""]},{"number":3676,"title":"Chapter 3676: This Is Not a Game That the Reclusive Families Can End Just Because They Want To","paragraphs":["This made her feel even worse than if Nie Qingru did not care about anyone.","A person who did not even care about her blood-related daughter cared about someone else. How ridiculous!","\"I’ve never felt that it’s unforgivable that she doesn’t love her daughter. Many parents in this world don’t love their children. I just can’t accept that she can kill them just because she doesn’t love them...\"","\"It’s meaningless to think about this. It doesn’t matter what she thinks. You just have to do what you think is right.\" Ye Wangchuan gently massaged her temples. From his angle, he could see the girl’s lowered eyelashes and the blood in the depths of her eyes.","Qiao Nian was very frustrated.","At the very least, she was irritable and chaotic at this moment.","\"The reclusive families want to show everyone their strength is still there. I’ve implicated... Beijing.\"","At this moment, Ye Wangchuan stopped massaging her temples and walked to her front. His eyes were frivolous and unrestrained, emitting a lazy and noble aura. \"It’s only a matter of time before this would have happened.\"","Qiao Nian watched him sit down.","\"Beijing has been doing chip research. Qing University’s research team has made a huge breakthrough in recent years, and the Ninth Branch has made a lot of progress in the aerospace industry... These are all areas that the reclusive families want to control. This time, rather than saying that they are taking revenge on you, it’s better to say that the Privy Council have its own considerations. They allowed Nie Qingru to act this way not only for her personal grudges but also to block the Ninth Branch and Qing University’s research teams...","\"And we’re going to have to deal with that sooner or later. What difference does it make if we do it sooner or later?\"","Ye Wangchuan picked up the apple and knife on the table and peeled it at a moderate speed. The knife obediently spun the apple skin, making the action aesthetically pleasing. His muscles and bones were well-defined, and his knuckles were long. A simple peeling action had a pleasing beauty.","It was like a movie scene.","Qiao Nian slowly calmed down under his unhurried actions. \"I’m still investigating the secrets in the USB drive Ji Qing left behind.","\"When I solve the last problem, I’ll know why those people wanted her dead...\" Qiao Nian’s voice was very soft.","She knew that once she grasped the last secret of the USB drive Ji Qing left behind, those people would swarm her like locusts, just like how they went after Ji Qing back then.","She wanted to see who those people were and what they were really after...","Ye Wangchuan finished peeling the apple and handed her the clean fruit. \"Eat it.\"","Qiao Nian looked at the apple, and her convoluted emotions disappeared.","Slowly taking the apple and taking a bite, she relaxed and returned to her usual self.","\"We’ll see.\"","These words seemed to be directed at Ye Wangchuan, but also at herself.","She wasn’t someone who liked to worry about things that had not happened yet. She would talk about it when it happened in the future.","The most important thing for her now was to solve the problem at hand.","Continent M wanted to use this opportunity to teach Beijing a lesson for others to see. She also wanted to see how long the reclusive families could last.","This was not a game where one side crushed the other.","As long as they solved the chip and the rare earth problem, they would return to the starting line.","The losers and winners... were not decided yet!","At the very least, this was not a game that could end just because they wanted to."]},{"number":3677,"title":"Chapter 3677: Things Are Indeed Going as Sister Nian Expected","paragraphs":["The next day.","Qiao Nian contacted a few people in the illegal district with chips and components in stock. After discussing the price and conditions, both parties reached a deal.","Then, she immediately asked Slim Waist Control to go get the goods. She planned for him to personally escort them to Beijing by sea.","Just in case, Qiao Nian contacted David and asked him to clear the way to ensure that nothing would go wrong on the way.","...","At the same time.","In the other room.","Ye Wangchuan was doing the same thing as her.","\"Ask Mo Xi to personally bring the goods from Continent F.\"","\"Okay.\"","\"Also, tell Cage to help again...\" Ye Wangchuan gave a concise explanation.","Mo Dong noted it down. \"Master Wang, is there a need for us to be so careful? I think the reclusive families might not know.\"","Ye Wangchuan did not comment. \"It’s best to be careful.\"","At her craziest, Nie Qingru sent pirates on the high seas to sink Cage’s ship.","Everyone knew the reason for her actions, but Nie Qingru’s disrespectfulness still angered this weapon tycoon who ran amok in Continent F.","If he went to the other party for help at this time, this big boss must have no reason to refuse.","Mo Dong was silent for a second. After thinking it through, he exhaled. \"Alright, I’ll follow your instructions and talk to Mr. Cage.\"","**","In fact, Ye Wangchuan only asked Mo Dong to look for Cage to help escort the rare earths from Continent F to Beijing.","This was just a small favor.","With their friendship, Cage wouldn’t have rejected this request even if Nie Qingru had not tried to sink his ship.","Qiao Nian and Ye Wangchuan arranged for the goods to be transported to Beijing in the safest way.","However, the outside world did not think so.","Just as Cage and David set off to escort the ship, the outside world was already in chaos.","The major forces of the few continents had received news of the abnormal movements in Continent F.","Continent F’s two biggest bosses came out at the same time.","...","Similar news spread like snowflakes to all the major factions and organizations.","Forget about David.","He ran the diamond business all year round and would show his face in public from time to time. Even Old Master Ye, who had taken a back seat, knew of his existence.","Most people were not too surprised that he had left the country. They thought he was just doing normal business.","But Cage was different!","He was also one of the big bosses in Continent F.","Cage’s business was much more single-minded.","He never did side jobs.","He only dealt in one business—weapons and weapons-related stuff.","Such a dangerous personrarely left Continent F. There was pitifully little news about him. This time, he was actually personally escorting a ship.","Besides the major factions being unable to figure out what he was trying to do, even the pirates on the high seas were trembling in fear. They were determined not to go out and wander around, afraid that they would be unlucky and bump into either of them, bringing about a fatal disaster.","...","Continuous news came from the sea surrounding Continent F.","The atmosphere in Beijing was also tense.","Last night, after Ye Maoshan and the others received the news, they discussed how to deal with it.","The next morning, as they had expected, Continent M publicly requested to stop the important cooperation project.","Continent M’s envoy was determined.","Ye Maoshan suppressed his anger and talked to a few people. The result was as they had predicted last night.","The other party refused to relent and acted arrogantly!","Ye Maoshan had never been one to swallow his anger. Both parties ended their discussion on the spot and parted on bad terms."]},{"number":3678,"title":"Chapter 3678: Why Did Guan Yan Go to the Independent Continent?","paragraphs":["He even said that until their attitude changed, Continent M would not change their decision.","Ye Maoshan was angered by the other party’s arrogance.","However, he video-called Qiao Nian and Ye Wangchuan yesterday. He already knew about the situation and decided not to argue with them. He stood up and left.","\"Let’s go!\"","After leaving with his men, he immediately went to the Ninth Branch to find Bo Jingxing.","Bo Jingxing had just returned from the independent continent, having slept for over 10 hours on the plane. After arriving at the airport, he hurriedly went home to shower and change his clothes. He didn’t even have time to relax before rushing to the Ninth Branch to comfort the others.","When Ye Maoshan found him, he had just finished making arrangements.","His handsome face was visibly exhausted, but he still greeted Ye Maoshan politely and respectfully, \"Elder Ye, you’re here.\"","Ye Maoshan: \"Mm.\"","\"Sit. I’ll ask someone to make tea.\"","Bo Jingxing invited Ye Maoshan to sit down and asked someone to bring tea in.","Soon, a staff member came in with a cup of Maojian tea.","The tea was this year’s new tea, but the tea leaves were definitely not as good as the ones at Ye Maoshan’s house. The Ninth Branch’s new tea leaves were slightly better than ordinary tea leaves.","Ye Maoshan took a sip before putting it down. Then, he went straight to the point. \"Our negotiation with Continent M has failed. How long can the components last?\"","Bo Jingxing looked up, his eyes beautiful behind his glasses. \"10 days.\"","\"Yes.\" Ye Maoshan frowned. It wasn’t too much, but it was not too little either. \"That should be fine.\"","Bo Jingxing still didn’t know that they had video-called Qiao Nian. He opened his mouth but did not have time to ask.","Ye Maoshan took the initiative to tell him, \"Nian Nian said she has a way to get the chip components. On the way here, I received a call from her saying that they are already on the way. The goods will arrive by water in a few days.\"","Bo Jingxing gently closed his mouth and looked at him. \"It’s... Tian Chen?\"","Ye Maoshan shook his head. \"No.\"","He did not say where the goods came from, mainly because he did not know which companies in the illegal district Qiao Nian made a deal with.","Ye Maoshan continued, \"Anyway, you don’t have to worry about the chip components. About rare earths the Ninth Branch needs. Wangchuan is also looking for someone to send them over.\"","Bo Jingxing’s back, tense for the entire day, finally relaxed. He adjusted his glasses and smiled. \"That’s good.\"","Ye Maoshan glanced at him and did not hide it from him. \"In the future, you’ll be in charge of the Ninth Branch. I’ll communicate with you in advance if I have any news.\"","\"Okay.\"","Ye Maoshan took another sip of tea. His tone was calm and dignified. \"We can’t be held by the neck forever. We have to fight them to the end in this ’battle’! Be mentally prepared.\"","Bo Jingxing’s heart suddenly burned with passion, and his mood surged. He nodded heavily, his expression extremely serious. \"Yes, Elder Ye.\"","**","On the route of the boundless sea.","David was on the phone. \"Don’t worry, boss. It’ll be delivered the day after tomorrow at most! We’ll be there tomorrow night if there’s no storm on the sea.\"","\"Just hand it to them when you reach the meeting place. There’s no need to go ashore.\" The girl on the other end of the call sounded young, no more than 20 years old. It was Qiao Nian.","David rubbed the bridge of his nose good-naturedly. \"I know... By the way, I heard that Guan Yan is with you. Why did she go to the independent continent?\""]},{"number":3679,"title":"Chapter 3679: Only Found Out What Sister Nian Was Giving Her","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian was getting water in the living room. Hearing this, she turned around and looked at the people in the living room before humming and saying, \"... She came to play.\"","\"Tsk, that’s not what Slim Waist Control said. Slim Waist Control said that she provoked a good man, and he wants her to take responsibility...\" David was very interested in gossip.","Qiao Nian wasn’t a gossipy person. She said bluntly, \"I’m hanging up.\"","\"Hey, don’t. Boss—\" Dave still wanted to ask for more gossip about Guan Yan, but the other party hung up without giving him any face.","He listened to the static sound from the earpiece and smiled as he turned around to enter the cabin.","At this moment, a man with a scar on his face walked over.","\"David, there’s something wrong in Continent F.\"","\"What?\"","\"It’s said that Cage’s people are also going to Beijing. We might bump into them on the way.\"","\"That’s what you meant?\" David waved his hand. \"Don’t worry about it. He has the same goal as us! Just say hi if you see him.\"","What?","Scarface scratched his head and watched him leave. After a while, he returned to his senses and followed him, asking himself when they became familiar with Cage’s people...","...","Time ticked by.","The sea weather for the past two days was unexpectedly good. The sky was clear and there were no dark clouds.","They did not encounter any storms.","David’s ship rushed towards Beijing at full speed. It only took them a day and a half to reach the edge of the Y Sea.","On the other side.","The reclusive families in Continent M, thousands of miles away, finally found out why David and Cage were heading towards Beijing at the same time.","The Privy Council’s Council Hall was brightly lit tonight.","Elder Xue rushed over the moment he received the news and was the first to arrive.","Right after, the Leonard family from the radical faction also arrived.","Archbishop Quentin was the last to arrive.","The heads of the three factions had all arrived at the council hall, so Nie Qingru naturally would not be absent. About five minutes after Quentin arrived, she pushed open the door and entered the council hall.","The Privy Council was the heart of the reclusive families.","Even Nie Qingru only complemented it.","After she entered the parliament hall, everyone in the circular staircase-like conference hall respectfully stood up and greeted her according to the rules.","\"Empress.\"","\"Your Majesty.\"","Wherever she passed by, people would immediately lower their heads in greeting.","This was originally Nie Qingru’s favorite scene. Unfortunately, she was no longer in the mood to enjoy this glory.","She walked on the expensive Persian carpet to her exclusive seat and sat down. Then, she smoothed her shawl and nodded slightly like a proud Phoenix. \"Everyone, sit down.\"","The dozens of people in the large parliament hall sat down majestically.","Nie Qingru sat at the head of the table. To show off her noble status and unique identity, there were no seats right next to her.","On the left below her was Quentin, wearing a bright red church robe, and on the right was Elder Xue, dressed in a simple old-fashioned Chinese tunic.","Below them were the people from the Leonard family.","Every position was strictly ranked according to status. The rules were strict, and it was difficult to break through the hierarchy barrier.","Nie Qingru watched as everyone sat down before unhurriedly saying, \"I’m here today to discuss Beijing with everyone. I believe everyone has already received the news from Continent F. I wonder what everyone has planned? Tell me.\""]},{"number":3680,"title":"Chapter 3680: The Problem Returns to Her","paragraphs":["As she spoke, her dignified and sharp gaze swept across everyone present.","However, Quentin nonchalantly drank his black tea as if he was there just to make up the numbers.","Those from the Leonard family avoided her gaze and did not intend to interfere.","Among the three giants present, only Elder Xue, on her right, took a deep breath and asked worriedly, \"Empress, what do you want to do?\"","Nie Qingru saw the situation clearly and clenched her fists tightly. The veins on the back of her hand bulged. However, she did not show it on her face. \"My idea is very simple. Stop them midway before they get to Beijing!\"","But as soon as she finished speaking, Quentin put down his teacup and mocked, \"I’m afraid it’s not that simple, right?\"","Nie Qingru looked at him unhappily. \"What do you mean, Archbishop?\"","Quentin had always been at odds with her, and he now spoke at a moderate pace. \"We all know that David and Cage are in charge of transporting the chips and rare earths, respectively. Neither of them are the simple characters you’re making them out to be. Stop them just like that? That’s too simplistic.\"","He did not give Nie Qingru any face and said directly, \"If the other party starts a conflict with us, should we stop them or retreat? If we want to stop them at all costs, is the Empress prepared to fall out with Continent F and Beijing? We need to rely on Cage’s power to cooperate with many minerals and weapons in Continent F. What’s your plan after we fall out with him?\"","He asked several questions in a row, each of which accurately hit Nie Qingru’s weak spot. At the same time, he reminded the others in the Privy Council of how stupid Nie Qingru’s idea was...","Whispers could be heard all around.","Nie Qingru’s breathing became heavier and heavier the more Quentin spoke, and the way she looked at him was as if she wanted to skin him alive. \"...What the Archbishop said makes sense.\"","In the end, she was still able to keep her composure.","After a short setback, she immediately knew how to control the Privy Council. \"But Archbishop, don’t forget that I’m not only doing this for personal grudges but also for the reclusive families’ prestige. Don’t say that it has nothing to do with you. You don’t care about failure at all.\"","The reason why Nie Qingru was able to persuade them to stop the important collaboration with Beijing this time was because she paid a high price.","For example, Smith Bank had taken the risk to ban trade transactions with Beijing.","Hence, she reminded Quentin indifferently. She was also warning him to stop while he was ahead.","As expected, Quentin straightened his expression. \"I’m just voicing my concerns.\"","\"It’s good that the Archbishop has concerns, but don’t scare yourself and boost others’ prestige.\" Nie Qingru ignored him after saying that. She turned to Elder Xue. \"There’s something I don’t understand. It’s not surprising that they can find rare earths in Continent F. But how did they bypass Tian Chen to find chip components in the illegal district?\"","She had a plot in Tian Chen, just waiting for Qiao Nian to ask Lu Zhi for help.","She had a way to force him not to help her.","Originally, everything was going according to her plan. Who would have thought that Qiao Nian would not take the ordinary path at all? She had never thought of obtaining the chip components through Tian Chen, but she still got them.","This was not part of Nie Qingru’s plan.","This accident was enough to catch her off guard.","She knew well that only two things could restrain Beijing and force it to lower its head—rare earths and chip components.","Qiao Nian countered her and returned the problem to her."]},{"number":3681,"title":"Chapter 3681: Go By Yourself, We Won’t Partake","paragraphs":["Nie Qingru frowned. \"We can’t just watch them get the chip components and rare earths. Stopping the ship is our only way now.\"","\"I don’t agree. If you decide to stop the ship, our church won’t participate in this operation.\" Quentin’s attitude was still the same.","Nie Qingru raised her eyebrows in anger and said gloomily, \"Archbishop, what kind of attitude is this? Isn’t the church not a member of the reclusive families?\"","Quentin tidied his robes and looked at her calmly. \"Of course, the church is a member of the reclusive families.","\"However, Empress, don’t forget that the reclusive families are gathered together for the common benefit of everyone.","\"I can’t see the benefits behind your suggestion to stop the ships of Continent F’s two big bosses. As the head of the church, I must choose to refuse to cooperate.\"","Nie Qingru couldn’t suppress her anger. She slammed the table hard, her eyes slightly cold. \"I gather you don’t want to be enemies with Qiao Nian!\"","Quentin looked at her neither too fast nor too slow. \"Empress, watch your words.\"","Nie Qingru said in a fit of anger, \"Am I not telling the truth? I’ve long heard that you have a good relationship with Qiao Nian. You also know the Young Master Ye beside her, right? I also heard that you have an illegitimate son who lives in the independent continent—\"","\"That’s enough.\" Quentin listened gracefully at first, but upon hearing the last bit, he suddenly waved his hand, stood up, and said to the woman sitting at the head of the table impolitely, \"If the Empress asked me to come to discuss my private life, then there’s nothing to talk about!","\"Everyone, I’ll leave first.\" He turned around and left expressionlessly.","This action shocked everyone in the council hall. As Quentin walked away with his head held high, the neutral party members looked at each other before standing up, taking their things, and moving to leave.","The Privy Council was in an uproar.","Seeing that the situation was about to go out of control, Elder Xue hurriedly stood up to stop the Archbishop.","\"Archbishop, the Empress didn’t do it on purpose. Her intentions are for the reclusive families’ sake. Perhaps there were some emotional factors when she spoke, you—\"","\"I don’t have any other intentions. I’m not feeling well and can’t participate in the meeting. You guys take your time to chat.\"","Quentin bypassed him and walked away without looking back.","With a flash of red, he pushed open the door and left the council hall.","The other Neutral Faction members were no longer afraid and found excuses to leave.","In the blink of an eye, one-third of the seats in the large council hall were empty. Even the remaining two-thirds were unable to sit still and wanted to leave.","No one had expected things to develop to this extent!","Nie Qingru’s face was ashen. Her hands gripped the armrests tightly, her nails digging into the fluffy cushion.","She tried to make herself look calm, but her ferocious expression gave her away.","Nie Qingru did not expect the archbishop to be so disrespectful just because she mentioned an illegitimate child.","This had never happened in the Privy Council’s decades of history.","Since it had already happened, as one of the parties involved, Nie Qingru could only grit her teeth and endure it coldly. \"Let’s continue the topic.\"","Elder Xue was unable to stop the archbishop from leaving and could only return to his seat resentfully.","Nie Qingru was still bent on stopping the ships. \"The church won’t participate, what about you? You won’t participate either? We definitely can’t let those things reach Beijing.\""]},{"number":3682,"title":"Chapter 3682: The Reclusive Families Have Missed the Best Time","paragraphs":["Elder Xue felt a headache coming on. He looked over and saw that, though the Leonard family did not leave, their nonchalant attitude already showed their stand...","Therefore, only he and Nie Qingru discussed this matter in the huge parliament hall.","He pressed his hand against his forehead and had no choice but to stop her. \"Empress, we can’t offend two big bosses of Continent F.\"","\"What do you mean?\" Nie Qingru was extremely displeased.","Elder Xue did not care if she was happy or not. He looked into her eyes and said solemnly, \"We also have a lot of cooperation with Continent F. In addition, Cage has previously expressed dissatisfaction because of what happened on the high seas. If we stop his ship again this time... Cage will definitely fall out with us.\"","\"Are we really afraid...\" Nie Qingru frowned.","Elder Xue did not wait for her to finish. \"Empress! This is not a matter of fear. The reclusive families have been passed down until now, and we are not afraid of any faction. However, you have to be clear that we also need to cooperate with external factions!","\"I know you don’t care about offending David, and I don’t care either.\" He softened his tone. \"Because I know that the person behind David is Qiao Nian. We’ve already reached a point of no return with her.\"","Elder Xue raised his voice and emphasized, \"But we have no choice but to be wary of Cage... Most of our cooperation with Continent F is through this arms dealer. We already have a feud with the other party. If we fall out with him over this matter, the losses will be too great. Even our reclusive families can’t afford so many losses... Therefore, the outcome of this matter has already been decided from the moment Qiao Nian persuaded Cage to escort the supplies!\"","He would agree with Nie Qingru’s decision if it was just David’s ship.","However, Qiao Nian had involved Cage. This was not as simple as a conflict between the two sides. There was also a third party involved.","This big boss of Continent F was famous for his bad temper.","Previously, they had already caused an extremely unpleasant scene in the open sea. The other party did not cause a scene because they were the reclusive families.","However, it was hard to say what would happen if they messed with him again.","Old Xue said, \"Empress, you have to look at the big picture!\"","He actually meant for her to watch how she was being slapped in the face!","Nie Qingru’s chest was heaving up and down as she tried to control her emotions, but the corners of her eyes and eyebrows still revealed a furious and cold aura.","Finally suppressing her anger, she said in a cold and hoarse voice, \"Don’t forget this is our revenge on the hit on the reclusive families’ reputation. If we don’t succeed, I won’t be the only one losing face. The entire reclusive families will lose face too. Since you’ve decided to do this, don’t harp on the worries. If you have too many worries, you’ll only fail!\"","Elder Xue wavered. \"Empress, I need to reconsider.\"","Nie Qingru couldn’t hide her disappointment. She did not say anything else and allowed Elder Xue to call the others to discuss the matter.","**","The fact that the reclusive families did not react immediately meant that the ships carrying the chips and rare earths successfully arrived at the agreed port through the high seas.","David and Cage met at the dock.","Both were big bosses in Continent F. They were neither friends nor enemies in private. They greeted each other warmly when they bumped into each other this time.","On the other hand, Bo Jingxing brought people over to unload the goods at the Ninth Branch in Beijing. Everything was proceeding in an orderly manner.","Bo Jingxing even called Qiao Nian, far away in the independent continent, to inform her that the goods had arrived safely."]},{"number":3683,"title":"Chapter 3683: Received The Items","paragraphs":["In the independent continent.","Qiao Nian was in the living room getting water when she accepted the call. Hearing this, she opened the fridge door, took out a bottle of Evian, then walked to the sofa and sat down.","\"So far, there’s been no movement from Continent M.\"","\"Oh.\"","She responded, placed her phone on the coffee table, unscrewed the cap, and took a sip of water. \"I understand.\"","Bo Jingxing looked at the girl’s exquisite eyebrows and said in a low voice, \"Qiao Nian, I apologize for what I said back then.\"","The girl’s eyes were frivolous, but upon hearing the man’s apology, they moved slightly. She slowly put down the water bottle and casually said, \"What did you say that night?\"","\"I...\"","\"I didn’t take it to heart. You don’t have to take it to heart either.\"","Bo Jingxing instantly understood what she meant. A bitter smile flashed across his lips, and he could not help but shake his head with a smile. \"I feel even more sorry if you say that.\"","If Qiao Nian scolded him or gave him a hard time...","He would feel better.","However, Qiao Nian was magnanimous and tolerated his overboard words that night. It made him unable to let go.","Qiao Nian was direct. \"You don’t have to overthink. We’re just ordinary friends. It’s normal for you to have your own concerns.\"","Bo Jingxing looked at her deeply and apologized gentlemanly. \"I’m sorry.\"","Qiao Nian did not respond this time.","She didn’t like accepting apologies, especially from Bo Jingxing, who insisted on apologizing to her. It was quite meaningless.","She knew very well that she and Bo Jingxing were only acquaintances who had met a few times. In fact, they might not even be ordinary friends.","This time, upon their cooperation being interrupted in Continent M, Bo Jingxing, as the person in charge of the Ninth Branch, asked her for a countermeasure. Actually, there was nothing to apologize for.","If the person who had asked her that night had been Ye Wangchuan, she might have felt a little uncomfortable.","But she did not feel offended since it was Bo Jingxing.","Some people were closer, and others were more distant.","She had never felt that this was wrong.","Bo Jingxing could also tell the girl was suppressing her impatience and indifference and did not continue this topic. \"These two from Continent F...\"","Qiao Nian relaxed her brows. \"There’s no need to keep them. I told David to leave after delivering the things.\"","Bo Jingxing heaved a sigh of relief. \"Thank you.\"","\"Mm,\" Qiao Nian replied. \"You don’t have to thank me. I was the one who caused this conflict. I should be responsible for it.\"","\"Elder Ye talked to me about this. He said that this day would come sooner or later. I also think it makes sense.\" Bo Jingxing’s eyes were filled with a smile. \"So, Miss Qiao, you don’t have to take responsibility for yourself. You’re the youngest among us. I didn’t face as much pressure when I was your age. You don’t have to shoulder so many things either.\"","\"Alright.\"","Qiao Nian did not explain her thoughts to him. She only nodded and looked quite easy to talk to.","Bo Jingxing knew that she had agreed so quickly because she did not take his words to heart. He was not sad. He smiled and chit-chatted before hanging up.","Qiao Nian hung up and received a call from Jian Jin.","\"Who were you on the phone with, talking for so long? I’ve called you several times.\"","\"A friend.\"","Qiao Nian did not beat around the bush.","\"Is there anything?\"","Jian Jin turned serious. \"Didn’t I say I’d help you investigate that person last time? I found something.\""]},{"number":3684,"title":"Chapter 3684: I Found That Person’s Name, Di Xicheng","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian sat up straight with a solemn expression. \"Speak.\"","Jian Jin said, \"I checked on the black market, and there really is a person named SEVEN. This person appeared half a year after you founded the SEVEN brand. In other words, half a year after you founded this brand, someone appeared on the black market with this nickname...\"","Qiao Nian had long realized that it was not a coincidence that the other party was named SEVEN.","Unexpectedly, he had already set his sights on her back then.","Jian Jin continued, \"At first, he appeared on the black market as a hacker and accepted a few orders rejected by the Red Alliance. He completed them very well. At that time, he was a little famous, but not long after he was offered an olive branch by the independent continent’s Hacker Alliance, he disappeared from the black market... Because he had only appeared for a short period and wasn’t very famous, no one paid special attention to him, nor did anyone expose his background...\"","\"What else?\" Qiao Nian’s intuition told her that Jian Jin had found something else.","Reality proved that her sixth sense was still so strong!","Jian Jin smiled and said, \"Qiao, you’re making me feel unfulfilled.\"","Jian Jin did not leave her hanging. \"In addition to this, I also happened to discover his name: Di Xicheng.\"","Qiao Nian raised her eyebrows, a little interested. \"Are you sure?\"","She had investigated SEVEN herself but did not find out his name.","Jian Jin did not expect to be questioned. \"Yes! I’m not mistaken. His name is Di Xicheng. It’s absolutely true.\"","\"How did you find out?\" Qiao Nian caught the main point.","\"Ahem.\" Jian Jin laughed. \"I-it was just a coincidence.\"","Qiao Nian remained silent.","Jian Jin knew she was not good at lying and simply admitted. \"Okay, I didn’t find out. It was Big Boss Lu!","\"Lu Zhi saw that I was investigating this SEVEN person on the black market and threw me a set of information. That person’s name and the hackers who took orders from the Red Alliance on behalf of the black market were written on it... I don’t know where he found these things... But it looks like he’s been investigating this person for a long time.\"","Jian Jin suspected that Lu Zhi might have been investigating this person in the dark since he found out that Qiao Nian wanted to investigate Ji Qing’s death.","However, he had an awkward personality and was unwilling to help Qiao openly.","\"He should have other channels.\" Jian Jin thought before saying, \"But since he gave me this information, that means everything is true.\"","Qiao Nian nodded, not knowing what to feel.","She did not want to owe Lu Zhi a favor, but it seemed like she owed him again.","This feeling was not good, but the information Lu Zhi found was very important to her.","\"By the way, Qiao, I heard about the chip. Why didn’t you ask Tian Chen for help this time? As long as you ask...\" Jian Jin said hesitantly.","Qiao Nian interrupted, \"Nie Qingru is watching. I can’t implicate you.\"","\"Phew, okay.\" Jian Jin let out a shaky breath and did not continue on the topic. \"Anyway, remember to tell me if you need help. I can’t get involved in big matters, but for the small matters, just say the word.\"","Qiao Nian agreed.","Jian Jin seemed to be very busy. She spoke briefly before hanging up.","Qiao Nian looked at the phone and thought of the name Di Xicheng. It corresponded to Nie Qingru’s ex-boyfriend’s surname.","She seemed to have grasped a corner of the truth and was about to lift the curtain hiding the truth of what decades ago."]},{"number":3685,"title":"Chapter 3685: Meeting an Acquaintance","paragraphs":["In the following period, the battle between Continent M and Beijing reached its climax.","This time, Nie Qingru was determined to teach Qiao Nian a lesson by suppressing Beijing. Beijing was also stubborn and refused to lower its head.","The two sides were fighting over several business deals.","As a large economy with the support of the reclusive families, Continent M was more competitive than Beijing, which had developed later.","Nie Qingru wanted to embarrass Beijing, so she kept intercepting Beijing’s negotiations.","Beijing was most likely at a disadvantage.","As time passed, Continent M and Nie Qingru’s suppression became more and more intense.","At the end of November, the research team in Beijing and Country C were discussing a three-year collaboration project, but it was ruined by Nie Qingru again. Jiang Zongjin was so angry that he did not even eat dinner.","Jiang Li had also heard about this. Backstage, he called Qiao Nian during the break.","The girl on the screen wore a black and white striped sweater as she got up to charge her cell phone. Passing by the laptop camera, her V-neck pulled down her white collarbone.","\"Wait.\"","\"Okay.\"","Jiang Li blinked and realized that he was almost stunned. He immediately slapped his face to wake up.","He was participating in a concert today.","In addition to himself, many singers were coming. He was scheduled to sing three songs at the back.","Originally, with Jiang Li’s popularity, he wouldn’t participate in such a concert. After all, it was too low-class. He had many fans and could even hold a tour himself.","However, Jiang Li decided to participate when his manager said that 50% of the proceeds would be donated to a children’s charity.","At this moment, he was not in the dressing room. He was leaning against a corner in the corridor outside.","There were few people here.","Aside from the occasional staff member going to the bathroom, few people noticed him.","Unfortunately, someone still saw him.","And it was Tang Ning of all people.","\"Young Master Jiang?\" Tang Ning was wearing a red evening gown, accentuating her graceful figure. She happened to notice Jiang Li, who was video-chatting with someone in a corner of the corridor.","Out of courtesy, she stopped, asked the staff to leave first, and walked over. \"Why are you here alone?\"","Jiang Li looked up and saw the person walking over. Remembering who she was, he nodded. \"You’re here too? I’ll call Nian Nian.\"","\"Miss Qiao?\" Tang Ning was surprised.","Jiang Li’s short blue hair was especially dazzling today. He smiled. \"Who else could it be?\"","\"Speaking of which, I haven’t seen Miss Qiao in a long time. Since we’ve bumped into each other, I’ll say hi to her,\" Tang Ning hesitated and said seriously.","She entered the entertainment industry this year.","With the Tang family’s status, Tang Ning did not need to enter the entertainment industry to develop.","However, ever since the Tang family offended Qiao Nian two years ago, their reputation deteriorated year by year. The circle had always supported the strong and trampled on the weak.","Tang Ning was also lucky to have obtained Zhang Yang’s recognition. With his protection, she was not bullied in the small circle of Beijing.","However, this year, Zhang Yang had started to take over the family business and did not have the time to care about her anymore.","Tang Ning encountered some trouble again and had no choice but to enter the entertainment industry to avoid the storm.","It wasn’t easy to survive in the entertainment industry.","Tang Ning did not tell anyone about her family background. She wasn’t very ’tactful’, so she was still a D-list celebrity.","She was often suppressed by celebrities from the same company.","This time, she participated in the concert because the other party could not stand her and found a ’financier’ to wheedle, deliberately throwing her here to humiliate her."]},{"number":3686,"title":"Chapter 3686: Grandpa and Your Father Were Afraid That You Would Overthink, So They Had Me Comfort You","paragraphs":["The other party’s ’financier’ was one of the company’s directors, so Tang Ning’s manager threw her over.","Jiang Li probably knew a little about her, but he did not like to meddle.","Seeing that Tang Ning only came over to say hello, he nodded. \"Alright. Wait a moment. She’s putting her cell phone to charge.\"","As Jiang Li finished speaking, the girl on the screen turned back, pulled out a chair, leaned against its back, and lazily rested her elbows on the armrests.","\"Why did you call me?\"","\"I can’t call you for no reason?\" Jiang Li was angry.","He turned the camera towards the uneasy Tang Ning and said, \"Look who I met.\"","Seeing Qiao Nian looking at her, Tang Ning straightened her back nervously and politely greeted her, \"Miss Qiao, long time no see.\"","Qiao Nian narrowed her eyes and stared at her face for a while. Then, she nodded casually. \"Long time no see.\"","\"I still have a concert. I won’t disturb you and Young Master Jiang’s talk.\" Tang Ning was a person who knew when to stop. She only said she would leave after greeting Qiao Nian out of respect. She didn’t want to deliberately curry favor with her.","She greeted Qiao Nian and indicated that Jiang Li could ignore her.","Jiang Li also moved the video camera to his side and watched as Tang Ning lowered her voice and mouthed that she was leaving.","He looked at Tang Ning’s back view as she lifted her skirt and left. Before she disappeared around the corner, he inadvertently saw from the corner of his eye that the cross strap she was wearing seemed to be broken.","Jiang Li frowned. He wasn’t sure if he was seeing things.","However, the other party had already disappeared around the corner. He didn’t have the time to see clearly.","\"Why are you looking for me?\" Qiao Nian asked.","Jiang Li returned to his senses. \"Oh, I wanted to ask if you know about a project that Uncle has been working on for three years.\"","The girl was silent for half a second. \"I heard a little.\"","Jiang Li sighed. \"Grandpa told me to tell you not to take it to heart. Uncle also asked me to speak with you. It’s not easy for either of them to talk, but they think it’s easy for me to talk to you. How can I comfort someone as a man? They don’t blame you. Don’t blame yourself for this. Don’t feel psychological pressure. Just know their intentions.\"","Qiao Nian rubbed her eyebrows and smiled. \"Alright, I understand.\"","\"I’ve relayed the message.\" Jiang Li stared at her face, afraid that she would go back on her word. \"Don’t let your imagination run wild. Eat and sleep when you should. When you come back, you’d better be looking energetic. Otherwise, the Old Master will slap me and think I didn’t speak to you.\"","\"It’s not like you’ll be slapped to death.\" It was rare for Qiao Nian to joke with him.","Jiang Li glared at her.","However, seeing that Qiao Nian did not seem affected by this matter, he finally felt relieved. He recalled his casual glance just now and frowned. \"I won’t talk to you anymore.\"","Qiao Nian wasn’t good at making small talk and just said, \"Okay.\"","Jiang Li hung up and returned to the dressing room. He looked around but did not see Tang Ning. He happened to bump into his manager and grabbed her arm.","\"Where’s Tang Ning?\"","\"Brother Li?\"","\"Did you see her?\" Jiang Li still remembered the strap on the back of Tang Ning’s gown. His expression was a little serious.","His manager did not know why Jiang Li would pay attention to a mid-tier celebrity. She thought about it before replying, \"It’s almost her turn.\""]},{"number":3687,"title":"Chapter 3687: Master Wang Took Down the Trending Topic","paragraphs":["At this moment, the emcee announced from backstage.","\"...Let’s welcome the rising star of the new generation, Miss Tang Ning!\"","Jiang Li’s eyebrows jumped. He let go of the manager’s arm and quickly walked to the platform.","\"Brother Li, where are you going?\"","\"Wait for me.\"","The manager chased after him.","Jiang Li’s footsteps were fast, just in time to catch Tang Ning going on stage. From this distance, he could see the little strap behind Tang Ning’s gown.","He had been in the entertainment industry for a long time. Even if not many people dared to provoke him, he had seen and heard of many cheap tricks over the years.","In the past, he did not meddle in other people’s business because the rules in this industry were like this. He was just playing around.","However, he couldn’t pretend not to see it this time.","Because Tang Ning knew Qiao Nian.","Furthermore, Tang Ning was a young woman. If the other party succeeded in this little trick, it would mean destroying a girl’s reputation.","Jiang Li only thought about it before pushing aside the double obstruction of the manager and staff and stepping onto the stage under the dazzling lights and music.","Tang Ning turned to look at him in shock as she held the microphone.","Jiang Li took off his jacket expressionlessly and put it on her. Under the audience’s exclamations and cameras, he held Tang Ning’s shoulder and said in a low voice, \"Hold on to my jacket. There’s something wrong with your dress.\"","Tang Ning was stunned for a moment. As she was pulled by Jiang Li, she noticed the straps on her shoulders sliding down. She didn’t make a scene and calmly grabbed Jiang Li’s jacket and followed him out of the stage...","**","Qiao Nian only found out about it in the afternoon.","Gu San told her that the trending topic had already exploded.","Jiang Li and Tang Ning’s names were trending. Many people began to expose Jiang Li’s background, including Jiang Zongnan and Jiang Zongjin.","Just Jiang Zongnan was fine.","Because of this entertainment gossip, Jiang Zongjin was discussed again. Someone dug up the failure of the Qing University scientific research team’s collaboration with Country C, seriously affecting his daily life.","Qiao Nian frowned at this. She didn’t care about Jiang Li’s scandal. She mainly could not let this implicate Jiang Zongjin.","Before she could clean up the messy trending topics on the Internet, she opened Weibo and realized that all the trending topics about Jiang Zongjin had been removed. The discussion square about Jiang Zongjin had also been taken down.","The methods were unyielding.","The attitude was firm.","She did not need to think to know who was behind it.","Qiao Nian came down from the second floor and bumped into a certain someone coming out of his room. She raised her eyebrows and went straight to the point. \"Were you the one who took down the trending topic on Weibo?\"","Ye Wangchuan raised his eyebrows. \"I shouldn’t have?\"","Qiao Nian smiled and gave him a thumbs up. \"Well done.\"","Ye Wangchuan walked to the fridge and took a bottle of water for her. Just as he was about to hand it over, he seemed to have thought of something and retracted his hand. His clear eyelashes were slightly lowered, and his pupils reflected the girl’s eye-catching face. His voice was charming. \"I’ll make you tea or coffee. What do you want?\"","Qiao Nian narrowed her eyes and stared at the water bottle, not understanding. \"Huh?\"","Didn’t he take a bottle of water?","Why did it have to be so troublesome?","Ye Wangchuan opened the fridge and put it back inside. Then, he turned around. \"It’s almost time for your Aunt Flo. You’ll have a stomachache if you drink it.\"","Qiao Nian was speechless.","She remembered that Ye Wangchuan had prepared a drawer of sanitary pads for her in Rao City.","She was already used to being controlled, so she did not rebel. If she couldn’t drink it, so be it. She walked towards the sofa. \"Warm water. I don’t want tea and coffee.\""]},{"number":3688,"title":"Chapter 3688: The More Urgent She Is, the More Difficult Her Situation Is","paragraphs":["\"Sure.\" Ye Wangchuan really spoiled her. Without another word, he went to get a cup of hot water for her.","He did not feel that his actions were degrading at all.","Young Master Ye had been taken care of since he was born. He rarely needed to do anything himself.","Even if Ye Wangchuan was not a delicate person and had stayed in Continent F and Continent M, he did not need to do anything as long as nothing serious happened.","However, ever since he picked Qiao Nian up in Rao City, he had often taken care of her. It was as if it was the natural thing to do.","Ye Wangchuan quickly took a cup of hot water and handed it to the girl. He did not forget to remind her, \"It’s a little hot. Drink it later.\"","\"Mm.\" Qiao Nian held the cup to warm her hands. She relaxed and raised her eyebrows at him. \"Why didn’t you ask me about the research project?\"","\"There’s nothing to ask.\"","Ye Wangchuan looked at the girl’s relaxed shoulders and neck. He sat down beside her and picked up an apple to peel. The simple task was extremely pleasing to the eye.","\"She’s getting more and more anxious, so she’s looking for trouble without caring about the consequences. The more she does this, the greater the pressure within the reclusive familes...\"","Ye Wangchuan handed her the peeled apple. His nose was straight and his lips thin. There seemed to be a small hook in his eyes. \"Have some fruit.\"","Qiao Nian had been fed a lot of fruit recently. She had a headache upon seeing them now. However, Ye Wangchuan insisted that she replenish her vitamins, so she could only unwillingly take them.","She took a bite of the apple to vent her anger. Her eyebrows relaxed, and she was no longer as sharp and unreasonable as before. There was a hint of warmth and peace.","Seeing that she was obedient and her eyes were clear, Ye Wangchuan said slowly, \"Old Master told me about this. That’s what he meant too.","\"Nie Qingru keeps going against Beijing and snatching these projects... The more she does so, the bigger the stall will be. In fact, the final backlash will be on her and the reclusive families.\"","He was like a stream of melted ice. His voice was calm and arrogant as if everything was under his control. He always placed himself between heaven and earth to look down on the entire situation.","\"Although the reclusive families are powerful and involved in all aspects of business, they are not a single entity after all. Instead, they are a group bound by interests. Nie Qingru will definitely need her subordinates to take over these businesses... However, her subordinates have their own projects and plans. This way, their plans will be disrupted.","\"It would have been fine if it were only a few of them, but she was too impatient and wanted to teach you a lesson. There must be many objections from within the reclusive families. At least, they aren’t as supportive of her suppressing Beijing as before. This time, she swallowed the chip project... The Leonard family should have been the first to protest.\"","The Leonard family was mainly involved in the chip business.","This time, Nie Qingru ruthlessly suppressed Beijing’s chips, causing the Leonard family to be forced to give in.","In terms of price and raw materials, the Leonard family suffered many losses, and even their original plan was disrupted.","The other small families did not dare to go against Nie Qingru, so they could only swallow their anger.","As one of the three heads of the Privy Council, the Leonard family also had the support of the radical faction. It was not so easy to shut them up.","Luke told Qiao Nian about the change in the attitude of the elders in his family.","She just didn’t expect Ye Wangchuan to know about this."]},{"number":3689,"title":"Chapter 3689: The Leonard Family Really Came Knocking on the Door","paragraphs":["In fact, Qiao Nian and Ye Wangchuan’s guess was accurate.","In the afternoon, the Leonard family received a notice that Nie Qingru had intercepted the cooperation between the Beijing scientific research team and Country C at a low price and stuffed this project on their heads. After discussion, the family’s older generation could no longer sit still. They formed a team and went to the Privy Council to ask Nie Qingru for an explanation.","\"Empress, why are we taking over this project? If I remember correctly, we just took over a similar project not long ago.\"","\"Empress, we also have a contract we have to sign. Every time you make decisions without informing us, it will make things difficult for us!\"","\"You should get someone else to do this project. The number of projects in our hands has already exceeded the load. We can’t take on any more...\"","Luke was one of the leaders the Leonard family had assigned to the Privy Council.","However, he was still young and couldn’t speak for his family in the Privy Council.","Currently, in such a situation where the older generation of the family appeared, he could only stand at the side and act as furniture.","Therefore, Luke knew his position before coming in. He gave up his position to the other family members and asked them to negotiate with Nie Qingru.","These people were about the same age as Nie Qingru. Some were even older... Suddenly, five or six people surrounded Nie Qingru and talked non-stop. Even Nie Qingru found it difficult to resist.","After roughly figuring out their intentions, she raised her hand, gesturing for them to pause.","The room fell silent.","Sitting on the leather swivel chair, she supported her forehead with her hand, and her sharp eyes shot towards the Leonard family members present. \"This is for the collective honor!\"","The few old men were obviously not easy to fool.","After she spoke, the few of them quickly exchanged glances and pushed out one to negotiate with her.","The old man had gray hair and strong facial features. He replied in a neither servile nor overbearing manner, \"But Empress, we’ve already taken enough responsibility. This time, you didn’t inform us in advance. Now, our factory has already reached its maximum capacity! Even if you beat us to death, we can’t complete the project you gave us. If you insist on us taking on Country C’s orders, we can only return Fei Teng’s orders.\"","Nie Qingru suddenly sat up, and her expression changed slightly.","The people from the reclusive families all knew about the relationship between Fei Teng and Smith Bank.","It could be said Smith Bank was behind Fei Teng, but Nie Qingru cleverly chose to be the President.","In fact, she was the boss of the internationally famous Internet company.","Soaring to make a fortune on the Internet.","They worked in high-end industries such as computers and cell phones.","Their demand for chips was much greater than that of ordinary industries.","This bunch of old fogeys had brought Fei Teng out at this time. They were clearly threatening her!","However, Nie Qingru had no choice but to face this problem seriously. \"...I’ll think about it.\"","\"Empress, take your time to consider. We’re not in a hurry. It’s not that we don’t want to work for the reclusive families, but we must tell you about the practical difficulties on our side.\" The old man’s attitude was respectful.","Nie Qingru looked at him coldly, her face covered with a layer of frost, not saying anything about it. \"I know. You guys can leave first.\"","\"Alright. Empress, please rest. We won’t disturb you anymore.\"","Having achieved their goal today, they did not stay any longer. They called Luke and left Nie Qingru’s lounge."]},{"number":3690,"title":"Chapter 3690: Di Xicheng’s Appearance","paragraphs":["Only after they walked out did the old men restrain themselves and say to Luke, \"We’ll suppress Fei Teng’s delivery date. Do you know what to do if the Empress asks for you?\"","Luke nodded. \"I do.\"","The old man was very pleased. \"That’s good.\"","They then arranged to go out and discuss specific countermeasures, leaving Luke alone at the Privy Council’s entrance.","After watching the car drive away, Luke returned to the Privy Council. After some thought, he sent a message to Qiao Nian, who was far away in the independent continent.","He did not reveal much information about the reclusive families. He only vaguely conveyed that they were unwilling to accept the order from Country C.","This was Qiao Nian’s repayment for helping him find out the Patriarch’s real murderer.","The Patriarch was not a good person, but he had raised him and made him respect and admire him like his father.","He had once promised in front of that person that if she found the Patriarch’s real murderer, he would owe her a favor and definitely repay her in the future.","It was not difficult for him to reveal information that did not affect the overall situation, nor did it hurt the family’s interests.","Luke was very happy to do so.","Because he couldn’t stand the high and mighty Empress either.","After all, if not for the Empress’ instigation back then, the Patriarch wouldn’t have died in the independent continent almost without a corpse.","He really wanted to see the Empress fall.","After sending the message, Luke deleted the message and walked into the Privy Council’s majestic archway without looking back.","**","Not long after Nie Qingru left, Shadow, together with a young man, knocked on the door.","\"Come in.\"","Squeak.","The door opened.","Shadow walked to Nie Qingru’s square desk and greeted her respectfully. \"Your Majesty, Young Master Di is here.\"","Nie Qingru stopped writing and noticed that another person was following behind him.","The man was 1.89m tall. His hoodie covered most of his face, and only his stubble could be seen from his chin.","\"Aunt.\"","His drooping bangs covered most of his eyes, but she could still tell they were beautiful. When he smiled, they would definitely turn bright and brilliant.","The vicious aura surrounding Nie Qingru suddenly dissipated when he called her \"Aunt.\" Even her usual domineering edge softened.","\"There you are.\"","She even stood up, walked over, and concernedly patted the young man’s arm. \"Why aren’t you resting at home for a few more days?\"","\"I’ve already recovered, so I asked Uncle Ning to bring me to see you.\" The young man’s gaze subconsciously landed on her hand. A trace of disgust flashed across his eyes, but it was hidden very well and disappeared in an instant.","Facing Nie Qingru, his voice revealed a bit of clarity.","This did not match his appearance at all.","However, Nie Qingru was convinced. \"If you want to see me, just let me know. I can go to your residence.\"","Di Xicheng did not respond. Instead, he changed the topic without a trace. \"Aunt, I heard the Leonard family looked for you?\"","As he spoke, he walked to the side, avoiding Nie Qingru’s hand.","However, he acted naturally, as if it was just an inadvertent action, making it seem as if it was not his intention to avoid Nie Qingru.","Even Nie Qingru did not notice anything wrong with his actions."]},{"number":3691,"title":"Chapter 3691: If It Had Been Di Xicheng","paragraphs":["Only Shadow, who had been standing at the side and observing, could tell that Di Xicheng was making a cheap shot. He pursed his lips and looked at the excited Nie Qingru. Then, he lowered his eyes and looked at his toes without saying anything.","Nie Qingru was in a good mood. \"They just left.\"","Di Xicheng found a place to sit down and looked up. \"Oh? They’re unwilling to accept Country C’s offer?\"","\"You know about it?\" Nie Qingru asked casually. Then, she did not hide anything from him. \"They used Fei Teng to weasel out of it. They don’t want to take on a job from Country C.\"","Di Xicheng smiled. \"Then... what does Eldest Aunt plan to do?\"","Nie Qingru narrowed her eyes disdainfully. \"Let me think about it.\"","The Leonard family was not easy to deal with. She needed to think of a dual solution. It would be best if she could persuade the Leonard family to take the initiative to cooperate with her.","She was unwilling to give up on the Country C approach. This was the only way to deal a strong blow to Beijing and Qiao Nian.","She had spent a lot of money and energy and would not allow this plan to fail.","Di Xicheng seemed to have grasped her thoughts. \"Eldest Aunt, why don’t you leave this matter to me? I might be able to find a solution.\"","\"You?\" Nie Qingru was silent for a moment. She looked him up and down and did not immediately agree.","She was an ambitious, capable, and ruthless woman.","Therefore, it was not easy for her to trust others.","However, the eyes of the person in front of her were as bright as that person’s smile, with a clear voice.","She hesitated.","\"What do you have in mind?\"","Di Xicheng knew she would give him a chance. \"I haven’t thought about it yet.\"","He asked next, \"Eldest Aunt... You don’t believe that I can do it well?\"","Nie Qingru could be ruthless to anyone, but upon meeting those eyes, her heart would always be shaken. In just a few seconds, her heart softened. \"Be careful. The Leonard family is not so easy to deal with. Tell me before you do anything.\"","\"Alright.\" Di Xicheng agreed quickly.","Nie Qingru frowned as she looked at him with pursed lips.","Di Xicheng came this time because he wanted to take over the right to deal with the Leonard family from her. Now that he had achieved his goal, he did not want to stay any longer. After patiently exchanging a few pleasantries with Nie Qingru, he reasoned that the doctor would examine him soon and asked for leave.","Shadow sent him out before returning.","Nie Qingru had already returned to her usual unapproachable noble appearance.","\"Empress.\" Shadow walked over and called out hesitantly.","\"Hmm?\" The woman sitting on the chair carved from red cedar had a different style even though she was already this old. She raised her eyelids indifferently and looked dignified.","Reading a document, her gaze was like a sharp knife as she looked at Shadow. \"I know what you want to say. If you can tell, I can also tell.\"","Shadow was speechless. \"Then you...\"","Nie Qingru’s expression was indescribably tired. \"He called me Eldest Aunt.\"","After a moment of silence, Shadow thought of another person.","Young Master Qixing also held his hand with bright eyes and often asked him why his ’godmother’ had not come to see him. Was it because he was not performing well?","However, what Young Master Qixing did not know until his death was that even though the Empress doted on him a little, she had once thought of handing over her position to him...","However, her nurturing and love toward him were nothing compared to her nurturing and love for another person. If the Empress had been forced to choose between status and this Young Master Di back then...","Would the Empress have sacrificed Young Master Di without hesitation?"]},{"number":3692,"title":"Chapter 3692: If Sister Qiao Doesn’t Go Back, You Won’t Go Back?","paragraphs":["Shadow did not dare to ask for the answer.","This was because just having this thought was already unpardonable in his eyes. He was the Empress’s servant, and he should never question his master.","\"I’m afraid Young Master Di is going against Qiao Nian.\" Shadow looked down and tried his best to persuade her. \"I’m worried that because of his youthfulness and frivolousness, he will be led by the nose by Qiao Nian’s actions and ruin your plan.\"","Nie Qingru indifferently said, \"I know he wants to compete with that evil creature. He has never lost to anyone since he was young. He definitely can’t let go of the fact that he suddenly suffered a loss at that evil creature’s hands. It’s fine if he wants to compete. Anyway, we’re in Continent M. I’ll try my best to protect him.\"","\"The Empress is wise.\" Shadow stopped trying to persuade her.","Nie Qingru knew her decision was not wise and waved her hand without looking up. \"You can leave first.\"","\"Yes.\"","Shadow stepped back and closed the door on his way out.","Then, he thought for a few seconds before walking towards Di Xicheng’s residence.","He wanted to see how Young Master Di wanted to solve the problem...","**","In the independent continent.","The morning sun was especially dazzling.","Over the past few days, autumn and winter had alternated, and the temperature had plummeted.","The sunlight outside still shone brightly on the leaves, but the temperature was extremely low. One could not withstand the cold outside just by wearing a sweater.","Gu San and Qin Si changed into thick gear and wrapped themselves up like bears.","They saw that Qiao Nian was still wearing the same sweater as before, and Qin Si couldn’t help but ask, \"Sister Qiao, aren’t you cold?\"","Qiao Nian floated past him. \"I added some down feather layers.\"","Qin Si was still glaring at her thin sweater. He did not understand why Qiao Nian did not seem afraid of the cold and even got ice water from the fridge.","At this moment, Ye Wangchuan walked out of his room.","Qin Si took a closer look and realized that Master Wang was not inferior. He was also wearing a high-collared wool sweater and was not even wearing a coat, handsome and outstanding.","He strode toward Qiao Nian and had the cheek to criticize her. \"Why are you wearing so little?\"","Qin Si smacked his lips and accepted the early morning’s display of affection. After taking it all in, he said to them, \"Beijing’s situation is getting more and more serious. When do you plan to go back?\"","Qiao Nian’s Evian had been replaced with a mug of cocoa. Turning around and leaning against the kitchen counter, her eyes were calm as she said casually, \"Don’t look at me. I can’t leave for the time being.\"","In the past two days, she had seized the time to gather Feng Yu, Xu Yi, and the others to discuss the last experiment. She wanted to figure out the biggest secret left behind by Ji Qing as soon as possible.","It was unrealistic for her to go back at this time.","Moreover, Old Master Ye and Bo Jingxing were in Beijing. Qiao Nian was not very worried that they wouldn’t be able to handle the situation.","\"Sister Qiao, don’t you plan to go back and take a look?\" Qin Si muttered as he looked at the girl. \"That Country C’s project—\"","\"I’ve already called my family to comfort them.\" Qiao Nian shrugged with a smile, looking like a good-for-nothing.","Qin Si was stunned. \"I thought you were going back to comfort Uncle.\"","\"He’s an adult. He knows how to adjust himself.\" Qiao Nian did not mind. Her shoulders were relaxed, and she lowered her head to take a sip of her hot cocoa.","Jiang Zongjin was a little disappointed at first but quickly adjusted his mood.","Although she could hear the disappointment hidden in his tone when she called, it was not a big problem. She believed he would adjust his condition himself.","Seeing that he couldn’t do anything to Qiao Nian, Qin Si asked Ye Wangchuan in a strange tone, \"Master Wang. If Sister Qiao isn’t going back, aren’t you going back too?\""]},{"number":3693,"title":"Chapter 3693: Master Wang Doesn’t Pick Up Bo Jingxing’s Call","paragraphs":["Ye Wangchuan sat beside Qiao Nian. \"I’m not going back.\"","Qin Si touched his neck and felt the pressure. \"No, Master Wang, you have to go back. What should I do if you’re not there? My family asked me to urge you to return.\"","Ye Wangchuan picked up a fruit from the coffee table, not even bothering to look up. He was handsome, but his words were quite shameless. \"What does it have to do with me?\"","Silence.","Qin Si was used to seeing him acting inhumanely. After being speechless for a moment, he immediately sought Qiao Nian’s help. \"Sister Qiao, Beijing is urging Master Wang to go back. Look...\"","Qiao Nian turned to Ye Wangchuan at Qin Si’s distress signal. \"Aren’t you going back?\"","Ye Wangchuan’s eyes were clear. \"I’m not going back.\"","Qiao Nian paused for a second before looking at Qin Si and casually relaying, \"He said he’s not going back.\"","\"...Sister Qiao, can you not play with me? Beijing is really urging Master Wang to go back. At least one of you should go back.\" Qin Si wanted to kneel and beg the two big bosses.","In fact, he did not want to take on such a thankless job. However, his family had given him a death order to convey the message. Otherwise, they would make him scram back.","Guan Yan was still in the independent continent. How could he go back?","\"Master Wang, just go back. In any case, you’ll return in a few days,\" Qin Si persuaded.","Ye Wangchuan still looked unmoved. \"I’m not going back.\"","\"F*ck!\" Qin Si pounded his chest in anger.","Gu San came out at this moment and said to Qiao Nian and Ye Wangchuan, \"Old Master called.\"","Ye Wangchuan peeled the grapes with his slender fingers and placed them on the porcelain bone plate. Then, he carefully wiped the liquid on his fingers with tissue paper, stood up, and said unhurriedly, \"I’ll answer it.\"","Qiao Nian watched him walk back into the bedroom before turning her head. Her side profile was handsome and smooth, and her nose was straight. \"Why is Beijing in a hurry to rush him back?\"","Qin Si sighed. \"Actually, it’s nothing much. Sister Qiao, you know that the rare earth resources are in Master Wang’s hands, right? Someone in the country has spread rumors that Continent M has taken over our supply of rare earths. Some high-end industrial corporations are very anxious, using all kinds of connections to inquire about the situation. Master Wang has always been in charge of this. Even Elder Ye can’t calm these people. Therefore, that kid, Bo Jingxing, jumped up and down and asked Master Wang to return. However, I don’t know what’s wrong with Master Wang this time. He didn’t give that kid any face at all... He’s still unwilling to go back.\"","Qiao Nian’s eyes flashed. She wondered if he was standing up for her.","However, she rejected this idea.","She did not tell him about her previous conflict with Bo Jingxing. Bo Jingxing was a smart person, he wouldn’t spill the beans himself...","\"Oh.\" Qiao Nian quickly threw this thought to the back of her mind. She speculated Ye Wangchuan was unwilling to return to Beijing for other reasons.","She knew he was not someone who did not see the big picture. He was not worried about Beijing, so she took out her phone and contacted Feng Yu while casually eating the peeled grapes on the plate.","...","In the bedroom.","Ye Wangchuan took the landline phone from Gu San and ordered, \"Close the door.\"","Gu San quickly closed the door.","Only now did Ye Wangchuan remove his hand covering the receiver and listen to Ye Maoshan’s roar on the other end. \"Young brat, when do you plan to return? Do you want me to fly over before you’re willing to come back?\"","\"I’ll be back tomorrow. I’ve already arranged a plane.\" Ye Wangchuan stopped the Old Master from continuing to roar."]},{"number":3694,"title":"Chapter 3694: Offending Sister Nian Is Better Than Offending Master Wang","paragraphs":["\"You’re coming back tomorrow?\" Ye Maoshan was in disbelief. \"Since you’ve already arranged a plane, why didn’t you give us a heads-up? Do you know that Jingxing is so anxious that he’s been looking for me for the past few days? He just came to our house to get me to call you.\"","Only then did he remember. \"By the way,\" he said doubtfully, \"do you not answer people’s calls?\"","\"My cell phone is out of battery.\"","What a convenient reason.","\"Like he—\" Ye Maoshan almost broke his defense. At least he remembered to be careful not to scold him. Instead, he asked angrily, \"Did you have a conflict with Jingxing? You grew up together. Why are you angry with him?\"","Ye Wangchuan had always been favored by the heavens and had status and brains.","Such a person was destined to be proud. In fact, not many people in the huge Beijing circle could enter his social circle.","Bo Jingxing was one of them.","The two of them had grown up together and had fought in the same courtyard.","The Bo family was not as well-off as the Ye family, but it was not bad either.","Bo Jingxing was also a smart person. In his teens, he learned how to invest in stocks. Later on, he opened a company and started a real estate business.","He had been friends with Ye Wangchuan in the early stages.","Later on, he was tricked by Ye Wangchuan and fell heavily. He rushed to the Ye residence and called Ye Wangchuan out for a fight.","Bo Jingxing was beaten up and sent to the hospital for three days.","Old Master Ye still remembered the matter had blown up quite big. He was prepared to lower his pride and apologize to the other party’s parents.","Unexpectedly, they became friends after the fight. They turned around and played together as if they were best buddies.","\"How did Jingxing offend you?\" Ye Maoshan knew his young brat well. He was stingy, but he was very tolerant of his friends.","Otherwise, Qin Si would have lost a layer of skin by now.","He couldn’t understand what conflict Bo Jingxing could have with Ye Wangchuan.","Ye Wangchuan’s long eyelashes curled up slightly. His outstanding eyes and eyebrows grew cold, but there was not much emotion on them.","\"He didn’t mess with me.\"","\"He didn’t mess with you. Why aren’t you answering his calls?!\" Ye Maoshan raised his voice.","Ye Wangchuan still looked calm. \"He might as well have messed with me.\"","Ye Maoshan was rendered speechless, but he quickly reacted. \"Did he mess with Nian Nian?\"","Ye Wangchuan did not answer. He held the receiver in his beautiful hand and stood there like a painting.","However, Ye Maoshan understood. \"Then he deserves it!\"","Ye Wangchuan did not waste any time. \"I’ll be flying at three in the afternoon tomorrow. I’ll probably land at the international airport at eight.\"","There was a 10-hour time difference between the independent continent and Beijing.","Ye Maoshan replied, \"I’ll arrange for a chauffeur to pick you up.\"","\"Okay.\"","Ye Wangchuan thought about it before his eyes grew deep. \"Don’t tell Bo.\"","How could Ye Maoshan not know that he wanted Bo Jingxing to be anxious for a while longer? Knowing the inside story, he did not feel burdened. \"I know. Does your grandfather still need you to remind him?\"","Ye Wangchuan smiled. \"Thank you.\"","Old Master Ye was still unhappy about being in the dark. \"Just don’t anger me in the future! I’m hanging up.\"","Ye Wangchuan heard the static sound and put the receiver down. Then, he turned around elegantly and looked at Gu San, who had accidentally heard the secret. \"Don’t talk nonsense outside.\"","\"Yes, Master Wang.\" Gu San silently lit a candle for Young Master Bo as he followed Ye Wangchuan out."]},{"number":3695,"title":"Chapter 3695: Sister Nian Believes in Master Wang’s Feelings","paragraphs":["Qin Si saw him come out. \"Master Wang, about returning to Beijing...\"","\"I’m not going.\" Ye Wangchuan walked over and wrapped her hands in his. He rubbed the girl’s slightly cold fingertips and gently asked, \"Why are your fingers still so cold?\"","Qin Si looked at the way he treated Qiao Nian and wished he could leave. However, the phone in his pocket kept buzzing.","He took it out and looked at it. It was Bo Jingxing calling him again.","He could only grab his hair and get up to answer the call outside.","Qiao Nian looked at his back as he walked out before elbowing the man’s chest. \"Why did you lie to him?\"","\"Huh?\" Ye Wangchuan’s eyes were deep as he raised his eyebrows. \"You know that I lied?\"","Qiao Nian looked at him speechlessly.","Ye Wangchuan was suddenly in a good mood. He grabbed her hand and carefully covered it in his palm before casually saying, \"He’s not tight-lipped. Telling him is equivalent to telling everyone.\"","Qiao Nian could feel his breath on her neck. It was itchy and she wanted to dodge, but her body was used to his warm approach, so she leaned lazily against his chest, not wanting to move. \"Oh.\"","Ye Wangchuan intertwined his hand with hers and played with her fingers. \"I’m going back to Beijing. I don’t know when I’ll return.\"","\"Alright, I understand.\" Qiao Nian leaned comfortably in his arms and even yawned. Her eyelids drooped and she wanted to sleep.","Ye Wangchuan looked at her heartlessness. He wanted to be angry, but he couldn’t help but smile. He couldn’t bear to wake her up. \"Is it okay for you to stay here alone?\"","\"Yes.\" Qiao Nian’s eyes narrowed.","Ye Wangchuan smiled. \"I’ll leave Gu San for you.\"","Only then did Qiao Nian open her eyes. Her dark eyes reflected his shadow. \"Aren’t you taking him with you?\"","He was going back alone?","\"There’s no danger in Beijing. I’m just going to deal with the rare earths problem. It shouldn’t take much time. He can’t help even if I bring him back. Why don’t I leave him here to cook for you?\" Ye Wangchuan’s tone was normal.","Qiao Nian sat up and looked at him. \"I remember... Gu San seems to be a financial expert?\"","Gu San was very outstanding.","He knew a little about finance, flying planes, shooting, equestrianism...","It was only because he was with Ye Wangchuan that he was not that eye-catching. He was considered a rare talent outside.","But he was leaving Gu San to cook for her...","Qiao Nian thought for a moment and supported her chin with her hand. \"That’s not a bad idea.\"","She needed someone to take care of the hospital matter.","Ji Lingfeng was about to be discharged from the hospital and return to the old residence to recuperate. At that time, some people would definitely become restless.","Guan Yan was helping her investigate Di Xicheng.","She didn’t have enough people around her.","She would be much more relaxed with Gu San around.","Ye Wangchuan lifted the hair by her ear, revealing his bright eyes. His voice was filled with a smile. \"Goddess Qiao, why don’t you say something about missing me while I’m gone?\"","Qiao Nian was stunned at first, but she immediately reacted. Without saying anything else, she raised her neck and kissed him on the lips. \"Just one more stamp and you’ll be mine. Don’t fool around when I’m not around.\"","Ye Wangchuan felt her soft lips and then her carefree voice. He couldn’t help but laugh. \"When have I ever fooled around?\"","Qiao Nian looked at him seriously and concluded, \"Your looks are already fooling around.\"","It was a little unsafe to release Ye Wangchuan outside. People would always ask him for his WeChat."]},{"number":3696,"title":"Chapter 3696: Someone Came Knocking on the Door in Just Three Days","paragraphs":["But she was not too worried.","Love makes people grow together and entrust themselves to each other. It isn’t worrying about gains and losses.","She trusted Ye Wangchuan and her feelings.","**","Ye Wangchuan left the next afternoon.","Qiao Nian did not send him off.","Qiao Nian received Ye Wangchuan’s message as she entered the First Research Institute.","After replying, she went straight to Feng Yu’s office.","She made a discovery. In addition to Feng Yu, she also called Xu Yi and Shi Fu to put this discovery into action.","The level of the experiment that Ji Qing left behind was very high.","This kind of high-level experiment did not allow for any mistakes. Even the slightest mistake would require a redo.","To experiment with her discovery, Qiao Nian did not return from the First Research Institute for three days as she experimented in her laboratory.","Shi Fu and Feng Yu had to leave sometimes because of their statuses.","She and Xu Yi were the only ones left in the laboratory.","After three days, the results were not satisfactory.","Even Xu Yi, who usually did not care about anything, could not hide his disappointment when he saw the results.","On the other hand, Qiao Nian was fine. She calmly accepted this imperfect outcome.","She gave Xu Yi some instructions before leaving.","When Qiao Nian walked out of the First Research Institute, she realized it was colder outside. Much colder than three days ago.","Her sweater was not doing its job. When the wind blew, even the gaps between the fabric left her bones feeling cold.","Qiao Nian walked to the side of the road as she messaged Gu San, asking him to pick her up.","The message had just been sent out when she heard the ear-piercing sound of an engine rushing in her direction.","Qiao Nian’s body reaction was fast. The moment she heard the sound, she was already on guard. She put away her cell phone and dodged the motorcycle charging at her.","After missing, the motorcycle braked and immediately turned around before charging in her direction again—","Qiao Nian only saw that the dark blue bike was so fast that it was almost an afterimage. In just a breath, it had almost reached her.","She agilely flipped to the left to avoid the fatal collision, but no matter how fast she was, she could not avoid it completely. Her elbow brushed against a branch, and the flesh under her sleeve split open, with blood almost seeping out.","Moreover, she managed to dodge it with much difficulty. Her back and knees were also bruised.","Qiao Nian gritted her teeth and endured the sharp pain in the back of her head. She looked around and grabbed a tree trunk when the motorcycle was about to hit her for the third time. Then, she turned around and kicked the rider off the motorcycle.","\"Ouch!\" She used all her strength in this kick, and her knee hit the other party’s jaw. The other party groaned in pain, and he lost his grip on the handle.","He fell heavily to the ground, and the motorcycle crashed into a tree trunk a few meters away.","The man on the ground did not give Qiao Nian much time to catch her breath. He got up and was about to take out his weapon from his pocket.","Qiao Nian did not give him the chance and stepped on the back of his hand. She bent down and grabbed his arm with her other hand, pinning him to the ground and pressing his face firmly.","\"#@¥%...\"","The other party spewed a series of vulgarities. It looked like he was in a lot of pain.","Qiao Nian ignored him and lifted his helmet, seeing an unfamiliar brown-skinned face.","\"A mercenary?\""]},{"number":3697,"title":"Chapter 3697: Sister Nian: I’ll Give You Three Seconds to Think","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian immediately recognized his fearlessness, only found in mercenaries. His eyes were also as fierce as a wolf’s.","Where did the mercenaries from the independent continent come from?","The other party continued to blabber. There was no need to look to know that he was cursing.","Qiao Nian had never indulged anyone. She slapped the man, causing blood to seep out of the corner of his mouth. Only then did he hear her scold calmly and impatiently, \"Shut up.\"","He had disturbed her.","The brown-skinned mercenary’s ears were buzzing. He was stunned for a few seconds before he began to struggle with all his might. \"Let... Let go of me!\"","This time, he mumbled something that Qiao Nian could understand.","The girl lowered her eyes and pressed his face against the ground before unhurriedly asking, \"Who sent you?\"","\"I’m telling you... to let go! B*tch!\" The man had yet to realize the danger and was still struggling fiercely.","The strange thing was that he could not break free from the other party’s grip no matter how hard he tried. He was crushed.","This feeling was not good. Mercenaries advocated martial arts, and martial arts mostly came from strength. Women were naturally weaker than men, causing most of them to look down on women and more or less hate them.","But now, he was pressed to the ground by a woman he looked down on. It was undoubtedly a great humiliation to him.","\"I f*cking told you to...\" The mercenary’s face was a red of humiliation. It was red and green, and one could tell that he was furious.","However, he was facing Qiao Nian.","Qiao Nian had never spent much time reasoning with people. In the next second, before the mercenary could curse, he heard a crack .","\"Ah!\" The man let out a miserable scream. Cold sweat dripped from his forehead, and the veins on his neck bulged in pain.","He widened his eyes and looked at the extremely young woman controlling him. She had an Asian face—the weakest of women who only knew how to cry.","However, his eyes were wide open in pain. He could feel the extreme pain caused by Qiao Nian’s dislocated hand.","In just a few seconds, his back was drenched in sweat. His lips were pale from the pain, and he could not curse anymore.","His mind buzzed as the girl’s low and hoarse voice said: \"From now on, you’ll answer every question I ask. If your answer doesn’t satisfy me, I’ll break one of your fingers. You have two hands and 10 fingers. You have 10 chances to mess with me. When you use up these 10 chances, you still have two legs... I’ve limited patience. I’ll give you three seconds to think about how to answer next.\"","\"3.\"","Before the mercenary could think about it, she started the countdown. Instinctively, he straightened his neck and blushed. \"You’re already counting?\"","\"2.\" Qiao Nian couldn’t be bothered to look at him.","The atmosphere became heavy.","The mercenary’s mind spun, and he could not think clearly. However, the girl did not give him time. Counting the last number seemed like the last second before his head was cut off.","\"1.\"","Qiao Nian did not stop at all when his mentality was shaken. \"Who instructed you to come?\"","\"I...\" The mercenary opened his mouth.","He met the girl’s calm eyes. They were dark, deep, and cold. \"Think carefully before you speak.\"","He felt a chill in his heart. His expression changed slightly. He shut his mouth and hesitated, but his dislocated left arm constantly reminded him of the pain."]},{"number":3698,"title":"Chapter 3698: That Person Wanted Me to Teach You a Lesson","paragraphs":["His buzz cut was covered in sweat. After a short moment of hesitation, he decided to give in. \"I don’t know either. That person only gave me your photo and location. He told me to teach you a lesson and said you owed him. I was only paid to do it. The rest has nothing to do with me.\"","He explained faster than Qiao Nian thought. She couldn’t help but raise her eyebrows. \"You don’t know who I am?\"","The mercenary was in so much pain that he couldn’t say anything. However, he was thinking that if he had known she had such skills, he would have done his homework before coming.","\"I don’t know. The other party only gave me a photo and didn’t say anything else. I saw you were a... a woman, so I couldn’t be bothered to ask.\"","He thought it was just a small business, but who knew that he had almost lost everything today?","Qiao Nian asked him one last question. \"Which organization are you from?\"","The mercenary didn’t expect her to know the various large organizations in the independent continent. He was stunned for a moment before mechanically reporting the name of a small organization.","At this moment, the sound of tires braking came from the roadside.","Right on the heels of that, Qiao Nian heard messy footsteps before Gu San nervously sized her up. \"Miss Qiao, are you alright?!\"","He pointed at the man on the ground. \"What’s going on?\"","\"I’m fine.\" Since he was here, Qiao Nian let go and stood up, signaling Gu San not to let him escape.","Gu San quickly grabbed the mercenary as he tried to run. He was smart enough to grab the man’s dislocated arm, causing him to scream in pain.","Gu San covered his mouth and frowned. \"Shut up!\"","The man’s face twisted in pain as he looked at him and then at Qiao Nian. He regretted accepting this job in a moment of confusion.","What the f*ck was going on?","Moreover, he had heard the name the pretty boy shouted.","Miss Qiao?","Someone with the surname Qiao from the independent continent who came out of the First Research Institute... There seemed to be only one person with this age.","He had also heard many legends about Miss Qiao.","Realizing he might have gotten into big trouble, the mercenary’s facial muscles twitched. He felt sorrowful and hurriedly defended himself. \"I really don’t know anything. That person has a grudge against you. I just took the money, I didn’t want your life. I was just trying to scare you.\"","Qiao Nian looked at the motorcycle not far away and then at the person anxiously explaining himself. She did not say anything.","Gu San was confused. \"Miss Qiao, what’s going on?\"","Qiao Nian wiped the blood off her hands and said indifferently, \"I just came out of the research institute and bumped into him. Then, you saw what happened. He said he was hired to scare me, but he doesn’t know by whom. The other party only gave him money and said he had a grudge against me. He asked him to teach me a lesson... It’s that simple!\"","This matter was indeed quite simple.","Moreover, she already knew who it was.","A face in a photoshopped photo appeared in Qiao Nian’s mind.","Di Xicheng!","\"I’ll bring him back for Mo Dong to interrogate!\" Gu San gritted his teeth.","Qiao Nian was unbothered. \"No need. He doesn’t know anything.\"","Gu San did not understand why she was so sure.","Qiao Nian did not hide it from him and roughly told him about the background of this mercenary.","Qiao Nian knew a little about this organization.","It was an underground organization unranked in the independent continent. It was even worse than an unrated organization like the Three Nine Gates."]},{"number":3699,"title":"Chapter 3699: No One Noticed that Sister Nian Was Injured","paragraphs":["This organization gathered assassins and mercenaries who came to the independent continent. They accepted the bad orders that others were unwilling to do.","Most of their activities were about kidnapping and intimidation caused by the internal strife of the relatively inferior forces in the independent continent.","These people lived on the independent continent but were not considered independent continent people.","Because they had never been accepted by the locals. They were like rats living in underground drains. They only dared to poke their heads out in the dead of night.","Therefore, these people did not know much about the people and matters of the independent continent. This was why Di Xicheng hired this person to teach her a lesson.","Di Xicheng already knew this person could not complete the mission. He only did this to provoke her and tell her to remember the grudge of being shot down into the deep sea.","\"Interesting.\" At this thought, Qiao Nian licked her dry lips and smiled. She forgot about the burning pain on the back of her hand as she put it in her pocket. Her aura was strong and arrogant.","She had thought Di Xicheng had the same style as Nie Qixing and would only put on airs. She didn’t expect him to be so courageous!","Nie Qingru was the kind of person who would calculate every penny and take revenge for the littlest grievance.","\"Give him to Mo Dong to investigate his identity. If there’s no problem, let him handle it.\" Qiao Nian was in the independent continent but didn’t particularly get involved in their matters.","Mo Dong was different.","Mo Dong had been managing the Bright Gate all this time and knew the complicated power relationships in the independent continent very well. It was the best choice to hand this person over to him.","\"Okay.\" Gu San was not long-winded. Before the man could react, he turned his hand and hit the back of the man’s neck.","The mercenary’s vision turned black and he fell to the ground.","Gu San did not have a good impression of him. He grabbed his collar expressionlessly and pulled him. Then, he opened the trunk and threw him inside.","The entire process was done in one go.","He threw the man into the trunk and slammed the door shut.","Gu San wasn’t afraid of being seen by passers-by as he returned and opened the passenger door for Qiao Nian, turning back into a gentle and polite assistant. \"Miss Qiao, get in the car.\"","\"Okay.\" Qiao Nian walked over and realized she had abrasions on her back, knees, and elbows as she buckled her seatbelt. \"Send me back.\"","\"Will do.\"","Gu San went around to the driver’s seat.","Soon, the Land Rover disappeared around the corner, leaving behind only the exhaust.","From the moment the motorcycle went crazy and rushed onto the pedestrian path to Gu San knocking the man out and throwing him into the trunk, the entire process took at most 15 minutes.","Just these 15 minutes were enough to make the passersby dumbfounded.","\"What happened just now?\"","\"This is the First Research Institute’s entrance, right? How dare these people cause trouble here?\"","\"I saw that the girl came out of the research institute. I just don’t know about the motorcycle rider—\"","**","The news had yet to spread.","After Gu San sent Qiao Nian back, he went looking for Mo Dong.","Qiao Nian greeted Qin Si and Guan Yan before going to her room as if nothing had happened. She took a shower and changed into a bathrobe, then pulled out a chair and sat down to treat her wounds with disinfectant and cotton swabs.","One of her legs was on the ground, and the other was on the chair as she took the disinfectant, opened the lid, and poured it on her knees."]},{"number":3700,"title":"Chapter 3700: Di Xicheng Just Wanted to Warn Her","paragraphs":["Hiss.","She felt a sharp pain when her torn knee came into contact with the alcohol. She only took a deep breath initially, but she endured it and did not make a sound. Then, she used a cotton swab to wipe the wet stains near the wound.","Qiao Nian nimbly disinfected her wound and applied medicine. She even used gauze to tie up the larger areas.","However, she tied it very casually to prevent the wound from rubbing against the fabric of her clothes. She did not treat it as carefully as a medical professional.","By the time Qiao Nian was done, over an hour was already gone.","For the past hour or so, she had been relying on herself to endure the pain. She had never cried out that she was tired or in pain.","Qiao Nian had just finished treating her wound and had yet to pull on her bathrobe when the phone screen on the desk lit up. Ye Wangchuan was calling.","She quickly pulled up her bathrobe to cover the gauze and walked to the window to answer the call.","\"Hey.\"","No one could tell from her tone that she was injured.","Ye Wangchuan turned on the video and saw that her hair was still wet and hanging on her shoulders. There was nothing strange about it. \"I heard from Gu San.\"","The moment Qiao Nian saw his call, she knew that he must have heard from Gu San about what happened at the entrance of the First Research Institute. \"It was an accident.\"","Her knee was still a little painful when she walked. Qiao Nian subconsciously frowned slightly but quickly relaxed. \"I’ve already taken care of it.\"","To her, it was just a microexpression.","Very few people noticed the changes in Qiao Nian’s expression, and Ye Wangchuan was one of them.","Seeing Qiao Nian walking slower than usual, he realized she might be injured.","However, he did not expose her. Instead, he went along with her. \"Do you know who’s behind this?\"","Qiao Nian sat by the bed and paid attention to the angle of her cell phone so he would not see the medicine on the desk.","\"Okay.\"","She leaned lazily against the bed, looking indifferent, but her eyes were cold. \"Someone from the reclusive families.\"","Ye Wangchuan thought she didn’t want to say it.","The next second, the girl lazily uttered a name.","\"Di Xicheng.\"","Ye Wangchuan narrowed his eyes, and his gaze became dangerous. \"I’ll arrange for a few people to protect you.\"","The rest could wait until he returned.","Unexpectedly, Qiao Nian said indifferently, \"I almost got him on the high seas some time ago. He just wanted to warn me that he’s different from the people I met previously.\"","That mercenary said that he did not want to kill her. Qiao Nian believed him.","If the other party wanted to kill her, he could have shot or attacked her with a knife when he rushed her with the motorcycle.","Then her injuries would be much more serious than now!","However, the mercenary did not do that. He just sped up and bumped into her.","Motorcycles were not like cars. With the same impact force, motorcycles could at most severely injure or cripple people. It was indeed difficult to kill.","Di Xicheng just wanted to teach her a lesson.","It was also a disguised provocation.","However, in the current Independent Continent, not many people dared to take on this job.","Di Xicheng was quite smart. He had found the underground organization and done it so cleanly. If he were not her direct enemy, Qiao Nian would admire him.","He had brains, could act on revenge, and had courage.","Qiao Nian was excited.","\"I’ve already gotten Guan Yan to investigate him. We’ll find out his whereabouts soon. When the time comes, I should return this gift.\""]}]);
